    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Single-Molecule-Biophysic-2628-CD/1372311857/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Single-Molecule Biophysic",
      "description": "PhD Position Single-Molecule Biophysic Job Details | TU Delft We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile All jobs Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Single-Molecule Biophysic We are seeking a motivated PhD student to use single-molecule techniques and computational tools to explore molecular interactions and apply them for therapeutic applications. Job description We are looking for a PhD student passionate about understanding molecular mechanisms in biological systems. This position involves applying single-molecule techniques to study molecular interactions, including protein-ligand interactions and protein-peptide interactions. The candidate will work in an interdisciplinary environment, combining experimental approaches (single molecule fluorescence and biochemistry) with computational methods. The candidate will obtain single-molecule multiplexing data and validate machine learning predictions using the high-throughput data. The successful candidate will collaborate with international partners for therapeutic applications of this research. The project offers opportunities to make significant contributions to understanding molecular interactions and their implications for both fundamental and medical sciences. Job requirements MSc degree (or nearing completion) in physics, biophysics, computational biology, or a related field. Strong programming skills (Python) and experience in data analysis and computational methods. Familiarity with molecular biology techniques. Excellent written and spoken English skills. Ability to work effectively in a collaborative, international, and interdisciplinary environment. This position is part of a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network. Applicants must satisfy the MSCA mobility rule: at the time of recruitment, they must not have lived or carried out their main activity, such as work or study, in the Netherlands for more than 12 months during the previous 36 months. The rule applies regardless of nationality. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3059 - €3881 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy please contact Chirlmin Joo, via c.joo@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 1 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter It is highly recommended that the candidate makes an inquiry by emailing Chirlmin Joo before submitting their application. You can address your application to Chirlmin Joo. #EUfunded This is an EU funded project, named MORPHEOS: neuroMORPHic fluidic circuits Enabled by artificial iOn channelS, with project number 101311970, within program Horizon Europe / Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Networks Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3059 - €3881 Hours per week: 38 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 1 Nov 2026 ID job: 3828 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Functional Cookies These cookies provide a better customer experience on this site, such as by remembering your login details, optimizing video performance, or providing us with information about how our site is used. You may freely choose to accept or decline these cookies at any time. Note that certain functionalities that these third-parties make available may be impacted if you do not accept these cookies. Consent to all Functional Cookies Show More Details Functional Cookies Provider Description Enabled YouTube YouTube is a video-sharing service where users can create their own profile, upload videos, watch, like, and comment on videos. Opting out of YouTube cookies will disable your ability to watch or interact with YouTube videos. Cookie Policy Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Consent to cookies from provider YouTube Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Technisch-Beheerder-Experience-en-Maakfaciliteiten-2628-CD/1375054057/": {
      "title": "Technisch Beheerder Experience en Maakfaciliteiten Functiedetails",
      "description": "Technisch Beheerder Experience en Maakfaciliteiten Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Technisch Beheerder Experience en Maakfaciliteiten Zorg jij ervoor dat de nieuwe experience van het TU Delft Science Centre veilig en betrouwbaar draait? Als Technisch Beheerder Experience en Maakfaciliteiten beheer en onderhoud je interactieve exhibits, AV-systemen en maakapparatuur, en leid je studentmedewerkers technisch op. Functieomschrijving Het TU Delft Science Centre werkt toe naar de opening van een nieuwe experience begin 2027. Als Technisch Beheerder Experience en Maakfaciliteiten zorg jij voor het veilig en betrouwbaar functioneren van de experience, tentoonstellingen, maakfaciliteiten en bijbehorende technische voorzieningen. Je draagt bij aan de voorbereiding van de opening en aan de exploitatie daarna. Omdat dit een nieuwe functie is, geef je processen, technische documentatie, onderhoudsprocedures en kennisoverdracht mede vorm. Zo bouw je mee aan een duurzame beheerorganisatie. Wat ga je doen? Technisch beheer en onderhoud Je voert preventief en correctief onderhoud uit aan interactieve exhibits, AV-installaties, technische opstellingen en maakfaciliteiten. Je analyseert storingen en lost ze zelfstandig op binnen je deskundigheid en bevoegdheden. Waar nodig schakel je tijdig leveranciers of interne specialisten in. Je beheert technische documentatie, configuraties, inventarissen en onderhoudshistorie. Je realiseert technische verbeteringen aan bestaande exhibits en adviseert bij nieuwe ontwikkelingen over onderhoudbaarheid, betrouwbaarheid en veilig gebruik. Coördinatie en continuïteit Je bent het technische aanspreekpunt voor collega's en externe leveranciers en coördineert onderhoud door gespecialiseerde partijen. Je stelt het onderhoudsplan op en bewaakt de opvolging van meldingen en de uitgaven binnen het onderhoudsbudget. Je richt procedures in voor het signaleren, registreren en opvolgen van storingen, en prioriteert incidenten op basis van veiligheid, impact op de bedrijfsvoering en bezoekerservaring. Je zorgt voor technische instructies, overdracht en escalatieroutes voor afwezigheid en piekperiodes. Technische opleiding van studentmedewerkers Je bent inhoudelijk verantwoordelijk voor de technische opleiding en instructie van studentmedewerkers die technische handelingen uitvoeren. Je ontwikkelt en onderhoudt een technisch inwerkprogramma, praktische trainingen, werkinstructies en stappenplannen voor eerstelijns storingsafhandeling. Je toetst en registreert of studenten handelingen veilig en correct uitvoeren, welke taken zij zelfstandig mogen doen en wanneer zij moeten escaleren. Veiligheid Bij een onveilige situatie ben je bevoegd om apparatuur buiten gebruik te stellen en onveilige werkzaamheden te laten stoppen. Met wie werk je samen? Je rapporteert aan het afdelingshoofd Presentatie- en MaakHub en werkt nauw samen met de Facilitair Medewerker. Jij richt je op exhibits, AV-systemen en maakapparatuur; je collega richt zich op ruimtes, logistiek en regulier facilitair onderhoud. Daarnaast stem je af met vakspecialisten binnen de maakfaciliteiten en met leveranciers. Je hebt geen hiërarchische leidinggevende taken. Waar en wanneer werk je? Dit is een functie op locatie bij het TU Delft Science Centre. De experience is ook in weekenden en tijdens schoolvakanties geopend. Daarom werk je incidenteel tijdens weekenden en schoolvakanties. Deze inzet wordt tijdig ingepland, met aandacht voor een evenwichtige verdeling en de combinatie van werk en privé. Daarnaast neem je volgens vaste afspraken deel aan een bereikbaarheids- of achterwachtdienst voor urgente technische storingen. Functie-eisen MBO-plus- of HBO-werk- en denkniveau in technisch beheer, AV-techniek, elektrotechniek, mechatronica, industriële techniek of een vergelijkbare richting. Je kunt de benodigde kennis en vaardigheden hebben opgedaan via opleiding, werkervaring of een combinatie daarvan. Aantoonbare ervaring met technisch beheer, onderhoud en storingsafhandeling van technische installaties, interactieve systemen of AV-omgevingen. Een brede praktische technische basis, bijvoorbeeld in AV-systemen, licht- en geluidstechniek, netwerken, besturingssystemen of interactieve installaties. Je hoeft niet elk systeem al te kennen: je werkt zorgvuldig en leert nieuwe technieken snel. Je analyseert storingen systematisch. Je legt technische handelingen begrijpelijk uit, stelt praktische instructies op en beoordeelt of studenten werkzaamheden veilig en zelfstandig kunnen uitvoeren. Je maakt duidelijke afspraken met vakspecialisten en leveranciers en bewaakt voortgang en kwaliteit, ook zonder hiërarchische bevoegdheid. Je kunt onderhoudskosten ramen, uitgaven bewaken en over afwijkingen rapporteren. Je houdt overzicht, stelt prioriteiten, neemt initiatief en past je planning aan wanneer de situatie daarom vraagt. Je brengt technische instructies en afspraken mondeling en schriftelijk over in het Nederlands en het Engels. Je bent flexibel inzetbaar op wisselende dagen en, wanneer nodig, in weekenden en tijdens schoolvakanties. We willen dat iedereen met passende kwaliteiten zich aangesproken voelt, ongeacht gender, achtergrond of leeftijd. We waarderen verschillende perspectieven en ervaringen. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Directie Communicatie Impact voor een betere samenleving; dat is de missie van TU Delft. De Marketing & Communicatiemedewerkers van de directie Communication dragen daar steeds meer ‘accountable’ aan bij en daar zijn ze trots op! We begeleiden onze 28.000 studenten in hun ‘engineer journey’ van studiekiezers tot en met professionals in de maatschappij. Binnen de wetenschapscommunicatie benadrukken we de vraagstukken en onderzoeksresultaten in de maatschappelijke thema’s Klimaatactie, Energietransitie, Digitale Samenleving, Veerkrachtige Steden & Mobiliteit, en Gezondheid. Vanuit TU Delft Campus leggen we de verbinding naar bedrijven en beleidsmakers in ons innovatieve ecosysteem, waar onderzoeksresultaten versneld hun weg naar de samenleving vinden. En onder het motto #BetterTUgether! verbinden we onze bijna 8.000 TU Delft-collega’s. Zo versterken we samen het merk TU Delft, dat staat voor grensverleggend onderzoek, excellent onderwijs en baanbrekende innovaties. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk. Een functieomvang van 36-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 09 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3873 - €5264 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Inzet op wisselende dagen, in weekenden en tijdens schoolvakanties maakt deel uit van de werkplanning. Daarnaast neem je deel aan een bereikbaarheids- of achterwachtdienst. Afspraken over inzet buiten reguliere werktijden en de bijbehorende vergoeding worden vooraf vastgelegd volgens de geldende regelingen. Thuiswerken maakt geen structureel onderdeel uit van de functie. Additionele informatie Wil je meer weten over deze functie? Neem dan contact op met Jules Dudok, hoofd Presentatie- en MaakHub, via j.dudok@tudelft.nl. Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 8 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Jules Dudok. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Communication Salaris range: €3873 - €5264 Uren per week: 36-40 FTE: 1 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 8 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3899 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Systematic-Derivation-of-Formal-Languages-and-Their-Correctness-2628-CD/1375074157/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Systematic Derivation of Formal Languages and Their Correctness",
      "description": "PhD Position Systematic Derivation of Formal Languages and Their Correctness Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Systematic Derivation of Formal Languages and Their Correctness From Semantics to Syntax — Systematic Derivation of Formal Languages and Their Correctness Job description Formal languages, such as type theories and program logics, let us state and prove precisely what software should do. Today, each new language is designed by hand: experts invent the syntax, then check that it really means what it should. This is slow, and it has to be redone for every new problem. This project explores a different approach: start from the mathematical meaning of a language and derive the language itself from it, together with a proof that the two match. Several recent type theories were built this way, but each one with its own ad hoc techniques. Together, we want to find out whether there is one general recipe behind them. You will develop this theory using tools from category theory and type theory, and check your results in the Agda proof assistant. You will be supervised by Dr. Benedikt Ahrens in the Department of Software Technology at TU Delft. Your responsibilities will include: conducting this research, both individually and as part of a team; participating in scientific life at TU Delft and in the Netherlands, for example by attending and organizing seminars; participating in scientific life more globally, including publishing papers and attending workshops and conferences; contributing to teaching in computer science, providing the opportunity to gain teaching experience. Job requirements Applications will be evaluated on the following criteria: Masters degree in mathematics, computer science, or a related field Experience in both category theory and theoretical computer science (e.g., type theory, logic or programming language semantics), or a strong motivation and ability to learn them. Experience with a proof assistant (e.g., Agda, Rocq or Lean) is a plus, but not required. Enjoyment of precise mathematical reasoning, Ability to work independently and to collaborate across the maths/CS boundary; Excellent written and spoken English Willingness to contribute to, and possibly experience in, student supervision and teaching TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Delft University of Technology is built on strong foundations. As creators of the world-famous Dutch waterworks and pioneers in biotech, TU Delft is a top international university combining science, engineering and design. It delivers world class results in education, research and innovation to address challenges in the areas of energy, climate, mobility, health and digital society. For generations, our engineers have proven to be entrepreneurial problem-solvers, both in business and in a social context. At TU Delft we embrace diversity as one of our core values and we actively engage to be a university where you feel at home and can flourish. We value different perspectives and qualities. We believe this makes our work more innovative, the TU Delft community more vibrant and the world more just. Together, we imagine, invent and create solutions using technology to have a positive impact on a global scale. That is why we invite you to apply. Your application will receive fair consideration. Challenge. Change. Impact! Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Benedikt Ahrens, via B.P.Ahrens@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 29 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter Transcripts from your Masters degree (if available). You can address your application to Benedikt Ahrens. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. We encourage candidates to submit their application at the earliest opportunity. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-38 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 29 Nov 2026 ID job: 3975 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-System-Engineeering-for-Floating-Wind-Farms-2628-CD/1375104657/": {
      "title": "Postdoc System Engineeering for Floating Wind Farms",
      "description": "Postdoc System Engineeering for Floating Wind Farms Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc System Engineeering for Floating Wind Farms Are you passionate about offshore wind energy? Apply for a Post-doctoral research position in Floating Offshore Wind Energy and help accelerate the supply chain readiness in this area. Job description Floating offshore wind turbines are widely regarded as a key technology to accelerate renewable power generation and reach climate targets. Installing a wind turbine on a floating structure comes with opportunities as well as new engineering challenges. In the Dutch-funded project HybridLabs (https://hybridlabs.tudelft.nl), we accelerate the development of innovations in offshore and floating renewable energy technologies. A key bottleneck to the implementation of these innovations is the system integration of different actors/needs and the supply chain readiness. In this context, we are looking for a post-doctoral researcher to work on multi-disciplinary design analysis and optimisation (MDAO) for floating wind farms in different regions. The tasks involve both the development and dissemination of our MDAO software and its application to assess logistical aspects of the large-scale deployment of floating wind farms. Key research questions include: (i) what are the supply chain requirements and bottlenecks for large-scale deployment of floating wind farms, (ii) how can the system be optimised, and (iii) how much can technical, monetary, and schedule risks be reduced or mitigated. As a researcher, you will work among diverse and energetic peers which offers a stimulating and inclusive working environment for developing your research and academic skills. In addition, due to the highly multidisciplinary nature of this project, your research will contribute to and benefit from others and you will work in teams with other researchers from TU Delft and other institutions within the HybridLabs framework. You will also have the opportunity to work closely with companies as well as help strengthening the European ecosystem in this area. Finally, there will be opportunities to use the MDAO framework for outreach activities. We are committed to fostering an inclusive, supportive and progressive workplace culture built on respect, community and wellbeing. We aim to attract outstanding global talent from all backgrounds and recognise that science and engineering benefit from diverse perspectives. We particularly encourage applications from women, who are currently underrepresented at this level within our university. Job requirements PhD. degree in system engineering, applied sciences, wind energy, or a related field. Fundamental knowledge and application of MDAO (multi-disciplinary analysis and optimisation). Good knowledge of scientific computing, object-oriented programming (e.g., Python), and version control (e.g., git). Experience with FAIR and open-source software development is a plus. Familiar with the system and/or supply chain challenges for offshore/floating wind energy. Experience with supply chain modelling for offshore/floating wind energy is a plus. Curiosity to engage with multi-disciplinary stakeholders. Experience with collaboration across institutions is a plus. Attitude to teamwork and excellent communication skills in spoken and written English, combined with demonstrated creativity, self-learning skills and an inclination towards research. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 2 years. Temporary. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Prof. Axelle Viré, via avire@tudelft.nl . This is a project supported by the Dutch National Research Council (NWO) under the project HybridLabs (project number NWA.1518.22.066) of the research programme Dutch Research Agenda – research along NWA routes by consortia. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Prof. Axelle Viré. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 3977 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-University-Teacher-Bachelor-Computer-Science-and-Engineering-Bachelor-Health-and-Technology-2628-CD/1375100357/": {
      "title": "University Teacher Bachelor Computer Science and Engineering / Bachelor Health and Technology Job Details",
      "description": "University Teacher Bachelor Computer Science and Engineering / Bachelor Health and Technology Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » University Teacher Bachelor Computer Science and Engineering / Bachelor Health and Technology Are you passionate about education? Would you be excited to share your Computer Science knowledge with the next generation? If so, we have the perfect opportunity for you! Job description The departments associated with Computer Science at TU Delft are seeking a highly motivated and passionate individual to fill the position of University Teacher. As University Teacher, you will be responsible for (co-)teaching high-quality instructions in both the Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) BSc program and potentially the new Health and Technology BSc Program in collaboration with Erasmus University Rotterdam. Additionally, you will contribute to the overall educational environment. We are looking for an additional full-time team member to our CSE Teaching Team who shares our desire to teach and improve education. Since its inception in 2018, the Teaching Team had a significant impact on the quality of education in the CSE BSc program, successfully teaching and guiding hundreds of students.  More information about our team can be found here . The Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) BSc program The Computer Science and Engineering BSc program is a comprehensive and accredited 3-year computer science program with a yearly intake of approximately 550 students and a total student population of around 1600 students. The program is taught in English, and we have a diverse and international student population. Our program balances theoretical computer science courses with practically oriented courses in which theory is applied. The students have two capstone projects, one where they typically do an industry internship, and one where they dive into a research assignment. The Health and Technology BSc program The Bachelor Health & Technology is a newly accredited BSc program that will start in September 2027. The program is taught fully at the Erasmus University campus in Rotterdam but is provided by the TU Delft. The program focusses on educating a new type of engineer who will be capable of tackling wicked problems in the health domain, by forming a bridge between medical professionals and engineers. An example of such a problem is the aging of the population. The Computer Science Teaching Team will (co-)teach at least two courses in this new bachelor program: a first-year course on programming where students learn about Python and AI tooling, and a second-year course on data visualisation. As the program is taught in Dutch, a work division will be made between the programs in Delft and Rotterdam, based on the capabilities and capacity of the candidate and the other members of the teaching team. What will you do as a University Teacher? You will (co-)teach courses from our CS-related programs. This includes preparing and delivering lectures, designing and/or improving course materials, organizing practical sessions, leading discussions, assessing student performance, and providing constructive feedback. All our courses are taught by a pair/team of lecturers, thus good cooperation skills are essential. You will work within a team of lecturers who are all passionate about education. You will get a lot of freedom to work on the things you enjoy, but you can also benefit from the guidance and experience of your team members. You will also be able to engage in education innovation. In addition, you will recruit and lead teams of teaching assistants. Job requirements We are looking for candidates who are passionate about teaching and education. We are committed to help you develop your teaching competencies further. You have completed a MSc in Computer Science or a related field. You have demonstrated affinity and enthusiasm with (some selected) topics taught in the first years of the Computer Science and Engineering BSc program, like algorithms, databases, embedded systems, software engineering, programming, artificial intelligence, computer networks, multimedia processing, etc. You have strong interpersonal and communication skills, and work well in teams and with diverse groups of students, faculty, and staff. You are expected to obtain a University Teaching Qualification (UTQ) within three years to develop your teaching competencies further. This is provided by the TU Delft UTQ program. If you already have relevant experience, this may result in a (partial) exemption. You are expected to have good command of the English language, as TU Delft sets high standards for the English competency of the teaching staff. The TU Delft offers training to improve English competency. As the Health and Technology program will be taught in Dutch, command of the Dutch language is highly appreciated, but not a hard requirement. Ideally, you have prior affinity with teaching and/or academia, for example through teaching at other institutions, obtaining a PhD degree, or other relevant experience. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 3 years. Temporary with prospect of permanent. A job of 32-40 hours per week. A salary based on Scale 10 of the CAO for Dutch Universities with a salary between €3706 - €5760 gross per month based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. You are expected to work on site at least 60% of the time. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Taico Aerts, Program Management, BSc CSE, via t.v.aerts@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 22 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: Detailed CV Motivational letter A teaching statement, outlining your personal teaching experience, teaching philosophy, and your preferred teaching best-practices. Please also clearly outline your previous teaching experience, and the fields / topics you could / would want to teach. Recent teaching evaluations (if available). You can address your application to Taico Aerts, Program Management, BSc CSE. Part of the second stage of the application process will be an interview with a committee and a trial lecture. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 32-40 FTE: 0.8-1.0 Submission is possible until: 22 Nov 2026 ID job: 3976 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-MENTOR-Multi-fidelity-ENgine-inTegration-Optimization-for-Next-Generation-AiRcraft-2628-CD/1374975957/": {
      "title": "Postdoc MENTOR: Multi-fidelity ENgine inTegration Optimization for Next Generation AiRcraft",
      "description": "Postdoc MENTOR: Multi-fidelity ENgine inTegration Optimization for Next Generation AiRcraft Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc MENTOR: Multi-fidelity ENgine inTegration Optimization for Next Generation AiRcraft Help shape the next generation of aircraft. At TU Delft, you will develop advanced simulation and optimization tools to improve engine-airframe integration, aerodynamic efficiency and noise performance. Job description The next generation of aircraft calls for innovative propulsion technologies, more efficient airframes and improved noise performance. But how can we accurately predict the complex interactions between engines and airframes? As a postdoctoral researcher at TU Delft, you will develop a multi-fidelity computational framework to optimize aircraft engine integration, aerodynamic performance and aeroacoustics. Your research will contribute to the design and assessment of future aircraft. You will work on MENTOR (Multi-fidelity Engine Integration Optimization for Next Generation Aircraft) , a research project bringing together experts from TU Delft and the Royal Netherlands Aerospace Centre (NLR). Your challenge is to develop an integrated toolbox combining high-fidelity simulations, fast aerodynamic prediction methods and aeroacoustic models. Your research will focus on three interconnected areas: High-fidelity aerodynamic optimization: Develop a design tool combining adjoint-based optimization with unsteady Reynolds-Averaged Navier–Stokes (URANS) simulations to integrate different propulsion systems with low-drag airframes. Fast performance prediction: Combine blade element momentum (BEM) theory and vortex lattice methods to efficiently predict propulsive efficiency and engine-airframe drag. Aeroacoustic prediction: Develop models compatible with NLR tools, using flow distortion theory to predict tonal noise and stochastic optimization approaches for broadband noise components. MENTOR is part of the Dutch Aviation Systems Analysis Lab (DASAL) , a flagship collaboration between TU Delft and NLR, funded through the Dutch National Growth Fund's Luchtvaart in Transitie programme. DASAL develops integrated models and simulations to support innovation in the Dutch aviation sector and inform public policy. You will join the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at TU Delft the Department of Flow Physics and Technology . Here, you will work in an interdisciplinary environment alongside PhD candidates, postdoctoral researchers and academic staff. Collaborating closely with NLR experts and researchers across the faculty, you will connect advanced computational methods with real-world aircraft design challenges and contribute to the development of more efficient and quieter aircraft. Job requirements You hold a PhD in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field. You have a strong foundation in aerodynamics, aeroacoustics and computational fluid dynamics (CFD). You have experience with numerical simulations and computational methods for aerodynamic analysis. You are familiar with CAD modelling software and its application to aerodynamic design. You have an interest in multidisciplinary optimization, propulsion integration and the development of computational prediction tools. You take initiative, approach complex research challenges analytically and develop practical solutions. You communicate effectively in English and enjoy collaborating with researchers from different disciplines and organizations. Knowledge of Dutch is an advantage, but not a requirement. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 3 years. Temporary. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about the Vacancy feel free to contact D. Ragni, d.ragni@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 29 October 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter Optionally, upload the best 3 documents (or links to resources) that show your experience in the aforementioned topics. You can address your application to Daniele Ragni. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 29 Oct 2026 ID job: 3972 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Procesmanager-Onderwijsplanning-2628-CD/1374925357/": {
      "title": "Procesmanager Onderwijsplanning Functiedetails",
      "description": "Procesmanager Onderwijsplanning Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Procesmanager Onderwijsplanning Gaat jouw hart sneller kloppen van het verbeteren van processen en ben je sterk in het verbinden van mensen en belangen? Dan zoeken we jou als procesmanager onderwijsplanning. Functieomschrijving Als procesmanager onderwijsplanning werk je aan een effectief, transparant en toekomstbestendig proces voor de planning en roostering van onderwijs en tentamens. Je brengt processen en werkzaamheden rondom roostering in kaart en maakt rollen, verantwoordelijkheden en afhankelijkheden inzichtelijk. Daarnaast zorg je voor de samenhang tussen processen, beleid en ondersteunende systemen, waaronder TimeEdit. Vanuit je centrale rol bij ESA werk je nauw samen met de faculteiten en andere onderdelen binnen de TU Delft. Je gaat actief in gesprek, signaleert verbetermogelijkheden en vertaalt deze naar heldere afspraken en concrete procesverbeteringen. Je werkzaamheden bestaan onder andere uit: Het analyseren, beschrijven en optimaliseren van processen rondom roostering. Het zichtbaar maken van werkzaamheden, rollen, verantwoordelijkheden en afhankelijkheden binnen het roosterproces. Het ophalen en afstemmen van werkwijzen en verbetermogelijkheden bij faculteiten en andere betrokken partijen. Het verbinden van verschillende belangen en perspectieven en deze vertalen naar heldere procesafspraken. Het begeleiden en borgen van nieuwe of gewijzigde processen. Het vertalen van beleidswijzigingen naar processen en procedures op het gebied van roostering. Het verbeteren van de aansluiting tussen processen en ondersteunende systemen, waaronder TimeEdit. Het functioneel aansturen van de roosteraars. Het deelnemen aan projecten en werkgroepen rondom onderwijsplanning. Het bijdragen aan de ambitie om meer data rondom onderwijsplanning en roostering te verzamelen t.b.v. analyses, gesprekken en besluiten. Het afstemmen van de match tussen onderwijsvraag en zalenaanbod met team Onderwijshuisvesting. Functie-eisen Je bent sterk in analyseren, structureren, vastleggen en verbinden. Dit komt tot uiting doordat je complexe processen snel kunt doorgronden en helder kunt beschrijven. Je weet verschillende perspectieven en belangen bij elkaar te brengen en onderwerpen op een constructieve manier bespreekbaar te maken. Je weet bevindingen en verbetervoorstellen om te zetten in concrete afspraken en resultaten. Essentieel hierbij is dat je goed kunt samenwerken met personen in operationele tot bestuurlijk functies en pro-actief bent in het zoeken naar verbinding met betrokken partners. Daarnaast vragen we: HBO+ of universitair werk- en denkniveau. Ervaring met het analyseren, beschrijven en verbeteren van processen. Affiniteit met data en informatieanalyse. Ervaring met informatiesystemen en digitalisering. Sterke schriftelijke en communicatieve vaardigheden. Goed ontwikkeld analytisch vermogen en organisatiesensitiviteit. Ervaring met functionele aansturing of het coördineren van werkzaamheden. Kennis van en ervaring binnen het hoger of wetenschappelijk onderwijs is een pré. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Education & Student Affairs Education & Student Affairs (ESA) ondersteunt het College van Bestuur en het onderwijs van de gehele instelling met (strategisch) onderwijsbeleid, met het voeren van de onderwijs- en studentenadministratie, coördinatie van het onderwijsbeleid, functioneel beheer onderwijsapplicaties en realisatie monitoring- en management rapportages, het begeleiden en ondersteunen van (buitenlandse) studenten en promovendi, het verzorgen van (didactische) trainingen, het geven van onderwijskundig advies en ondersteuning, en het aanbieden van sport & cultuur activiteiten. ESA bestaat uit de afdelingen Policy & Implementation, Education Service Centre, Academic Services, Information Management en X en telt ongeveer 500 medewerkers. ESA staat binnen de TU Delft bekend om de hoge kwaliteit van haar dienstverlening en kent een proactieve en oplossingsgerichte cultuur. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 11 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €4925 - €6682 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Laura Bovelander via l.bovelander@tudelft.nl of 06-18597542. De selectiegesprekken vinden plaats op: donderdag 12 november 2026. Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 9 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Laura Bovelander. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Education & Student Affairs Salaris range: €4925 - €6682 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 9 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3971 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Positions-on-Silicon-Carbide-Quantum-Networks-2628-CD/1374936757/": {
      "title": "PhD Positions on Silicon-Carbide Quantum Networks Job Details",
      "description": "PhD Positions on Silicon-Carbide Quantum Networks Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Positions on Silicon-Carbide Quantum Networks Job description We are recruiting several PhD candidates to join the Taminiau lab in research on quantum networks based on spin defects in silicon carbide (SiC). As a part of the team, you will work alongside scientists to investigate and develop SiC devices that enable fast optical entanglement links and high-fidelity spin-qubit control. The research combines the design and fabrication of nano-photonic SiC devices, with quantum optics experiments to demonstrate small, but scalable, quantum networks for distributed quantum computation, simulations, and communication. The Taminiau Lab is an international and collaborative group where people from different backgrounds work closely together, share ideas openly, and support each other's development. We value diversity, teamwork, and creating an environment where everyone can contribute and grow. Requirements You have a MSc in science in (applied) physics, quantum technologies, material science, or a related field. You are highly motivated to work on the nano fabrication and characterization of quantum devices for quantum networks. Relevant experience in device fabrication, nanophotonics and/or experimental quantum physics (e.g. with spins or superconducting systems) are appreciated but not essential. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. QuTech At QuTech, we work on radically new technologies with world-changing potential. Our mission: to develop scalable prototypes of a quantum computer and a quantum internet by integrating world-class research and groundbreaking innovation. Through excellence, relevance, and leadership, we cultivate a vibrant quantum technology ecosystem. Together, we are creating the quantum future, because we believe that quantum technologies can be a game changer in many societal and economic sectors, including health, agriculture and safety. Have a look at our video and get a glimpse of QuTech. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact Dr, Tim Taminiau at T.H.Taminiau@TUDelft.nl . Group website: https://taminiaulab.qutech.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 December 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Dr. Tim Taminiau. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: QuTech Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 38 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 15 Dec 2026 ID job: 3973 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-on-Quantum-Control-2628-CD/1374937557/": {
      "title": "PhD Position on Quantum Control",
      "description": "PhD Position on Quantum Control Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position on Quantum Control Job description We are looking for an enthusiastic PhD candidate to join the Taminiau Lab investigating the high-fidelity and scalable control of qubits based on spins associated to atomic defects in solids, including in diamond and silicon carbide. One key challenge towards larger quantum networks for quantum communication and distributed quantum computation is to realize extremely high-fidelity quantum control, in ways that are compatible with scaling to hundreds to thousands of qubits. In this research, we aim to realize high-fidelity control through a combination of quantum gate design and precise understanding of the spin physics (i.e. the Hamiltonian and noise processes in the material). The Taminiau Lab is an international and collaborative group where people from different backgrounds work closely together, share ideas openly, and support each other's development. We value diversity, teamwork, and creating an environment where everyone can contribute and grow. Requirements You have a MSc in science in (applied) physics, quantum technologies, electrical engineering, or a related field. You are highly motivated to work on quantum physics and quantum control. Relevant experience in experimental quantum physics (e.g. with spins or superconducting systems) is appreciated but not essential. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. QuTech At QuTech, we work on radically new technologies with world-changing potential. Our mission: to develop scalable prototypes of a quantum computer and a quantum internet by integrating world-class research and groundbreaking innovation. Through excellence, relevance, and leadership, we cultivate a vibrant quantum technology ecosystem. Together, we are creating the quantum future, because we believe that quantum technologies can be a game changer in many societal and economic sectors, including health, agriculture and safety. Have a look at our video and get a glimpse of QuTech. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact Dr, Tim Taminiau at T.H.Taminiau@TUDelft.nl . Group website: https://taminiaulab.qutech.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 31 October 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Dr. Tim Taminiau. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: QuTech Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 38 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 31 Oct 2026 ID job: 3974 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Exam-Support-Officer-2628-CD/1374981557/": {
      "title": "Exam Support Officer Functiedetails",
      "description": "Exam Support Officer Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Exam Support Officer Werk jij graag in een dynamische omgeving en wil jij ervoor zorgen dat ruim 2.500 tentamens vlekkeloos gemaakt kunnen worden? Functieomschrijving Als Exam Support Officer verzorg je de logistieke organisatie van de tentamens voor de gehele TU Delft. In samenwerking met andere afdelingen zorg je ervoor dat de docenten de tentamens schriftelijk of digitaal kunnen afnemen. Je zorgt dat alle studenten bij de juiste zalen zijn aangemeld en je zet de toetsen klaar voor afname in de diverse toetsapplicaties. Wij maken onder andere gebruik van ANS en Grasple. Het logistieke beheer in de MyCase-applicatie is hier een belangrijk onderdeel van. Tijdens tentamens ben je de digitale steun en toeverlaat van onze surveillanten in de zaal via de Microsoft Teams chat. Bij problemen ken jij de weg in onze toetsapplicaties en help je de studenten snel weer aan de gang. Je denkt actief mee over verbetervoorstellen voor de processen omtrent tentamineren. Hierover stem je af met de procescoördinator. Rond en in onze tentamenweken is er sprake van 'piekdrukte' in het team en kan extra inzet van de medewerkers worden gevraagd. Ook kan er tijdens tentamenweken geen verlof opgenomen worden. Functie-eisen Je hebt een HBO werk- en denkniveau en een goed ontwikkeld analytisch vermogen. Je hebt goede sociale en communicatieve vaardigheden en neemt graag initiatief. We zoeken een collega die zeer nauwkeurig werkt en het leuk vindt om alle details kloppend te krijgen. Je bent gewend om met diverse doelgroepen te communiceren en hebt hierin een open en dienstverlenende houding. Je beweegt je met gemak door de digitale wereld en hebt affiniteit om met diverse ingewikkelde applicaties te werken. Daarnaast lukt het je om overzicht te houden over de werkzaamheden. Je hebt teamspirit en je kunt goed samenwerken. Voor deze functie is het van groot belang dat je stressbestendig bent, je flexibel opstelt en een groot verantwoordelijkheidsgevoel hebt. Ervaring in het ondersteunen van studenten of docenten wordt gewaardeerd, evenals affiniteit met het hoger onderwijs en kennis van tools zoals Microsoft Teams. Een vloeiende beheersing van zowel de Nederlandse als Engelse taal is vereist en ervaring met Excel is een pré. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Education & Student Affairs Education & Student Affairs (ESA) ondersteunt het College van Bestuur en het onderwijs van de gehele instelling met (strategisch) onderwijsbeleid, met het voeren van de onderwijs- en studentenadministratie, coördinatie van het onderwijsbeleid, functioneel beheer onderwijsapplicaties en realisatie monitoring- en management rapportages, het begeleiden en ondersteunen van (buitenlandse) studenten en promovendi, het verzorgen van (didactische) trainingen, het geven van onderwijskundig advies en ondersteuning, en het aanbieden van sport & cultuur activiteiten. ESA bestaat uit de afdelingen Policy & Implementation, Education Service Centre, Academic Services, Information Management en X en telt ongeveer 500 medewerkers. ESA staat binnen de TU Delft bekend om de hoge kwaliteit van haar dienstverlening en kent een proactieve en oplossingsgerichte cultuur. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 08 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3537 - €4673 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Laura Bovelander via l.bovelander@tudelft.nl of 06-18597542. De selectiegesprekken vinden plaats op: vrijdag 13 november 2026 Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 9 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Laura Bovelander. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Education & Student Affairs Salaris range: €3537 - €4673 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 9 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3979 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Healthy-Joints-Multiscale-Modeling-of-in-Vivo-Knee-Loading-2628-CD/1374806757/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Healthy Joints Multiscale Modeling of in Vivo Knee Loading",
      "description": "Postdoc Healthy Joints Multiscale Modeling of in Vivo Knee Loading Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Healthy Joints Multiscale Modeling of in Vivo Knee Loading Are you looking to make a positive impact on people’s health and quality of life? Do you have the skills and desire to shape the future of multiscale musculoskeletal modeling for human health? Job description Healthy joints are essential for mobility, independence and quality of life. Yet osteoarthritis (OA) is rapidly becoming one of the largest chronic health challenges in the Netherlands and worldwide. The Convergence Health & Technology ‘Healthy Joints’ Flagship brings together a consortium from TU Delft, Erasmus MC, and Erasmus University Rotterdam to better understand OA and its progression. We are a large team of clinicians, engineers, data scientists, imaging specialists and more, and we are working together to improve prevention, early diagnosis, and personalized treatment for individuals with OA. Our multi-scale approach investigates joint health and disease at the cellular-, tissue-, joint-, whole person-, and societal-levels. The Biomechanical engineering department at TU Delft is seeking a talented and motivated part-time postdoctoral researcher to join our team in a fixed-term position for the final year of the Healthy Joints project. You would be joining the work package focused on “Multiscale modeling pathomechanics of joint and tissue load In vivo”. In this role, you would support the team in continuing to build and refine existing multiscale musculoskeletal models and apply these models to evaluate cartilage stress in individuals with OA. This will include tasks like developing or refining algorithms, processing and analyzing biomechanics and imaging data, supporting translation and dissemination activities, and supervising masters and PhD students. Your primary focus would be to work strategically to ensure the sustainability of this research line beyond the Healthy Joints project, working together with the team to write proposals and apply for funding. Job requirements We are looking for an ambitious, independent, and collaborative postdoctoral researcher with a strong background in multiscale musculoskeletal modeling, who is motivated to build an independent research line that extends the work of Healthy Joints. Required qualifications A PhD in Biomechanical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Computer Vision, Robotics, or a related discipline A strong curiosity for human movement analysis and multiscale musculoskeletal modeling Experience with optical motion capture data collection, processing, modeling, and analysis, preferably with clinical/experimental gait data in musculoskeletal populations Advanced skills in algorithm development, data analysis, and computational modeling (Python, OpenSim) Excellent project management and communication skills to manage a multi-site project across academic and industry partners Works independently yet thrives in a collaborative, multidisciplinary team Fluent in Dutch and English Persuasive scientific writing Excellent track record in acquiring grants within an academic or industry setting Demonstrated track record in knowledge dissemination (publications in top tier scientific journals, presentations at international conferences) in biomechanics, osteoarthritis, or a related field TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporarily with a posibility for extension. A job of 8-14 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information For more information about this position please contact Ajay Seth ( a.seth@tudelft.nl ). Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 31 October 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Ajay Seth. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 8-14 FTE: 0,33 Submission is possible until: 31 Oct 2026 ID job: 3925 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Optomechanical-IR-Sensing-2628-CD/1374854657/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Optomechanical IR Sensing",
      "description": "Postdoc Optomechanical IR Sensing Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Optomechanical IR Sensing Sensing enabled by optomechanical systems Job description We are seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to join a collaborative project between TU Delft (Simon Gröblacher’s group) and AMOLF (Ewold Verhagen’s group), centered around the development of cutting-edge optomechanical sensors. The position is embedded within QSTeM, a recently established Testbed for mechanical sensing led by Letizia Catalini, where novel sensors are designed, benchmarked, and developed with both academic and industrial partners. The research conducted within this framework will initially focus on the development of optomechanical devices for infrared sensing and imaging. Infrared sensing will serve as a starting point for the project, while other sensing modalities and device concepts may be explored as the work develops and new application opportunities emerge. The work will span several aspects of sensor development, including device and material engineering, nanofabrication, optical characterization, and measurement protocols. Particular attention will be given to the design and fabrication of nanostructured devices and to understanding how material properties, thermal transport, and device geometry influence sensor performance. The project will also explore strategies to improve sensitivity, stability, reproducibility, and robustness, with the broader goal of advancing optomechanical sensor technology toward real-world applications. This applied and interdisciplinary orientation creates an excellent opportunity to explore fundamental research questions while engaging directly with the challenges associated with developing reliable and high-performance sensor systems. In addition to conducting research, the postdoc will actively contribute to measurements and benchmarking services for external partners. This includes performing characterization of sensor devices developed by collaborators and supporting QSTeM’s mission as a reliable and high-performance testing facility. The researcher will be primarily based at the QSTeM testbed facility in Delft, working day-to-day with the joint TU Delft and AMOLF teams. Led by Letizia Catalini, QSTeM provides a highly interdisciplinary and application-driven setting in which researchers from both institutions work closely together and interact with academic and industrial partners. Additionally, the postdoc will be part of the Gröblacher group at the Department of Quantum Nanoscience at TU Delft, with full access to mentoring, to group activities and to an exciting and collaborative environment and to state-of-the-art facilities, including advanced cleanroom infrastructure for realizing next-generation nanostructures. At the Gröblacher Lab, we aim to create an inclusive environment where a diverse mix of talented people can learn, pursue their scientific interests, and do their best work. We are committed to promoting equality, creating a safe and supportive environment for everyone, and fostering diversity across race, gender, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, national origin, age, socioeconomic background, and the many other characteristics that shape our perspectives and experiences. We believe that diversity strengthens both our science and our community. Job requirements PhD in optomechanics, nanophotonics, nano-engineering, applied physics, or a related field. Strong hands-on experience with nanofabrication and the development of nanoscale, photonic, or optomechanical devices. Experience with experimental optics, photonics, optomechanics, nanomechanics, or optical sensing. Interest in device and material engineering, including the role of material properties and thermal transport in sensor performance. A collaborative mindset and strong communication skills. Experience with numerical modelling and simulation of mechanical or optical systems (e.g. finite-element simulations) is an advantage. Prior experience with infrared sensing, multimode mechanical systems, or advanced sensing protocols is a plus. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 2 years. Temporary. A job of 38 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Recruitment-tnw@tudelft.nl . For more information about our work and this position please see https://nl.linkedin.com/company/qstemnl/ and https://groeblacherlab.tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 11 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: Cover letter, in your cover letter (max. 1 A4) please elaborate on your vision on mechanics based sensing / your experience with related topics / your motivation to join our team / your personal drive and ambitions. Please note that in line with our department's vision, we value personally written letters with \"imperfections\" above AI generated \"perfection\". CV, in your CV please ensure your previous level of experience with nanofabrication, quantum optics, photonics and / or nanomechanics is clearly stated. You can address your application to Simon Groeblacher. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 11 Nov 2026 ID job: 3927 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Flexibility-in-Nuclear-Power-2628-CD/1374840257/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Flexibility in Nuclear Power",
      "description": "PhD Position Flexibility in Nuclear Power Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Flexibility in Nuclear Power Can nuclear- and renewable energy play nice? Job description Both Europe and the Netherlands are committed to transitioning to a CO2-neutral economy by 2050. As part of this commitment, the Netherlands has built large-scale wind park, and a significant amount of energy comes from solar power as well. While wind and solar energy help to decarbonize power generation, it also comes at a cost. Due to the intermittent availability of wind and solar energy, grid congestion can occur (which means that the grid lacks sufficient capacity to handle demand or supply of electricity). Therefore, the grid must be carefully managed. In many countries, gas power plants help manage the grid. However, since natural gas counteracts decarbonization, the question arises: “which other technologies can help reduce grid congestion? Small modular reactors (SMR) - nuclear reactors below 300 MWe – may be able to operate flexibly to help counteract grid congestion. As such reactors have less inertia, they are better suited to load-following than large-scale nuclear power plants. Even so, their ramp rates are much lower than other technologies. Through smart design of the power cycle and the inclusion of thermal energy storage, ramp rates of SMR’s can be greatly enhanced. In this thesis project, you will design advanced power cycles with or without energy storage for SMR’s to enable enhanced load-following. Using numerical techniques, you will couple transient power cycle modelling with nuclear reactor modelling to analyse any feedback to the reactor. You will run different load-following scenarios to ascertain technologically feasible enhanced ramp rates. You will be assisted by an expert supervisory team during your PhD. As the Dutch Nuclear industry is growing rapidly, and the Dutch Government has announced a significant expansion of nuclear energy, your results may actively contribute to shaping the Dutch nuclear landscape. Your Working Environment You will join the Process & Energy (P&E) department at TU Delft’s Mechanical Engineering faculty.Our department works along the themes of Energy, Flow and Processes. You will work together with top researchers highly skilled in thermodynamics, heat transfer, fluid mechanics. Moreover, we collaborate with researchers from the Reactor Institute Delft. You will have opportunities for professional development through both technical and non-technical courses. We expect that as part of your PhD you will take the lead on interacting and collaborating with other researchers at TU Delft, with research groups at other universities, and with industry and other stakeholders. Job requirements We are looking for a candidate with 1) ample experience in thermodynamic system modelling, in particular transient modelling; for example, heat pumps or power cycles. Any interest in nuclear is a plus. Furthermore, we expect that you have 2) A MSc. degree in either physics or mechanical engineering or similar field. 3) Strong affinity with thermodynamics and transport equations. 4) A keen interest in the nuclear industry and its future roles in society. 5) Keen interest in transient modelling and analysis. 6) Good communication skills and the ability to be a team player in a highly multidisciplinary setting. For this vacancy, a knowledge embargo exemption is required. Please check the following website: https://www.government.nl/themes/education/secondary-vocational-education-mbo-and-tertiary-higher-education/exemption-certain-engineering-or-nuclear-related-courses-of-study TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. For this vacancy, a knowledge embargo exemption is required; please see here. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters ( j.w.r.peeters@tudelft.nl ). Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Applying for an exemption for specific research and educational areas is an obligatory part of the selection procedure for this vacancy. This exemption must be obtained from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science (OCW) before an employment contract is agreed upon. Click here for more information. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 3936 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Experimental-Analysis-of-Boiling-Instabilities-in-Advanced-Nuclear-Steam-Generators-2628-CD/1374840057/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Experimental Analysis of Boiling Instabilities in Advanced Nuclear Steam Generators",
      "description": "PhD Position Experimental Analysis of Boiling Instabilities in Advanced Nuclear Steam Generators Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Experimental Analysis of Boiling Instabilities in Advanced Nuclear Steam Generators Help determine operational limits of next-gen nuclear steam generators! Job description Advanced nuclear reactor designs like the high temperature gas cooled reactor or molten salt reactor offer certain advantages compared to traditional light water reactors. One such advantage is their potential to operate with a high thermal efficiency. This advantage stems from the fact that these reactors operate at much higher temperatures, enabling superheated steam generation. Traditional light water reactors utilize so-called U-tube steam generators in which saturated steam is produced. It is well known that such steam generators suffer from spontaneous oscillations of two-phase mass flow and pressure drop on the shell side. This phenomenon is well understood in light water reactors, allowing for safe and stable operation. However, these boiling instabilities are more severe in once-through helical steam generators, as the dryout point will shift rapidly up and down along the helical tubes. This oscillating behaviour can lead to thermal fatigue of the tube walls, which can ultimately result in mechanical failure. While this phenomenon is already complex enough in and of itself, it typically coincides with parallel channel instabilities. In this project, you will develop and build a laboratory steam generator set-up to study boiling instabilities in helical tubes. In the first year, you will help design and build the set-up along with a team of skilled technicians and an energetic supervisory team. Subsequently, you will study the characteristics of the boiling instabilities within the set-up and compare them to a numerical model. Your Working Environment You will join the Process & Energy (P&E) department at TU Delft’s Mechanical Engineering faculty.Our department works along the themes of Energy, Flow and Processes. You will work together with top researchers highly skilled in thermodynamics, heat transfer, fluid mechanics. Moreover, we collaborate with researchers from the Reactor Institute Delft. You will have opportunities for professional development through both technical and non-technical courses. We expect that as part of your PhD you will take the lead on interacting and collaborating with other researchers at TU Delft, with research groups at other universities, and with industry and other stakeholders. Job requirements We are looking for a candidate with 1) ample experience in experimental techniques and design of experiments involving physical transport phenomena. Furthermore, we expect that you have 2) A MSc. degree in either chemistry, physics or mechanical engineering or similar field. 3) Strong affinity with thermodynamics and transport equations. 4) A keen interest in the nuclear industry and its future roles in society. 5) An interest in transient modelling and analysis. 6) Good communication skills and the ability to be a team player in a highly multidisciplinary setting. For this vacancy, a knowledge embargo exemption is required. Please check the following website: https://www.government.nl/themes/education/secondary-vocational-education-mbo-and-tertiary-higher-education/exemption-certain-engineering-or-nuclear-related-courses-of-study TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters ( j.w.r.peeters@tudelft.nl ). Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Applying for an exemption for specific research and educational areas is an obligatory part of the selection procedure for this vacancy. This exemption must be obtained from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science (OCW) before an employment contract is agreed upon. Click here for more information. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 3937 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
