    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Battery-Health-Assessment-for-Energy-Storage-Systems-2628-CD/1374662257/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Battery Health Assessment for Energy Storage Systems",
      "description": "Postdoc Battery Health Assessment for Energy Storage Systems Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Battery Health Assessment for Energy Storage Systems Develop next-generation battery diagnostics for large-scale energy storage. In this postdoc, you will combine EIS, data-driven modelling and power electronics to advance battery health assessment. Job description Battery energy storage systems are playing an increasingly important role in the transition towards renewable and resilient power systems. To operate these systems safely and efficiently throughout their lifetime, reliable information about battery health and degradation is essential. Conventional battery monitoring methods, however, provide limited insight into the internal electrochemical processes that determine ageing and performance. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) offers a promising way to obtain this information. Translating EIS from controlled laboratory measurements to practical large-scale battery energy storage systems introduces new scientific and engineering challenges. These include extracting robust health indicators under varying operating conditions, combining impedance information with operational data, and implementing impedance measurements using existing power-electronic hardware. In this postdoc project, you will develop impedance-based and data-driven methods for advanced battery health assessment and investigate their integration into battery energy storage systems. Your research will bridge battery diagnostics, artificial intelligence and power electronics, with a strong focus on methods that can ultimately be applied in industrial BESS applications. The project is carried out in collaboration with Sungrow, providing an opportunity to work at the interface between academic research and industrial battery energy storage technology. You will collaborate with researchers and engineers from TU Delft and the industrial partner and contribute to scientific publications and the dissemination of project results. The postdoc will work in the DC Systems, Energy Conversion and Storage (DCE&S) group of the Department of Electrical Sustainable Energy at TU Delft. The group conducts research and education in energy storage, DC systems, power electronics, electric mobility and renewable energy integration. Would you like to know more about the ESE department and the DCE&S group? Please take a look at the webpage www.tudelft.nl/ewi/ese . Job requirements Who are we looking for? You have a PhD degree in Electrical Engineering or a related engineering discipline from a well-established university. A solid background in battery management systems, battery ageing, battery diagnostics, and power electronics. Experience with electrochemical impedance spectroscopy or other frequency-domain battery characterisation techniques. Experience with experimental battery testing and analysis of measurement data. Experience with scientific programming and data analysis using Python, MATLAB or comparable tools; A good command of written and spoken English. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporary. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. Zian Qin, via Z.Qin-2@tudelft.nl . For information about the selection procedure, please contact Sharmila Rattansingh, management assistant, email: s.rattansingh@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 27 October 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter addressed to Dr. Zian Qin that explains your personal motivation in pursuing a Postdoc in general, and this topic in specific, and why you would be an excellent fit to the job requirements. Please do not use ChatGPT or other tools for providing a standard/non-personalized letter PhD degree or proof of defense date You can address your application to Dr. Zian Qin. NOTE that applications will be assessed on a rolling basis and suitable candidates will be invited for interview, so it is recommended not to wait until the deadline with your application. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 27 Oct 2026 ID job: 3959 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Information-Security-Officer-2628-CD/1374558857/": {
      "title": "Information Security Officer Functiedetails",
      "description": "Information Security Officer Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Information Security Officer Maak impact op de digitale weerbaarheid van de TU Delft! Als Information Security Officer help je directies en faculteiten om risico’s te beheersen en securitymaatregelen daadwerkelijk in de praktijk te brengen. Functieomschrijving De TU Delft is een complexe organisatie met een grote diversiteit aan informatie, systemen en processen. Van digitale onderwijs- en onderzoeksomgevingen tot financiële systemen en de IT die onze campus ondersteunt. Als Information Security Officer (ISO) draag je bij aan het veilig en weerbaar houden van deze omgeving. Als ISO ben je de verbindende schakel tussen het centrale securityteam en verschillende directies, zoals ICT, Finance, Education & Student Affairs en Campus Real Estate en faculteiten. Je brengt informatiebeveiligingsrisico's en kwetsbaarheden in kaart, adviseert over passende beheersmaatregelen en bewaakt de voortgang en effectiviteit daarvan. Daarbij zorg je ervoor dat securitybeleid niet alleen op papier bestaat, maar daadwerkelijk wordt toegepast in de praktijk. Ook speel je een belangrijke rol in het vergroten van security awareness binnen de organisatie. Actuele thema's zijn onder meer de implementatie van de Cyberbeveiligingswet, Patchmanagement, ISO 27001-compliance en het versterken van de digitale weerbaarheid van de organisatie. Je helpt directies inzicht te krijgen in hun risico's en kroonjuwelen, prioriteiten te stellen en noodzakelijke maatregelen aantoonbaar op te volgen. Je voert security assessments uit, bespreekt risico's met management en IT-verantwoordelijken en ondersteunt bij het opstellen en monitoren van verbeterplannen. Je toetst de werking van beheersmaatregelen en adviseert gevraagd en ongevraagd over informatiebeveiligingsvraagstukken. Daarnaast zorg je ervoor dat relevante ontwikkelingen, dreigingen en risico's tijdig bij de juiste stakeholders terechtkomen. Om succesvol te zijn combineer je technische kennis met organisatiesensitiviteit. Je weet waar verantwoordelijkheden liggen, welke risico's het meest relevant zijn en welke maatregelen nodig zijn om deze effectief te beheersen. Je verbindt stakeholders, spreekt verantwoordelijken aan op risico's en gemaakte afspraken en helpt hen deze te vertalen naar concrete en haalbare verbeteringen. Als ISO werk je vanuit de tweede lijn. De uitvoering van securitymaatregelen ligt bij de lijnorganisatie en de verantwoordelijke directies. Jouw rol is om te adviseren, richting te geven, risico's inzichtelijk te maken en de voortgang van maatregelen onafhankelijk te bewaken. Je werkt nauw samen met collega's binnen het centrale securityteam, informatiemanagers, ICT-verantwoordelijken, architecten, privacy professionals en andere stakeholders. Je bent regelmatig in gesprek met management en weet complexe technische vraagstukken helder en praktisch uit te leggen. Zo draag je bij aan een eenduidige, risico gestuurde aanpak van informatiebeveiliging binnen de TU Delft, met ruimte voor de specifieke context en belangen van iedere directie. Je werkt in een innovatieve omgeving waar digitalisering, onderzoek en onderwijs samenkomen. Dat maakt informatiebeveiliging uitdagend en veelzijdig en biedt volop ruimte om impact te maken en jezelf verder te ontwikkelen. Geen dag is hetzelfde: de ene dag bespreek je risico's en maatregelen met ICT, de volgende dag adviseer je een directie over een beveiligingsvraagstuk of werk je mee aan een organisatiebrede securityaanpak. Je beweegt moeiteloos tussen techniek, risico, beleid en management en weet deze werelden met elkaar te verbinden. Functie-eisen Je hebt wo werk- en denkniveau. Je hebt enkele jaren relevante ervaring op het gebied van informatiebeveiliging, bijvoorbeeld als security consultant, security officer, auditor of risk professional. Je hebt kennis van informatietechnologie, informatiebeveiliging en de risico’s die daarmee samenhangen. Je bent in staat om snel inzicht te krijgen in processen, systemen, belangen en risico’s binnen een complexe organisatie. Je bent analytisch sterk en kunt complexe securityvraagstukken vertalen naar concrete en begrijpelijke adviezen. Je bent communicatief vaardig en vindt het prettig om met verschillende stakeholders, van IT-specialisten tot management, in gesprek te gaan. Je bent organisatiesensitief, zelfstandig en tegelijkertijd een teamspeler. Je weet mensen op een constructieve manier mee te krijgen in het belang van informatiebeveiliging. Ervaring met onderwerpen als patchmanagement, vulnerability management, riskmanagement of security assessments is een pré. Je beheerst het Nederlands en Engels goed, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Directie ICT Bij de directie ICT werken we met circa 200 collega’s verdeeld over een aantal teams: Shared Service Center, Project Management Services, Informatiemanagement, Security, Privacy & Architectuur en Innovatie. We werken als directie ICT gezamenlijk met de faculteiten en andere directies van de TU Delft aan uiteenlopende projecten. De complexiteit en grootte van de organisatie zorgen ervoor dat ons werk vaak een uitdagende puzzel is. De grootste opdracht waar we de komende jaren als TU Delft voor staan, is het versnellen van de digitalisering om zo onze positie als universiteit van wereldklasse te versterken. We werken veel samen met de specialisten op onze eigen ICT-afdeling en met onze collega’s verspreid over de universiteit. De campus is een bruisende omgeving waar altijd van alles gebeurt. De cultuur is informeel en inclusief. Er is ruimte voor een belangstellend gesprek bij de koffieautomaat en als je het leuk vindt, kun je deelnemen aan diverse activiteiten die op de campus worden georganiseerd. Bovendien krijg je binnen de directie ICT het vertrouwen en de vrijheid om je eigen werk in te delen. Er is veel mogelijk op het gebied van opleidingen en wij vinden jouw persoonlijke ontwikkeling belangrijk. Wil je meer weten over hoe het is om bij ICT te werken en zien welke vacatures er nog meer zijn? Bekijk dan hier onze werken-bij-ict pagina. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 38-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 12 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €5932 - €7573 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Jan Bouwsma, Manager CIO Office J.Bouwsma@tudelft.nl Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 2 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Jan Bouwsma. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – IT Salaris range: €5932 - €7573 Uren per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 2 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3923 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Senior-copyright-medewerker-Onderwijs-2628-CD/1374546957/": {
      "title": "Senior copyright medewerker",
      "description": "Senior copyright medewerker - Onderwijs Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Senior copyright medewerker - Onderwijs Help jij de TU Delft met adequaat en kostenbewust omgaan met auteursrechten? Functieomschrijving Als senior copyright medewerker ben jij de spil in onze dienstverlening rond copyright. Waar kom je te werken? Je maakt deelt uit van het team Education Support van de TU Delft Library - een hecht, gezellig en gedreven team van 10 collega’s. Het team runt het copyright informatie punt, verzorgt trainingsmodules op het gebied van informatie- en datavaardigheden, ondersteunt docenten bij open onderwijs publicaties en voert de regie op een aantal applicaties. De universiteit vindt naleving van auteursrechtwetgeving, licentievoorwaarden en regelingen, zoals de landelijke Easy Access Regeling, belangrijk.  Als ondersteuning hiervoor is ons copyright informatie punt ingericht. Binnen dit informatiepunt zet jij je talenten in drie gebieden in: coördinatie, afstemming, controle & advisering. Coordinatie Je coördineert de dienstverlening vanuit ons Copyright Informatiepunt. Het gaat hierbij om werkzaamheden van 4 collega’s aangevuld met student assistenten. Je plant copyright controles op onderwijsmaterialen en open publicaties, zet taken hiervoor uit bij collega’s (en jezelf) en coördineert de uitvoering. Ook bewaak je dat vragen over auteursrecht adequaat worden beantwoord door het team. Antwoorden op veel vragen staan op onze websites – je stuurt op de juistheid en actualiteit hiervan. Omdat het informatiepunt nog in ontwikkeling is, zie jij het als een uitdaging om diensten en processen samen met je collega’s verder aan te scherpen. Je denkt mee hierover en doet voorstellen voor verdere automatisering. Kennis van ICT of de bereidheid deze kennis te ontwikkelen is hierbij een sterke pré (in het bijzonder van Microsoft 365, Excel, Planner, Lists). Afstemming Je onderhoudt de contacten met onze faculteiten voor de controles van leermaterialen en met rapportages informeer je ze over controle-uitkomsten. Binnen de faculteiten kan de kennis van auteursrecht versterkt worden. Je weet relevante medewerkers bij de faculteiten in beweging te krijgen. Wanneer er behoefte is aan een goed inhoudelijk gesprek, heldere presentatie of een training over auteursrecht, pak je dat met plezier op, in zowel Nederlands als het Engels. Je stemt daarnaast af met andere afdelingen, zoals Legal Services. Extern vertegenwoordig je onze universiteit in werkgroepen rond auteursrecht, waar je input geeft bij landelijke vraagstukken. Je volgt ontwikkelingen in auteursrechtelijke wet- en regelgeving en geeft input voor beleid en acties. Controle en advisering Je werkt zelf actief mee in het team. Je voert periodieke controles uit. En beantwoordt, samen met je collega’s, binnenkomende vragen (waarbij jij met name de complexere vragen oppakt, soms in samenwerking met  andere specialisten). Algemeen Bij TU Delft vinden we een goede werk-privébalans belangrijk. Je kunt rekenen op flexibele werktijden en de mogelijkheid om 40% van je tijd per week thuis te werken. Daarnaast geloven we in ontwikkeling - als je nog niet voldoet aan bepaalde vereisten, maar sterk gemotiveerd bent om deze te ontwikkelen, solliciteer dan en licht dit toe in je motivatiebrief – we bieden diverse mogelijkheden, zoals trainingen, om verder te groeien in je vak. Functie-eisen HBO-werk- en -denkniveau Ervaring met auteursrecht of minimaal sterke affiniteit ermee. Je bent bereid je hierin verder te ontwikkelen en relevante cursussen te volgen. Pré: ervaring met auteursrecht in de context van hoger onderwijs. Je houdt van organiseren en coördineren en kan dit ook goed - je kunt planningen en procedures ontwikkelen en je team hierin meekrijgen. Je zet taken uit, houdt overzicht, ondersteunt, grijpt in waar nodig, werkt gestructureerd en resultaatgericht. Je bent pragmatisch ingesteld. Het gaat bij copyrightcontroles om variërende aantallen controles. Jij organiseert en brengt rust en ritme in het team. Je denkt procesmatig en analytisch, signaleert waar verbetering mogelijk is, lost problemen graag op en werkt nauwkeurig en zorgvuldig. Het geeft je energie om proactief contacten te leggen en te onderhouden, kennis over te dragen en je invloed gepast in te zetten. Je hebt goede communicatieve vaardigheden en vindt het leuk juridische regels en consequenties begrijpelijk uit te leggen, via verschillende kanalen. Je spreekt en schrijft goed Nederlands en Engels (beiden minimaal C1 niveau, een inhoudelijke presentatie leveren in beide talen kun je prima aan). Je bent IT-vaardig, kent Office tools goed (met name Excel, Teams) en leert snel nieuwe applicaties aan. Je hebt al enige ervaring in het inrichten en verbeteren van administratieve processen (deels geautomatiseerd) en bijbehorend digitaal gegevensbeheer. Pré: Je hebt affiniteit met de universitaire wereld en weet je goed in te leven in de behoeften van docenten, studenten en onderzoekers. Je bent woonachtig in Nederland. We bieden voor deze functie geen internationale verhuisregeling. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – TU Delft Library TU Delft Library is de grootste technisch-wetenschappelijke bibliotheek van Nederland, een fysieke en virtuele ontmoetingsplek. De Library helpt bij het vinden van waardevolle kennis die nodig is voor onderwijs en onderzoek, en bij het publiceren en bewaren van de gegenereerde kennis van de TU Delft. We vinden het belangrijk dat kennis gemakkelijk toegankelijk is en vrij beschikbaar is voor iedereen. Zo kan kennis vrijelijk gaan stromen en de kennis van de TU Delft van waarde worden voor anderen. In de Library kan iedereen ook altijd terecht om in alle rust te studeren. Dit past bij onze inclusieve organisatie. De Library heeft drie strategische thema’s gekozen als leidraad voor haar dagelijkse werkzaamheden. 1) Open Science. We hebben een belangrijke bijdrage in het TU Delft brede strategische programma “Open Science – Research and Education in the Open Era”. 2) Zichtbaarheid en impact. Met onze expertise en tools op het gebied van research datamanagement, research intelligence en publiceren, vergroten we de vindbaarheid, zichtbaarheid en impact van TU Delft-kennis. 3) Inspirerende leer- en werkomgeving. Door middel van een prikkelende programmering laten we zien hoe vrij beschikbare en betrouwbare kennis het leven rijker maakt. Daarmee is de Library een plek waar je nieuwe ideeën en inzichten vindt. https://www.tudelft.nl/library/ Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is Bepaald. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 09 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3873 - €5264 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Roeland Loggen, r.p.loggen@tudelft.nl of 06-14770908. Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 6 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Geef in je brief een helder beeld van jezelf door antwoorden op deze vier vragen: 1. wat jou drijft, 2. wat je aanspreekt in de functie en 3. waarom jij een goede kandidaat bent, 4. en waar je nog verder in kan en wil groeien. We stellen op prijs als je dit zonder AI doet, omdat het zelf beantwoorden van deze vragen een essentiele reflectiestap is (en AI deze informatie niet heeft over je, hopelijk). Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Roeland Loggen. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – TU Delft Library Salaris range: €3873 - €5264 Uren per week: 32 FTE: 0,8 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 6 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3934 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-in-Natural-Fiber-Composites-with-Recyclable-Resins-2628-CD/1374589057/": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Natural Fiber Composites with Recyclable Resins",
      "description": "Postdoc in Natural Fiber Composites with Recyclable Resins Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc in Natural Fiber Composites with Recyclable Resins From polymer to bio-fibre composites and back. Job description The position aims to contribute to our on-going activities within the COMPOCYCLE consortium, financed by the TopSectorEnergy program including several industrial partners, research institutes and academic partners. In the project we aim to develop 100% biobased, thermosetting fibre composites that are both recyclable and immediately deployable. You will work on the development of natural-long fibre composites with recyclable and dynamic (vitrimer) polyester resins. Your research focuses on the processing and recyclability of these composite materials, including investigation of the curing behaviour, impregnation, and chemical/physical ageing impact on recycling and reprocessing using various manufacturing routes. Through processing experiments you will explore small-scale composite production and chemical recycling, analyse the resulting microstructure and its efffects on mechanical properties, and link processing parameters to performance and circularity. The work will be carried out at the Aerospace Structures and Materials department labs including the Delft TapeLab, polymer processing and advanced characterization labs at the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering and in close collaboration with academic and industrial partners. Job requirements You have a PhD in with significant knowledge on relevant components such as Composite/Processing Engineering, Chemical Engineering, and Polymer Technology and Processing. Knowledge on dynamic polymers and recycling is highly welcome. You have experience with experimental research, preferably involving natural-fibre or thermoset/thermoplastic composites, vitrimer and other dynamic polymer chemistries, or curing and rheological characterisation. Knowledge of chemical recycling, resin degradation mechanisms, or microstructural analysis (e.g. microscopy, DSC, DMA, FTIR) is an advantage. You have demonstrated capabilities in scientific and report writing as well as oral communication. You are curious, interested in underlying science, self-motivated, and able to work independently as well as in a multidisciplinary team. You have excellent communication skills in English and enjoy connecting with both academic and industrial partners. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 2 years. Temporary. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact Prof. Santiago Garcia, ( S.J.GarciaEspallargas@tudelft.nl ) or Prof. Clemens Dransfeld ( C.A.Dransfeld@tudelft.nl ). Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 1 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter in which you outline which part of the job description you find the most compelling. 3 references will be required at a later stage. You can address your application to Prof. Santiago Garcia and Prof. Clemens Dransfeld. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 1 Nov 2026 ID job: 3960 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Synthesis-and-Application-of-Radiation-triggered-Block-Copolymer-Micelles-2628-CD/1374588357/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Synthesis and Application of Radiation-triggered Block Copolymer Micelles",
      "description": "PhD Position Synthesis and Application of Radiation-triggered Block Copolymer Micelles Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Synthesis and Application of Radiation-triggered Block Copolymer Micelles Job description As part of a large national consortium aimed at the development of nanoparticle-based immunotherapy for cancer treatment, you will design, synthesize and characterize radiation-sensitive block copolymers that self-assemble into micelles, and test their ability to encapsulate and release immunotherapeutic agents. You will develop a library of block copolymers with variations in polymer block length and structure, as well as the radiation-sensitive linker. You will assess the efficiency of radiation-induced polymer degradation and cargo release, as well as initial cell studies. The project will be carried out as a collaboration between the groups of prof. Rienk Eelkema (Chemical Engineering) and prof. Antonia Denkova (Radiation Science and Technology). Job requirements You have an MSc degree in chemistry, chemical engineering or equivalent You have proven expertise in multistep organic synthesis You have experience in purification and characterization of organic molecules Experience in polymer synthesis, polymer characterization and physical chemistry are desirable You work well in a team You have a high level of written and spoken English TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact prof. Rienk Eelkema ( r.eelkema@tudelft.nl ). Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 26 October 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to prof. Rienk Eelkema Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 26 Oct 2026 ID job: 3876 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Radio-Science-&-Orbit-Determination-ResearcherDeveloper-%28Tudat%29-2628-CD/1375784757/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Radio Science & Orbit Determination Researcher/Developer (Tudat)",
      "description": "Postdoc Radio Science & Orbit Determination Researcher/Developer (Tudat) Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Radio Science & Orbit Determination Researcher/Developer (Tudat) Contribute to developing an open science orbital dynamics platform based on the TU Delft Astrodynamics Toolbox (Tudat), focussing on applications to radio science for planetary missions. Job description We are seeking a researcher/developer to combine core development of the TU Delft Astrodynamics Toolbox (Tudat) with radio-science application development for the development of an open science spaceflight dynamics infrastructure. The goal is to enable high-fidelity orbit propagation and estimation from real tracking data (Doppler, range, VLBI, etc.) for planetary missions. Additional work packages in the same project will focus on space situational awareness and solar system dynamics. Responsibilities Develop and maintain Tudat’s C++ core and Python interfaces, ensuring performance, robustness, and long-term maintainability. Implement and validate extensions and improvements to radio-science estimation pipelines, including observation models, dynamical models, and mission-specific configuration. Extend relevant background models in Tudat (gravity variations, radiation pressure, atmosphere, spacecraft dynamics) and interfaces for mission data ingestion. Lead the application of the framework to selected missions and representative datasets, including defining validation cases, producing reference results, and coordinating scientific priorities with project partners. Contribute to scientific publications describing the platform and demonstrating scientific results enabled by the radio-science workflows and open-source toolchain. Build end-to-end workflows supporting FAIR and open science, including version-controlled analysis setups and consistent outputs. Write documentation, tutorials, and developer guides; support users via issue tracking and community channels. Collaborate closely with platform developers and scientists across TU Delft and partner institutes. Job requirements A Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Physics, Astronomy or similar Strong software engineering skills in C++ and Python, as well as git, CI, testing, code review, etc. Strong background and research experience in astrodynamics/orbit determination and numerical methods. Experience in the usage and development of Tudat is a strong plus. Experience in usage and development of Tudat or a similar tool is required. Experience with radio tracking data analysis or planetary mission spacecraft dynamics is a strong plus. Ability to work in a multidisciplinary, open-source environment. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. . Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 30 months. Temporary. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dominic Dirkx, via d.dirkx@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Dominic Dirkx. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Applying for an exemption for specific research and educational areas is an obligatory part of the selection procedure for this vacancy. This exemption must be obtained from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science (OCW) before an employment contract is agreed upon. Click here for more information. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 4001 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Bayesian-Modeling-and-Counterfactual-Methods-for-Nanoparticle-Transport-in-Human-Tissue-2628-CD/1375788757/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Bayesian Modeling and Counterfactual Methods for Nanoparticle Transport in Human Tissue",
      "description": "PhD Position Bayesian Modeling and Counterfactual Methods for Nanoparticle Transport in Human Tissue Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Bayesian Modeling and Counterfactual Methods for Nanoparticle Transport in Human Tissue Shape the future of nanoparticle safety and design. Join TU Delft as a PhD researcher using Bayesian and counterfactual modelling to predict nanoparticle transport in human tissue. Job description We are looking for a PhD candidate to build the computational model at the center of a European project on nanoparticle transport in human tissue. You will join the research group of Dr. Sepinoud Azimi, working within the SYNERGIE project (Horizon Europe), a consortium of thirteen partners including Fraunhofer, Roche, the Karolinska Institute, University Hospital Aachen, Mimetas, Ruhr University Bochum and Maastricht University. Small particles from the environment have been detected in human blood, placenta and brain tissue, but it is still not clear what they do there. Dose-response data for humans does not exist and animal studies have not transferred well, and as a result there is no exposure limit for these particles. Part of the reason prediction is so hard is that a particle changes as it moves through the body. It acquires a layer of proteins, it aggregates with other particles, and depending on the material it may partly degrade, so that the particle reaching a given tissue is not the same object that was administered or characterised at the start. Most transport models do not account for this. They treat the particle as fixed, which means they are predicting the fate of something that has already changed. The same difficulty affects engineered nanoparticles for drug delivery, and it is one of the reasons so few of them reach their intended target. SYNERGIE is building a platform of nine human tissue-on-chip models that can be connected to follow a particle through uptake, circulation and storage. TU Delft leads the in silico work package. As a PhD candidate, you will: Build a mechanistic model of how particles move between nine human tissues, and calibrate it against experimental data using Bayesian inference. Work out which physical and chemical properties of a particle decide where it ends up. Develop methods that go beyond prediction: for a particle that behaves badly, what is the smallest change that would fix it, and when should that answer not be trusted. Release the model as open-source software and support its use in regulatory dialogue. You will also contribute to teaching in the department and to the supervision of BSc projects. You will work alongside a postdoctoral researcher and PhD candidates on related problems, and interact with experimental partners across the SYNERGIE consortium. You will have access to the DelftBlue high-performance computing cluster. The intended start date is January 2027. Job requirements MSc in applied mathematics, computational science, physics, systems biology, or a closely related quantitative field. Demonstrated experience building and solving ODE or dynamical systems models. Demonstrated experience with Bayesian inference in a probabilistic programming framework such as PyMC, Stan or NumPyro. Strong scientific programming in Python. Please point us to a repository. Excellent written and spoken English. Preferred qualifications: Continuous optimization or optimal control. Causal inference or counterfactual reasoning. Surrogate modelling, Gaussian processes, or emulation. Physiologically based pharmacokinetic modelling or systems pharmacology. Experience packaging and documenting scientific software. No background in toxicology, nanomaterials, chemistry or biology is required. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Technology, Policy & Management The Faculty of TPM provides an important contribution to solving complex technical-social issues, such as energy transition, mobility, digitalisation, water management and (cyber) security. TPM does this with its excellent education and research at the intersection of technology, society and policy. We combine insights from both engineering and social sciences as well as the humanities. TPM develops robust models and designs, is internationally oriented and has an extensive network of knowledge institutions, companies, social organisations and governments. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Technology, Policy and Management. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. Sepinoud Azimi, via s.azimirashti@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 29 November 2026 via the application button and upload your CV, a brief cover letter, a one-page research statement, and a link to a code repository you have built. In your research statement, please describe what you want to work on, why this position fits, and your experience with dynamical systems modelling and Bayesian inference. If the applicants are selected for an interview, they will be asked to provide contact details of two referees with their consent. You can address your application to Dr. Sepinoud Azimi. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: #EUfunded This is an EU funded project, named SYNERGIE with project number 101288129 within European Union's Horizon Europe research and innovation program You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Technology, Policy & Management Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 29 Nov 2026 ID job: 3924 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Assistant-Associate-professor-in-Resilient-Infrastructure-2628-CD/1375812357/": {
      "title": "Assistant/ Associate professor in Resilient Infrastructure",
      "description": "Assistant/ Associate professor in Resilient Infrastructure Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant/ Associate professor in Resilient Infrastructure Help strengthen the resilience of critical infrastructure through research and education that addresses complex societal challenges. At TU Delft, you will develop innovative approaches to interconnected infrastructure systems, collaborate across disciplines and shape your own research and teaching ambitions. Job description Critical infrastructures, such as energy, water, mobility, food and digital systems, are becoming increasingly interconnected and interdependent. Decisions or disruptions in one domain can have far-reaching consequences for others, affecting the essential services that people and societies rely on every day. Addressing these challenges involves a wide range of actors, such as public authorities, private operators, regulators, and citizens, each bringing different perspectives, priorities and responsibilities. Ensuring resilience of such infrastructures is the core challenge that this position addresses. Understanding these complex systems requires methods that capture interactions between technical, social, organisational and institutional factors. It also requires approaches that can reveal cascading effects across infrastructure domains and help identify effective interventions to strengthen resilience. Drawing on systems analysis, modelling and simulation, and participatory approaches, this research can support a deeper understanding of how critical infrastructures function and how they can better withstand and adapt to disruption. As an Assistant / Associate Professor, you will contribute to this mission through both research and education. You will help advance knowledge and methods for resilient critical infrastructures while inspiring students to address complex societal challenges through systems thinking and inter- and transdisciplinary collaborations. Your responsibilities In this role, you will: Teach and coordinate courses in our core educational programmes, contributing to the development of students’ knowledge of systems thinking, modelling and complex socio-technical challenges. Develop and apply methods to analyze, model and design interventions to address the resilience of complex socio-technical critical infrastructures. Investigate the socio-technical characteristics of infrastructure systems and cascading effects across vital societal functions, such as healthcare systems, energy, water management, food and mobility. Publish your research and contribute to national and international collaborations. Acquire research funding and supervise PhD candidates and postdoctoral researchers, appropriate to your career stage. Supervise Bachelor’s and Master’s students and contribute to the continued development of our educational programmes. Strengthen and complement the section’s methodological expertise through mixed-methods research, building on approaches such as systems engineering, agent-based modelling, participatory modelling and design, co-design and data analytics. Your work environment You will join System Engineering section, part of the Multi-Actor Systems department within the Faculty of Technology, Policy and Management (TPM) at TU Delft. The section brings together expertise in systems engineering, modelling and simulation, agent-based modelling, participatory modelling and design, co-design, and data analytics. These approaches provide a methodological foundation for studying complex socio-technical systems and developing ways to address challenges in critical infrastructure resilience. We believe that we are humans first and academics second. Diverse perspectives strengthen both our research and education, and we foster an environment where colleagues support one another, exchange ideas and have the space to develop their own academic profile. You will work in an academic environment that brings together researchers with different disciplinary backgrounds and perspectives. As part of this community, you will contribute to research and education that addresses societal challenges and helps develop knowledge for positive change. Job requirements We are looking for a collaborative and motivated academic who is passionate about teaching, supervision and research. You bring strong analytical and communication skills, enjoy working across disciplines, and can contribute to a team-oriented research environment while developing your own academic profile. Furthermore, you meet the following requirements: You hold a relevant Master’s degree and PhD in industrial engineering, systems engineering, systems analysis, environmental engineering or another methodologically relevant field. You have a strong publication and research track record, appropriate to your career stage. You have the ability and vision to develop competitive research proposals and secure external research funding. You have enthusiasm for academic teaching and supervision, and can teach courses related to design, modelling and simulation at Bachelor’s and Master’s level. Excellent command of the English language, both spoken and written. Command of the Dutch language is preferred but not required at the start of this position. As all Bachelor's courses are taught in Dutch, we expect the willingness to learn Dutch within two years of your appointment. We realise that we ask for the proverbial 'sheep with five legs' here, so we explicitly encourage you to apply even if you don't meet all criteria but think you are a good fit. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Technology, Policy & Management The Faculty of TPM provides an important contribution to solving complex technical-social issues, such as energy transition, mobility, digitalisation, water management and (cyber) security. TPM does this with its excellent education and research at the intersection of technology, society and policy. We combine insights from both engineering and social sciences as well as the humanities. TPM develops robust models and designs, is internationally oriented and has an extensive network of knowledge institutions, companies, social organisations and governments. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Technology, Policy and Management. Conditions of employment The position is at the level of assistant professor (Academic Career Track) or associate professor, depending on background, experience and leadership (potential). For candidates with a strong interest in education, TU Delft offers a full teaching career path alongside the research track. Assistant Professor During the Academic Career Track, we expect you to grow towards an Associate Professor position within a maximum of eight years, for which a position will be available. With other Academic Career Track colleagues, you will participate in the Academic Career Track Development programme, where you are offered ample opportunities to develop yourself in the areas of Education, Research, Societal Impact & Innovation, and Leadership & Organisation. You will regularly discuss your development and results with senior staff based on a personalized development and performance criteria agreed upon at the start of your Academic Career Track. You will start with a temporary contract that will be converted to a permanent contract no later than 12 -18 months after a positive evaluation, based on continuous confidence in your development potential and fit in the organisation. Salary scale 11-12: €4.925,-- to € 7.573,-- per month gross. Associate Professor For an Associate Professor position, we offer an initial temporary position with the prospect of a permanent contract. The duration of the temporary position is a maximum of 1 year. After a positive performance assessment, you will be employed in a permanent Associate Professor position. Salary scale 13-14: € 6.764,-- to € 8.992,-- per month gross. Inspiring, excellent education is our central aim. We expect you to obtain a University Teaching Qualification (UTQ) within three years if you have less than five years of teaching experience. This is provided by the TU Delft UTQ programme as part of the Academic Career Track Development programme. TU Delft sets high standards for the English competency of the teaching staff. The TU Delft offers training to improve English competency. If you do not speak Dutch, we offer courses to learn the Dutch language within three years. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged and you can work partly from home. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , provides information and personal one-on-one guidance to help you prepare your relocation, and to find housing and schools for children (if applicable). In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact dr. ir. Igor Nikolic, head of the Systems Engineering Section of the MAS Department of TPM, email: recruitment-tbm@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this position? Please apply no later than 7 December 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: Motivation letter (aim for one to a maximum of two pages). We value personally written, authentic letters. Please explain your interest in joining this specific section within TU Delft at this stage of your career, and how you connect with our values, mission, and leadership style. Detailed CV, detailed list of your publications (including a selection of your top 5 publications and a reason of why you chose those ones) as well as key initiatives and contributions in other areas such as communication, (personal) leadership, teaching, entrepreneurship, and societal impact. Statement on research. Your research vision should include a brief overview of your current research and a more extensive description of the future research you aim to pursue in our department as part of your appointment. It should primarily be written from the heart, reflecting your intrinsic motivation for an academic career within your chosen direction. What drives and inspires you in your research work? In addition, it should provide an intellectual reflection on how your research vision aligns with this position and, where possible, how it connects with other research lines in our department. Visit our section page to get an idea of our current people and research: People - Multi-Actor Systems .  The research statement may be as short as one page, but no longer than three pages. Statement on education. Your teaching vision should outline the topics or course programmes you feel confident teaching and can bring to life with that magic touch of contagious enthusiasm. We are also interested in your perspective on teaching and supervision, both in classroom settings and when working with individual students or small groups. Please visit our website to check the courses currently covered by the existing team: Education Department Multi-Actor Systems . The education statement is typically up to one page. You can address your application to dr. ir. Igor Nikolic. Please note: To protect your personal data, we only accept applications submitted via the ‘Apply’ button advertised under the vacancies on our website. Applications and additional information sent by email or through other channels, including unsolicited applications, will not be considered or responded to. This also applies to open applications. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Technology, Policy & Management Salary range: Zie vacaturetekst Hours per week: 32-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 7 Dec 2026 ID job: 4008 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Onderzoeksmedewerker-selectieve-vangmethoden-voor-platvis-2628-CD/1375831757/": {
      "title": "Onderzoeksmedewerker selectieve vangmethoden voor platvis Functiedetails",
      "description": "Onderzoeksmedewerker selectieve vangmethoden voor platvis Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Onderzoeksmedewerker selectieve vangmethoden voor platvis Wil jij bijdragen aan innovatieve vistechnologie voor een selectieve en toekomstgerichte platvisvisserij? Functieomschrijving Als onderzoeksmedewerker ben je betrokken bij het volledige ontwikkeltraject: van het bedenken en ontwerpen van nieuwe concepten tot het testen en valideren van prototypes. Je werkzaamheden bestaan onder andere uit: Ontwerpen en ontwikkelen: Uit het onderzoek ontstaat een conceptueel ontwerp, je maakt de vertaalslag van het onderzoeksidee naar een praktisch werkbare opstelling/experiment Experimenteren en testen: je bereidt de experimenten voor en voert ze uit met behulp van bestaande methoden en technieken Rapid prototyping en proof-of-principle: je ontwikkelt, ontwerpt, bouwt en test diverse opeenvolgende prototypes om de technische haalbaarheid van verschillende oplossingen aan te tonen. De aanpassingen aan het ontwerp worden samen met de betrokken wetenschappers uitgewerkt Je rapporteert de resultaten aan de onderzoekers betrokken bij het onderzoeksproject Prototypeontwikkeling op praktijkschaal: je ondersteunt binnen het project de ontwikkeling naar een minimum viable product (MVP) dat op ware grootte kan worden ingezet tijdens prototypetests in het Visinnovatiecentrum in Stellendam Je werkt nauw samen met een promovendus aan de TU Delft en de vakgroep Experimentele Zoölogie van Wageningen University & Research. Deze samenwerking biedt je de mogelijkheid om technische kennis en experimenteel onderzoek te combineren en bij te dragen aan de ontwikkeling van innovatieve en toekomstgerichte vismethoden. De functie is ondergebracht bij de vakgroep Maritieme en Transporttechnologie en wordt begeleid door Rudy Helmons en Geert Keetels. Functie-eisen Achtergrond in werktuigbouwkunde of een vergelijkbare opleiding Kennis en ervaring met gereedschap-zeebodem interactie is een pre Ervaring met (conceptueel) ontwerpen en het doen van experimenten is een pre Kan goed communiceren in zowel Nederlands als Engels TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Mechanical Engineering Van chip tot schip. Van machine tot mens. Van idee naar oplossing. Vanuit de wil om de omgeving te begrijpen en te achterhalen welke mechanismen daaraan ten grondslag liggen, richten onderzoek en onderwijs zich op fundamenteel begrip, ontwerp, productie, toepassing en verbetering van producten, materialen, processen en (mechanische) systemen. De faculteit ME is een dynamische en innovatieve faculteit met een internationale scope en high-tech lab-faciliteiten. Omdat we zo groot en veelzijdig zijn, kunnen we unieke dwarsverbanden leggen en vakgebieden combineren. Dit vindt zijn weerslag in uitstekend en modern onderwijs dat studenten opleidt tot maatschappelijk betrokken en verantwoordelijke ingenieurs en onderzoekers. De kennis en inzichten die we opdoen, vertalen we in oplossingen voor maatschappelijke vraagstukken, bijdragen aan een duurzame samenleving en aan de ontwikkeling van welvaart en welzijn. Dat is wat ons verbindt in grensverleggend onderzoek, inspirerend onderwijs en (inter)nationale samenwerking. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Mechanical Engineering te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 12 of 13 maanden (einde project 30-11-2027). Tijdelijk. Een functieomvang van 36-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 09 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3873 - €5264 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie en sollicitatieprocedure? Neem dan contact op met Rudy Helmons of Geert Keetels, email: recruitment-me@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 9 November 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Rudy Helmons en/of Geert Keetels. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salaris range: €3873 - €5264 Uren per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 9 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4000 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Ammonia-fuelled-SOFC-ICE-Power%2C-Propulsion-and-Energy-System-Ship-integration-2628-CD/1375849457/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Ammonia-fuelled SOFC-ICE Power, Propulsion and Energy System",
      "description": "Postdoc Ammonia-fuelled SOFC-ICE Power, Propulsion and Energy System - Ship integration Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Ammonia-fuelled SOFC-ICE Power, Propulsion and Energy System - Ship integration The AmmoniaDrive project partners are looking for a post-doc that will bring the AmmoniaDrive concept closer to realisation by addressing ship integration aspects. Job description Decarbonizing shipping? Ammonia is considered by many as an effective hydrogen carrier and sustainable e-fuel for sea-going vessels and other heavy-duty applications, mainly because of its promise of being a cost-effective, carbon-free and relatively energy-dense fuel. However, choosing ammonia as a sustainable shipping fuel does not yet solve the question of how the energy stored in ammonia can be converted into useful (mechanical or electric) power on board of ships. AmmoniaDrive offers a unique solution to this question: a single-fuel, high-efficiency, zero-emission SOFC-ICE power plant that will fit on board of ships without sacrificing range and speed. In this postdoc project, part of the larger AmmoniaDrive project, you will investigate the performance of the NH3-fueled SOFC-ICE power, propulsion and energy system, when it is applied on board of a ship capable of transporting ammonia (a benchmark vessel, with an ideal size and operational profile for the project, is available). Ammonia carriers are expected to be vital for a florishing global hydrogen economy and as such are very good candidates to become early-adoptors of the AmmoniaDrive concept. You will investigate ship design and integration aspects, part-load operation (e.g. in port), off-design and transient loading performance, power and energy management strategies and compliance with safety regulations, to name a few of the unsolved challenges. As part of the AmmoniaDrive team you will have access to the latest insights, developments and modelling techniques as established by the nine PhD researchers within the research project as well as to the enthusiastic AmmoniaDrive partners (10+ maritime companies). Topics in scope of this position include: Gather insights into AmmoniaDrive Power Plant fundamentals, working principles and operational limitations. Gather relevant design and engineering information from AmmoniaDrive partners (e.g. Anthony Veder, Bureau Veritas, C-Job Naval Architects) for a specific case study vessel (e.g. ammonia / chemical tanker). Investigate new modelling approaches and sub-model improvements to enable time-domain simulations of ship voyages and port operations together with MARIN's Zero Emission Laboratory to assess performance, emissions, transient loading capability and to test power&energy management strategies. Disseminate your findings to the scientific community and industrial partners. More information on the AmmoniaDrive project: http://resolver.tudelft.nl/uuid:dd34837a-65d4-497c-b989-8330887d7d89 https://www.linkedin.com/groups/12718699/ https://ammoniadrive.net Job requirements Candidates for this challenging project have a PhD degree and background in Mechanical Engineering, Marine Engineering or similar. Good communication and writing skills in English and the ability to collaborate are necessary as well. Being a postdoctoral researcher at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well with colleagues and project partners. Need-to-have: A PhD degree in Mechanical Engineering, Marine Engineering or similar. Good communication skills in English. Experience with Matlab, Simulink, GT-Power or similar relevant engineering software packages. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporary. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact dr.ir. P. de Vos at p.devos@tudelft.nl or +31(0)152781040. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 23 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to . This publication is part of the project AmmoniaDrive with project number 14267 of the research programme NWO Perspectief which is financed by the Dutch Research Council (NWO). Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 23 Nov 2026 ID job: 3939 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Safe-Planning-and-Decision-Making-under-Uncertainty-for-Long-Horizon-Robot-Autonomy-2628-CD/1375678657/": {
      "title": "PhD Position: Safe Planning and Decision-Making under Uncertainty for Long-Horizon Robot Autonomy",
      "description": "PhD Position: Safe Planning and Decision-Making under Uncertainty for Long-Horizon Robot Autonomy Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position: Safe Planning and Decision-Making under Uncertainty for Long-Horizon Robot Autonomy Join TU Delft and the EU-funded OPERA consortium. Push the frontier of general-purpose AI for robotics and tackle the fundamental tension between long-horizon reasoning and real-time safety guarantees. Job description Robots that operate for long periods among people must plan beyond the next few seconds while staying safe. They need to predict how their surroundings and the people in them will evolve, know how reliable these predictions are, and adapt their plans when the predictions fail. In the EU-funded OPERA project, TU Delft contributes to General-Purpose AI for robotics by developing methods that combine fast, reactive behavior with more deliberate reasoning, planning, and decision-making. In this PhD position, you will develop planning and decision-making methods that let robots act safely and reliably over long time horizons when their knowledge of the environment and of the people around them is incomplete. The research sits at the intersection of model-based planning and control and learning-based models, and addresses the trade-off between safety, performance, and real-time computation. You will formulate the methods and analyze their guarantees and failure modes. This research is connected to OPERA's tasks on GPAI-powered planning and decision-making, on long-term reasoning in human-centered environments, and on adaptive human-robot and robot-environment interaction. Depending on your background, the work may draw on optimal control and model predictive control, motion planning, probabilistic modeling and estimation, or learning-based methods. The emphasis is on methods with a clear formulation and well-understood failure modes, validated in simulation and on real robots. You will work in the Cognitive Robotics Department at TU Delft under the supervision of Prof. Robert Babuška and Dr. Laura Ferranti, and you will be embedded in the Reliable Robot Control Lab (https://r2clab.com/). You will collaborate with OPERA partners across Europe on simulation, perception, and the OPERA open-source toolbox. Job requirements The ideal candidate for this PhD position has a strong background in control, optimization, or motion planning and is motivated by the question of how robots can plan safely and reliably over long time horizons. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds who want to work at the intersection of planning, control, and learning. You have: An MSc degree in Systems and Control, Robotics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field. A strong interest in safe planning and decision-making for robots, at the intersection of planning, control, and learning. A passion for rigorous, theoretically grounded research, combined with an eagerness to validate ideas in simulation and on real robots. Strong analytical and mathematical skills, in particular in optimization, probability and statistics, and dynamical systems. Excellent communication skills and proficiency in English (written and verbal), as required for academic publication and international collaboration. You are particularly encouraged to apply if you have experience in one or more of the following areas: Hands-on experience implementing optimization-based planners or controllers (e.g., model predictive control with acados or CasADi) in C++ or Python. Safe or robust control and planning under uncertainty. Learned dynamics or prediction models, model-based reinforcement learning. Uncertainty quantification, probabilistic or Bayesian modeling, state estimation. Long-horizon or hierarchical planning, prediction of human or multi-agent behavior. Real-robot deployment with ROS or ROS 2. As part of OPERA, you will travel to meet and collaborate with the project’s European partners and attend regular consortium meetings. We particularly encourage applications from women and other underrepresented groups, as we are committed to building a diverse and inclusive research environment. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3059 - €3881 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information, please reach out to Laura Ferranti and Robert Babuska [ l.ferranti@tudelft.nl , r.babuska@tudelft.nl ] Please do not use LinkedIn and other channels for applications or inquiries. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: A letter of motivation explaining why you are the right candidate for this project An updated cv Exam transcipts from your Bachelor and Master A copy of your MSc thesis, or draft MSc thesis (or a link to access it) You can address your application to Laura Ferranti and Robert Babuska. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: #EUfunded This is an EU funded project, named OPERA, with project number 101298363, within program HORIZON/HORIZON-CL4-2025-04-DIGITAL-EMERGING-07 You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3059 - €3881 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 3993 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Hoger-Veiligheidskundige-2628-CD/1375687257/": {
      "title": "Hoger Veiligheidskundige Functiedetails",
      "description": "Hoger Veiligheidskundige Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Hoger Veiligheidskundige Wil jij bijdragen aan gezonde en veilige arbeidsomstandigheden binnen een inspirerende academische organisatie? Bij de TU Delft kan je duurzaam impact maken! Functieomschrijving Bij de TU Delft staan gezondheid, veilig werken en het welzijn van medewerkers en studenten hoog in het vaandel. De afdeling Health, Safety & Environment (HSE) speelt een cruciale rol in het adviseren en ondersteunen van de organisatie op dit gebied. De afdeling HSE bestaat uit 16 gedreven professionals, die werkzaam zijn als HSE adviseur (veiligheidskundigen en arbeidshygiënisten), biologisch veiligheidsfunctionaris, arbeids- en organisatiedeskundige, verzuimregisseurs, projectleiders uitvoering participatiewet, projectleider op het gebied van vitaliteit en managementassistent. Daarnaast is de bedrijfszorg door een extern gecontracteerde arbodienst en bedrijfsmaatschappelijk werk in onze afdeling ondergebracht. Als HSE adviseur maak je samen met zeven collega's deel uit van het HSE adviesteam. Je werkt vanuit dit team zowel voor en op locatie van de faculteit(en) en dienst(en), als aan TU brede beleidsstukken op het gebied van arbeidsomstandigheden. De HSE adviseur werkt samen met faculteiten en diensten op het brede terrein van veiligheid, het optimaliseren van de arbeidsomstandigheden ter voorkoming van onveilige situaties, ongevallen en mogelijke gezondheidsschade. De HSE adviseur is de aangewezen specialist op het terrein van risicobeoordeling en risicobeheersing van de werkomgeving. De komende jaren ligt de focus op verdere professionalisering van de afdeling HSE. Een belangrijk aandachtsgebied hierin is de versterking van de TU brede organisatie op HSE gebied waaraan we gezamenlijk met ketenpartners uit andere diensten (integrale veiligheid, vastgoed en facility management) en faculteiten zullen werken. De HSE adviseur is in staat om een goede balans te vinden tussen het werken aan TU brede onderwerpen en het werken voor de account(s). Daarbij vinden we het belangrijk dat de HSE adviseur zich voortdurend professionaliseert en ontwikkelt in het vakgebied en in vaardigheden. Functie-eisen Je hebt een afgeronde opleiding Hogere Veiligheidskundige en je bent bij voorkeur gecertificeerd. Een aanvullend specialisme zoals biologische veiligheid, arbeids- en organisatiedeskundigheid, arbeidshygiëne, gevaarlijke stoffen of milieu is een pré. Je hebt minstens 5 jaar aantoonbare werkervaring op het gebied van veiligheidskundige vraagstukken, bij voorkeur in grote complexe organisaties. Je hebt ervaring met RI&E’s in dynamische omgevingen, bij voorkeur in onderzoeksomgevingen zoals laboratoria en werkplaatsen. Je haalt energie uit adviseren en creëren van draagvlak, je bent goed in plannen en organiseren, onderzoek en analyse, voorlichting en instructie. Je vindt het leuk om je te bewegen tussen strategisch, tactisch en operationeel niveau. Je beheerst het Nederlands en Engels goed, mondeling en schriftelijk. Deze functie vraagt om een deskundige die inhoud combineert met organisatiesensitiviteit en veranderkracht. Herken je jezelf in dit profiel, maar voldoe je niet volledig aan alle eisen? Ook dan nodigen we je uit om te reageren. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Human Resources Om haar strategische doelstellingen te realiseren zet de TU Delft in op het aantrekken en ontwikkelen van ambitieuze en getalenteerde medewerkers. Het personeelsbeleid is gericht op recruitment en de ontwikkeling van talent, leiderschap en de organisatie, en draagt bij aan de versterking van onderwijs, onderzoek en valorisatie. Een veilige, uitdagende en betekenisvolle werkomgeving staat voorop. Hieraan draagt de HR-organisatie bij met de medewerkers van HR Advies die werken bij de faculteiten en de Universiteitsdienst (de ondersteunende diensten) op locatie, en daarnaast met de centrale HR-diensten van de afdelingen HR Talent & Development, Health Safety Environment (HSE), Compensation & Benefits en HR Services. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 11 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €4925 - €6682 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Thea Overgaauw, manager Health Safety & Environment, via T.A.E.Overgaauw@tudelft.nl of telefonisch 06-41634979. Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 25 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Thea Overgaauw. Het streven is om de eerste ronde sollicitaiegesprekken te voeren op 1 en 3 december 2026. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. Een pre-employment screening kan onderdeel zijn van de selectieprocedure. Een kennisveiligheidscheck maakt onderdeel uit van de sollicitatieprocedure. Deze check zal worden uitgevoerd op de laatst overgebleven kandidaten. Voor meer informatie over deze check verwijzen wij u naar hoofdstuk 8 van de ‘ National Knowledge Security Guidelines ’. Deze check voeren wij uit op basis van de grondslag gerechtvaardigd belang. Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Human Resources Salaris range: €4925 - €6682 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 25 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4007 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-in-Digital-Twins-for-Flood-Resilient-Infrastructure-2628-CD/1375576057/": {
      "title": "PhD Position in Digital Twins for Flood-Resilient Infrastructure",
      "description": "PhD Position in Digital Twins for Flood-Resilient Infrastructure Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position in Digital Twins for Flood-Resilient Infrastructure Develop and implement a Digital Twin that strengthens our ability to protect critical infrastructure against flooding. Job description Current and future impact of flooding to critical infrastructure (e.g. dikes, bridges) is a major concern worldwide. Unfortunately, the management of flood-prone structures is extremely challenging because underlying processes are complex and uncertain. If our capacity to anticipate flood-induced impacts on infrastructure does not improve, societal and economic consequences are likely to be unsustainable. Digital Twins (DTs) offer a promising opportunity to combine recent advances in modelling, data assimilation and machine learning. However, for DTs to support the management of flood-prone infrastructure, they must be effectively integrated with flood-risk modelling. The scientific challenge is to develop methods that enable Digital Twins to leverage multiple models, datasets and computational techniques to improve predictive capacity in real flood-risk contexts. FlooDT (Digital Twin for flood-resilient infrastructure management) is a prestigious and ambitious project funded by NWO. It aims to develop a new methodological framework to exploit the capability of DTs for managing flood risk “from climate prediction to structure protection”. TU Delft is leading the project and a consortium that involves multiple universities (e.g. ETH Zurich, Univ. Polytechnica of Catalunya) and stakeholders (e.g. Deltares, Rijkswaterstaat). The project has also the support of the TU Delft Digital Competence Centre (DCC). For this unique project we are seeking a motivated and talented PhD candidate for a 4-year appointment. In your role you will: Develop functional modules for Digital Twins, such as risk analysis, scenario modelling and processing of monitoring data. Develop hybrid (physics based/machine learning) modelling for flood risk. Apply and validate the Digital Twin functionalities for simplified representation of infrastructure (first) and real case studies (second). Implement the developed functionalities into end users' platforms. Co-organise workshops and co-coordinate stakeholder engagement (e.g. regular meetings, presentations, visits). You will join the FlooDT team and the Flood Risk and Hydraulic Structures section, a collaborative and international team where curiosity, interdisciplinary research and scientific excellence are valued. Our section closely collaborates with the other sections within the Department of Hydraulic Engineering, other departments within our Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geoscience and many research groups around the world. We offer strong support for your professional growth, including mentoring, training, and ample opportunities for international collaboration and networking. This position will open doors to exciting career opportunities in both academia and the future-facing companies that are shaping the next generation of digital technologies. Job requirements We are looking for an excellent, enthusiastic and inquisitive computational researcher who enjoys working in an international and multidisciplinary environment. You have: A MSc degree in Civil Engineering, Computer Science or Hydro-informatics (or in a related discipline). Demostrated experience in numerical modelling, hydrodynamic simulation and data management. Scientific and/or practical knowledge of machine learning. Excellent programming skills (e.g. in Python, SQL, Java, PyTorch, etc.). A critical, creative and pro-active approach to research, with distinctive problem-solving skills. Proven experience with writing scientific reports/publications. Confidence/willingness in engaging with partners and stakeholders. Excellent command of English (oral and written). Previous internship experience with non-academic institutions is desiderable. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences The Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences (CEG) is committed to outstanding international research and education in the field of civil engineering, applied earth sciences, traffic and transport, water technology, and delta technology. Our research feeds into our educational programmes and covers societal challenges such as climate change, energy transition, resource availability, urbanisation and clean water. Our research projects are conducted in close cooperation with a wide range of research institutions. CEG is convinced of the importance of open science and supports its scientists in integrating open science in their research practice. The Faculty of CEG comprises 28 research groups in the following seven departments: Materials Mechanics Management & Design, Engineering Structures, Geoscience and Engineering, Geoscience and Remote Sensing, Transport & Planning, Hydraulic Engineering and Water Management. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences. C onditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information All information are cointained here and general questions will not be answered. For specific requests, please contact Maria Pregnolato ( m.pregnolato@tudelft.nl ). After the first selection, online interviews will be held in December. The candidate is expected to start in March/April 2027. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 18 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV (max 4 pages). Cover letter (max 1 page) describing your motivation and qualifications for the position. Applicants selected for an interview will be asked to provide contact information of at least 2 references. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 32-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 18 Nov 2026 ID job: 3994 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Protection-and-Control-of-DC-Microgrid-for-Electric-Aircraft-2628-CD/1375602257/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Protection and Control of DC Microgrid for Electric Aircraft",
      "description": "Postdoc Protection and Control of DC Microgrid for Electric Aircraft Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Protection and Control of DC Microgrid for Electric Aircraft Join us to advance DC microgrid protection, control, and stability for safe and reliable future sustaibale aviation! Job description DC microgrids with integrated energy storage are a key enabler of the electrification of transportation, industry, data centers, and renewable energy systems. However, the high-power, low-impedance, and dynamically varying DC microgrids introduces significant challenges in system stability and fault resilience. These challenges are particularly critical for electric aircraft, requiring high power density, stringent weight constraints, fast electrical dynamics, and demanding safety requirements. The objective of this postdoctoral position is to develop efficient, stable, and fault-resilient DC microgrids for electric aircraft, addressing challenges from the converter level to the system level. At the converter level, you will investigate power conversion, control, and protection technologies to achieve high power density, robust operation, and effective fault handling. At the system level, you will design DC microgrid architectures that integrate diverse energy sources, power converters, and aircraft loads. A hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) test platform will be developed to validate the proposed solutions. This platform will support research on stability analysis, and the transient and steady-state responses under various faults. A particular focus will be placed on the interaction between protection actions and system control to ensure stable and resilient operation under normal and fault conditions. What You Will Do Develop and validate digital models of energy sources and storage, power electronic converters, and aircraft loads Design DC microgrid architectures for electric aircraft, balancing reliability, efficiency, power density, and weight. Implement an HIL test platform for the selected architecture Investigate DC fault dynamics by analyzing transient and steady-state system behavior under pole-to-pole and pole-to-ground faults, and propose mitigation measures Investigate the interaction between protection and control and develop coordinated protection and control strategies to enhance overall system performance and fault resilience Validate proposed solutions through simulation and HIL experiments What the Position Offers You A state-of-the-art power electronics laboratory, equipped with advanced research and testing facilities, including OPAL-RT, PLECS RT Box, and Imperix power amplifiers An opportunity to conduct high-impact research on electric aircraft, contributing to the future of sustainable aviation Opportunities to contribute to the DC Systems and EV Charging Summer School About the department The research in ESE Department is inspired by the technical, scientific, and societal challenges originating from the transition towards a more sustainable society and focuses on four areas: • DC Systems, Energy Conversion and Storage (DCE&S) • Photovoltaic Materials and Devices (PVMD) • Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) • High Voltage Technologies (HVT) ESE Department owns the ESP laboratory is actively used for testing of grid integration of power electronics, battery degradation, hardware in loop simultion (HIL), AC and DC protection, and wide-area monitoring, protection and control. The DCE&S group is responsible for research and education in the fields of DC systems, energy storage, electronic power conversion (power electronics), electro-mechanics for electric mobility and recently electro-chemical conversion. DC systems is a multidisciplinary field of research, exploring the electronic power conversion of electrical energy for different applications. The group is currently active in applications such as Direct Current distribution grids and microgrids, electrification of mobility (charging of electric vehicles), and renewable generation of electrical energy (such as wind and solar energy) as well as sustainable production of chemicals and fuels through large-scale conversion of renewable electricity into molecular bonds. Job requirements Essential job requirements: Strong research record on electronic power conversion and DC systems Completed a PhD degree in a highly quantitative and analytical discipline (electrical engineering) Demonstrable experience with HIL tests or power system simulations Very good command of English, in both writing and speaking You enjoy performing research. You are independent, self-motivated, and eager to learn Desirables: Knowledge of DC microgird control and stability analysis Knowledge of electric aircraft TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 2 years and 2 months. Temporarily with a posibility for extension. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. Wenli Shi, via W.Shi-3@tudelft.nl . For information about the selection procedure, please contact Sharmila Rattansingh, Secretary, email: S.Rattansingh@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 10 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Dr. Wenli Shi. You will benefit from extensive training in technical and transferrable skills. You will be expected to assist in teaching activities (student supervision, labs) related to your subject area. You will have access to excellent research facilities in ESP lab. If you are interested, do not wait to apply, we are happy to schedule an interview while the response period is running. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 10 Nov 2026 ID job: 3962 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Markerless-Motion-Capture-for-Home-Monitoring-in-Neurological-Populations-2628-CD/1375594157/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Markerless Motion Capture for Home Monitoring in Neurological Populations",
      "description": "Postdoc Markerless Motion Capture for Home Monitoring in Neurological Populations Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Markerless Motion Capture for Home Monitoring in Neurological Populations Are you passionate about shaping the future of healthcare? Do you want to develop technology that truly matters in people’s lives? Join us in creating radical innovations that support patients at home Job description The department of Biomechanical Engineering TU Delft seeks a motivated postdoctoral researcher with a background in biomechanical engineering for a full-time, fully funded project on the clinical validation of single-camera markerless motion capture for assessment and long-term home monitoring of motor impairments in stroke and Parkinson's disease patients. The position is based at TU Delft, supervised by Dr. Eline van der Kruk and Dr. Ajay Seth, with measurements at clinical partner sites and in patients' homes, and part of your time spent on-site at Model Health (Leuven, Belgium) to co-develop the home-based prototype. You will work closely with clinicians, patients, and Model Health, embedded in the multidisciplinary \"Care is coming home!\" program, a 5-year consortium of 2 technical universities (TU Delft, UTwente), 6 hospitals, 13 companies (including Model Health), 1 rehabilitation centre, and 5 patient organisations. The Challenge Reliable, long-term monitoring of motor impairments outside the clinic is essential to support home-based rehabilitation, yet existing markerless motion capture systems are rarely validated on neurological gait patterns and struggle to generalize across pathology, body morphology, camera viewpoint, and home environments. Before such systems can support clinical decisions, we need to know how accurate they really are, for which patients, and under which conditions. We also need to understand which outcome measures are valid and meaningful to patients, caregivers and clinicians.This position aims to close that gap: you will verify and validate a single-camera markerless motion capture system against gold-standard 3D marker-based motion capture and musculoskeletal models, first in the lab and then in patients' homes, linking biomechanical accuracy to clinically meaningful outcomes. You will: • Assess the accuracy of markerless outcome measures against marker-based 3D motion capture and musculoskeletal modelling in people with stroke and Parkinson’s disease. • Use musculoskeletal modelling to compare markerless and marker-based estimates, evaluate their biomechanical plausibility and perform sensitivity analyses • Evaluate whether these outcome measures are valid, meaningful, and acceptable in the home environment, in collaboration with patients, caregivers and clinicians • Generate biomechanically realistic synthetic movement data from musculoskeletal simulations to train and improve markerless motion capture models • Design and carry out home measurements with a single-camera prototype developed together with Model Health, and compare its real-world performance with lab-based measurements • Contribute to clinician-facing visualization of the results, with privacy-by-design protection of patients and their home environment You will translate this into a research plan aimed at peer-reviewed publications, alongside consortium deliverables. Our offer You will become part of the funded research program in the Netherlands named 'Care is coming home!', which involves 9 PhDs and 5 Postdocs. So, we offer an excellent inspiring, collaborative, and international research environment, with access to leading experts in medical technology and AI-driven healthcare solutions. Additionally, you will have access to state-of-the-art labs, clinical partners, and patient organisations, which are preconditions to make a meaningful contribution to the future of sustainable healthcare. • Full-time postdoctoral position for one year, with the possibility of extension by up to two years • Excellent mentorship and a stimulating international research environment with excellent facilities Job requirements We are seeking an ambitious, hands-on postdoctoral researcher who wants to find out whether markerless motion capture truly works for patients, in the lab and at home. You combine a strong engineering background in biomechanics with the communication skills to work directly with clinicians and patients. You bring: • A PhD in Biomechanical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Human Movement Sciences, or a related engineering discipline. • Hands-on experience with musculoskeletal modelling (e.g., OpenSim, AnyBody), including critical evaluation of model outputs. • Experience with marker-based 3D motion capture (e.g., Vicon, Qualisys) and force plates, from protocol design to data processing. • Strong programming skills (e.g., Python and/or MATLAB) for data processing, analysis pipelines, and statistics; experience with markerless or video-based pose estimation (e.g., OpenCap) is a plus. • Experience with, or a strong motivation to work on, measurements in patient populations, preferably people with stroke or Parkinson’s disease. • Excellent communication and organization skills to explain technology clearly to clinicians and to work with patients, including in their home environment. • Willingness to travel regularly to Model Health in Leuven (Belgium), clinical partner sites, and patients' homes in the Netherlands. • Ability to work independently while thriving in a collaborative, multidisciplinary consortium team. • Fluency in English, both written and spoken. • Proficiency in Dutch is strongly preferred, as you will visit patients at home; proficiency in Moroccan Arabic or Turkish is an additional advantage. If you enjoy bringing biomechanics from the lab to the clinic and into people's homes, this postdoc is the perfect opportunity to make a real impact in home-based neurological monitoring. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Mechanical Engineering From chip to ship. From machine to human being. From idea to solution. Driven by a deep-rooted desire to understand our environment and discover its underlying mechanisms, research and education at the ME faculty focusses on fundamental understanding, design, production including application and product improvement, materials, processes and (mechanical) systems. ME is a dynamic and innovative faculty with high-tech lab facilities and international reach. It’s a large faculty but also versatile, so we can often make unique connections by combining different disciplines. This is reflected in ME’s outstanding, state-of-the-art education, which trains students to become responsible and socially engaged engineers and scientists. We translate our knowledge and insights into solutions to societal issues, contributing to a sustainable society and to the development of prosperity and well-being. That is what unites us in pioneering research, inspiring education and (inter)national cooperation. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering. Do you want to experience working at our faculty? These videos will introduce you to some of our researchers and their work. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 36 months. Temporary. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. ir. Eline van der Kruk, email: e.vanderkruk@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 13 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Cover letter If the applicants are selected for an interview, they will be asked to provide contact details of at least two referees with their consent (at least one academic) You can address your application to Dr. ir. Eline van der Kruk. Please note: To protect your personal data, we only accept applications submitted via the ‘Apply’ button advertised under the vacancies on our website. Applications and additional information sent by email or through other channels, including unsolicited applications, will not be considered or responded to. This also applies to open applications. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 13 Nov 2026 ID job: 4003 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Onderzoekstechnicus-Neutroneninstrumenten-bij-TU-Delft-Reactor-Instituut-2628-CD/1375432157/": {
      "title": "Onderzoekstechnicus Neutroneninstrumenten bij TU Delft Reactor Instituut Functiedetails",
      "description": "Onderzoekstechnicus Neutroneninstrumenten bij TU Delft Reactor Instituut Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Onderzoekstechnicus Neutroneninstrumenten bij TU Delft Reactor Instituut Functieomschrijving Onderzoek naar waterstof sensoren die onder extreme omstandigheden nauwkeurig werken. Een dun laagje antibiotica coating onderzoeken op tandimplantaten. Een inkijkje in een oud beeldje uit India dat door een museum beschikbaar is gesteld. Of bijdragen aan de ontwikkeling van nieuwe meetmethodes met een nog hogere resolutie of kortere meettijd. Bij het TU Delft Reactor Instituut hebben we twee neutronenimaging instrumenten en een neutronenreflectometer die de geheimen van dit soort systemen helpen te ontrafelen. Deze experimenten worden uitgevoerd voor en door onderzoekers uit de hele wereld en moeten in goede banen worden geleid. We zoeken twee onderzoektechnici: één met focus op de reflectometer en één met focus op de neutronenimaging-instrumenten. Je maakt ons team compleet met goede computer skills, kennis van natuurkunde, organisatorisch vermogen en passie voor onderzoek.  Op deze manier neem je een unieke plek in binnen het team dat dit onderzoek mogelijk maakt. Werk met impact dus! Je focus ligt op de reflectometer of op de neutronenimaging-instrumenten. Samen met de “instrument scientist” van jouw instrument vorm je een hecht team en zorg je dat gebruikers deze specialistische instrumenten optimaal kunnen inzetten. Daarbij werk je samen met een team van ervaren en minder ervaren technici met uiteenlopende technische specialismen. Je vindt het leuk om gebruikers verder te helpen en technische vragen samen op te lossen. De ene keer betreft het een master student van de TU Delft en de andere keer hebben we onderzoekers uit Italië, waarbij je meegebrachte apparatuur moet integreren in de opstelling. Het TU Delft Reactor Instituut heeft unieke mogelijkheden voor Nederland en zelfs daarbuiten waardoor de levendigheid een internationaal karakter heeft. Binnen het gezellige team zijn er volop kansen om jezelf én nieuwe technieken te ontwikkelen. We kijken goed waar ieders voorkeur naar uitgaat en willen graag een sterk team neerzetten met collega’s die elkaar aanvullen. Samen zijn we onze gebruikers zo goed mogelijk van dienst en faciliteren we de wetenschap. Functie-eisen Je hebt een hbo-diploma, bij voorkeur Technische Natuurkunde. Een stevige basis in natuurkunde is belangrijk en je weet uit ervaring dat je energie krijgt van programmeren en dataverwerking. Je voelt je thuis in een internationale omgeving en kunt in het Engels communiceren met onderzoekers, studenten en collega’s. Nederlands is een pré. Je bent in staat om de wensen van gebruikers te vertalen naar technische mogelijkheden van apparaten en je denkt creatief en praktisch mee. Je bent flexibel en vindt het leuk om technische uitdagingen op te pakken waarvoor niet altijd direct een standaardoplossing bestaat. Je bent flexibel en houdt van uitdagingen die niet altijd volledig te overzien zijn. Je combineert graag praktisch technisch werk met het helpen en begeleiden van gebruikers. Houd er rekening mee dat je incidenteel werkt met radioactieve stoffen en straling. Uiteraard nemen we daarbij de nodige veiligheidsmaatregelen en hebben daarbij zeer hoge interne veiligheid ambities. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. TU Delft | Reactor Institute Het TU Delft| Reactor Institute is het Nederlandse kenniscentrum voor nucleaire technologie en aan straling gerelateerd onderzoek en onderwijs. Het beheert een unieke onderzoeksreactor (2.3 MW), bestralingsfaciliteiten en straling gerelateerde onderzoeksinstrumenten. Het TU Delft |Reactor Institute faciliteert onderzoekers en gebruikers van verschillende onderzoeksdisciplines. Het onderzoek richt zich voornamelijk op materialen voor energieconversie en opslag, en gezondheidstechnologie voor beeldvorming, diagnose en therapie met radionucliden en protonen. Het verzorgt onderwijs aan studenten van verschillende opleidingen binnen de TU Delft en professionals. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 09 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3873 - €5264 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie en sollicitatieprocedure? Heb je de juiste opleiding en ben je benieuwd naar de functie binnen het TU Delft Reactor Instituut? Kom vrijblijvend kennismaken, we geven je graag een rondleiding met informatief gesprek. Neem dan contact op met Jeroen Plomp via j.plomp@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 19 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload jouw documenten. We lezen graag een persoonlijk geschreven motivatie. Liever een brief die echt van jou is en niet helemaal perfect, dan een door AI gegenereerde brief. Een motivatie bijvoegen is niet noodzakelijk, wel ontvangen we graag je CV en/of een linkje naar je LinkedIn. Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Jeroen Plomp. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Bij deze vacature is het aanvragen van een ontheffing kennisembargo een verplicht onderdeel van de selectieprocedure. Voordat er een arbeidsovereenkomst wordt overeengekomen moet deze ontheffing worden verkregen bij het ministerie van Onderwijs, Cultuur en Wetenschap (OCW). Lees hier alvast meer over op de website van OCW. Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. RIDTECH Faculteit/Dienst: RID Salaris range: €3873 - €5264 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 19 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3965 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Veiligheidskundige-voor-wetenschappelijk-onderwijs-en-onderzoek-bij-de-faculteit-TNW-2628-CD/1375360257/": {
      "title": "Veiligheidskundige voor wetenschappelijk onderwijs en onderzoek bij de faculteit TNW Functiedetails",
      "description": "Veiligheidskundige voor wetenschappelijk onderwijs en onderzoek bij de faculteit TNW Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Veiligheidskundige voor wetenschappelijk onderwijs en onderzoek bij de faculteit TNW Ben jij de Veiligheidskundige die graag complexe veiligheidsvraagstukken oplost én vooruitkijkt? Wil je bijdragen aan baanbrekend onderzoek bij TU Delft en tegelijk meebouwen aan een HSE-team en veiligheidscultuur in ontwikkeling? Dan is dit jouw kans om écht impact te maken! Functieomschrijving Bij TU Delft werken we aan een gezonde en veilige werkomgeving, met een proactieve veiligheidscultuur als uitgangspunt. Ons HSE-team en de bijbehorende werkwijzen zijn volop in ontwikkeling om deze visie verder vorm te geven. Daarom zoeken we voor de faculteit Technische Natuurwetenschappen (TNW) een veiligheidskundige, oftewel Department Safety Officer. In deze rol ondersteun en adviseer je twee wetenschappelijke afdelingen over veilig werken en de bijbehorende wet- en regelgeving. Binnen deze afdelingen vindt chemisch, biologisch en fysisch onderwijs en onderzoek plaats. Je werkt in een unieke, innovatieve omgeving waar dagelijks baanbrekend onderzoek en vernieuwend onderwijs samenkomen. De diversiteit aan laboratoria, technieken en veiligheidsvraagstukken maakt je werk afwisselend en uitdagend. Je maakt deel uit van een team van vier Department Safety Officers en twee HSE-adviseurs. Binnen jouw afdelingen werk je zelfstandig en stimuleer je het veiligheidsbewustzijn van onderzoekers, docenten, technici en studenten. Je organiseert veiligheidsrondes, signaleert risico’s en stelt op basis van je bevindingen risico-inventarisaties en -rapportages op. Ook geef je praktische adviezen om risico’s tijdig te herkennen en te beperken. Je vertaalt wettelijke eisen naar werkbare oplossingen en stelt veiligheidsinstructies op voor de verschillende laboratoria. Bij nieuwe experimenten denk je vanaf het begin mee over veilige werkwijzen. Daarbij combineer je je kennis van wet- en regelgeving met inzicht in de dagelijkse onderwijs- en onderzoekspraktijk. Wanneer dat nodig is, spreek je betrokkenen aan op onveilige situaties. Je stemt eventuele handhaving af met de HSE-adviseur en de voorzitter van de betreffende afdeling. Na een incident of ongeval analyseer je wat er is gebeurd en rapporteer je je bevindingen, zodat we ervan kunnen leren. Ook bij verbouwingen en aanpassingen aan de hightechlaboratoria speel je een belangrijke rol. Je adviseert over veiligheidsmaatregelen en denkt mee over een veilige inrichting van onderzoeksruimtes. Daarnaast bereiden de betrokken wetenschappelijke afdelingen zich voor op een verhuizing naar een nieuw gebouw in 2028. Ook daarbij is jouw expertise van belang. Omdat het HSE-team en de werkwijzen nog in ontwikkeling zijn, krijg je de ruimte om mee te bouwen aan betere procedures, een effectieve samenwerking en een sterke veiligheidscultuur. Zo draag je met jouw expertise direct bij aan een omgeving waarin wetenschappers baanbrekende ontdekkingen kunnen doen en studenten praktijkgericht onderwijs kunnen volgen, veilig en met vertrouwen. Functie-eisen We verwelkomen zowel ervaren veiligheidskundigen met kennis van laboratoriumomgevingen die hun expertise verder willen verdiepen en delen in onze unieke wetenschappelijke omgeving als ook zelfstandig werkende technici met ruime ervaring in chemische of fysische laboratoria, inclusief de bijbehorende veiligheidsaspecten. Afhankelijk van je achtergrond heb je een HVK-opleiding afgerond, of ben je bereid om je praktische ervaring als technicus aan te vullen met een MVK- of HVK-opleiding. Daarnaast vragen wij: Je hebt een hbo-diploma in een relevante richting. Overzicht over de verschillende aspecten van veilig werken binnen (bio)chemische en fysische laboratoria. Je communiceert helder en weet veiligheidsaspecten op verschillende niveaus in de organisatie overtuigend en tactisch voor het voetlicht te brengen. Je luistert goed en weet de juiste balans te vinden tussen veiligheid en begrip voor de dagelijkse onderwijs- en onderzoekspraktijk. Je bent leergierig en verdiept je in de werkzaamheden van de wetenschappelijke afdelingen. Je vertaalt complexe wet- en regelgeving naar begrijpelijke adviezen. Je werkt praktisch, handelt onafhankelijk binnen een grote organisatie en bewaakt zelfstandig de kwaliteit van je werk. Je spreekt en schrijft goed Nederlands en Engels. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Technische Natuurwetenschappen Met meer dan 1.100 medewerkers, waaronder 150 baanbrekende hoofdonderzoekers (principal investigators), en ongeveer 3.600 gepassioneerde studenten is de faculteit Technische Natuurwetenschappen een inspirerend wetenschappelijk ecosysteem. Onze faculteit richt zich op sleuteltechnologieën, zoals quantum- en nanotechnologie, fotonica, biotechnologie, synthetische biologie en materialen voor energieopslag en -conversie, en biedt oplossingen voor belangrijke problemen van de 21e eeuw. Daarvoor leiden we studenten op in brede bachelor- en specialistische masteropleidingen met een sterke onderzoekscomponent. Onze wetenschappers verrichten baanbrekend fundamenteel en toegepast onderzoek op het gebied van Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology en Engineering Physics. We leiden ook de volgende generatie middelbare school docenten op. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Technische Natuurwetenschappen te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 10 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3706 - €5760 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie en sollicitatieprocedure? Neem dan contact op met Marja van den Bergh via M.C.M.vandenBergh@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 10 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Marja van den Bergh. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salaris range: €3706 - €5760 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 10 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3980 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Archaeological-Remote-Sensing-Specialist-2628-CD/1375351457/": {
      "title": "Archaeological Remote Sensing Specialist",
      "description": "Archaeological Remote Sensing Specialist Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Archaeological Remote Sensing Specialist Are you the specialist that develops novel Machine Learning methods to extract hidden archeological information from massive remote sensing data? Job description The research to which this vacancy belongs is part of the “Mapping the Archaeological Pre-Columbian Heritage in South America – MAPHSA” project funded by Arcadia – a charitable fund of Lisbet Rausing and Peter Baldwin. The MAPHSA project aims at mapping the pre-Columbian heritage of South America. Within this project we look for an experienced computational scientist with a background in archaeology that is able to lead the contribution of TU Delft. Your daily work will consist of the  development of methodology to identify and interpret typically sparse and hidden information in massive remote sensing data sets of suitable areas in South America. In addition your work will consist of project coordination, communication with other project partners, and communication on your project results to the outside world, by means of scientific publications. An important part of your work will also consist of supervising additional staff and students working on different topics (in)directly related to MAPHSA. Finally you will be asked to contribute to the funding and educational activities of the Department. Your will work with Dr. Roderik Lindenbergh, an expert in 3D environmental and structural monitoring and geometry extraction from complex point cloud and remote sensing data. Within the Dept. of Geoscience and Remote Sensing you will find further expertise on spectral and thermal remote sensing, microwave remote sensing, positioning and navigation, and atmospheric modeling and remote sensing. Job requirements PhD in Archaeology, and knowledgeable in pre-Columbian archaeology. Working knowledge of state-of-the art Machine Learning methodology. Proven experience with different remote sensing acquisition mehods, including LIDAR and spectral Remote Sensing. Able to efficiently process large data sets. Fluent in Spanish and English in speaking and writing. Proven capabilities in acquiring research funding. Experience in education, notably in supervising educational research projects, including BSc, MSc and PhD thesis projects. Experience in project coordination. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences The Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences (CEG) is committed to outstanding international research and education in the field of civil engineering, applied earth sciences, traffic and transport, water technology, and delta technology. Our research feeds into our educational programmes and covers societal challenges such as climate change, energy transition, resource availability, urbanisation and clean water. Our research projects are conducted in close cooperation with a wide range of research institutions. CEG is convinced of the importance of open science and supports its scientists in integrating open science in their research practice. The Faculty of CEG comprises 28 research groups in the following seven departments: Materials Mechanics Management & Design, Engineering Structures, Geoscience and Engineering, Geoscience and Remote Sensing, Transport & Planning, Hydraulic Engineering and Water Management. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 33 Months. Temporary. A job of 28-32 hours per week. A salary based on Scale 11 of the CAO for Dutch Universities with a salary between €4925 - €6682 gross per month based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact Roderik Lindenbergh ( r.c.lindenbergh@tudelft.nl ). Please apply via the website of TU Delft, unsolicited emails will not be considered or answered. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 11 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae. Cover letter, including your motivation for this specific position. Transcripts from your BSc and MSc degrees. If available, a copy of your MSc thesis will be appreciated. Applicants selected for an interview will be asked to provide contact information of at least 2 references. You can address your application to Roderik Lindenbergh. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences Salary range: €4925 - €6682 Hours per week: 28-32 FTE: 0,8 Submission is possible until: 11 Nov 2026 ID job: 3991 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Medewerker-Processen-&-Systemen-Studentmobiliteit-2628-CD/1375314957/": {
      "title": "Medewerker Processen & Systemen",
      "description": "Medewerker Processen & Systemen - Studentmobiliteit Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Medewerker Processen & Systemen - Studentmobiliteit Ben jij de verbindende schakel die ervoor zorgt dat processen en systemen binnen de Student Administration op elkaar zijn afgestemd? Functieomschrijving Binnen de Student Administration wordt het inschrijf- en toelatingsproces van zowel Nederlandse als internationale studenten verzorgd. We begeleiden studenten met een Nederlandse vooropleiding met hun aanmelding via Studielink en we zijn het aanspreekpunt voor studenten met een internationale vooropleiding tijdens het uitgebreide toelatingsproces. Daarnaast verzorgen de collega’s van de Student Administration alles wat er komt kijken op het gebied van beurzen, collegegelden, visa en huisvesting. Het Europese subsidieprogramma E+ is een belangrijk programma binnen Mobility waarmee studentuitwisseling binnen Europa plaatsvindt en waarvan de administratie gedigitaliseerd wordt (ESCI+). Voor het team Admission & Mobility zijn we op zoek naar een collega die ervoor zorgt dat de (digitale) processen rond studentuitwisseling (inkomende en uitgaande exchange) soepel verlopen. Jij bent de verbindende schakel tussen faculteiten, studenten en systemen. Je onderhoudt de gebruikte administratieve systemen en signaleert actief verbeterpunten in de processen. Door analyse en evaluatie draag je bij aan continue procesverbetering en digitalisering. Je werkt nauw samen met de procesmanager en procesbeheerder, functioneel applicatiebeheerders en eindgebruikers om processen efficiënt in te richten en te ondersteunen. In (project)overleggen fungeer je als sparringpartner en adviseer je over systeemaanpassingen. Daarnaast ben je het eerste aanspreekpunt voor collega’s en faculteiten bij vragen over de werking van het studentinformatiesysteem Osiris. Je traint eindgebruikers in functionaliteiten van het systeem, test het systeem voor aankomende wijzigingen en houdt handleidingen en procesbeschrijvingen actueel. Functie-eisen Je bent iemand die initiatief neemt, het eigen werk organiseert, goed kan samenwerken en in staat is draagvlak te creëren voor nieuwe ideeën. Je bent organisatiebewust, beschikt over analytisch vermogen en bent communicatief sterk. De functie vraagt daarnaast: HBO werk- en denkniveau; Ervaring met administratieve processen en vertaling naar geautomatiseerde systemen, waarbij de vertaalslag wordt gemaakt van een knelpunt in het proces naar een oplossing in het systeem; Ervaring met het uitwerken van procesbeschrijvingen en schrijven van (gebruikers)handleidingen en het implementeren hiervan in de uitvoering; Uitstekende communicatieve en digitale vaardigheden (Kennis en ervaring in Excel is een vereiste); Uitstekende beheersing van de Nederlandse en de Engelse taal in woord en geschrift; Ervaring met het (zelfstandig) analyseren, beschrijven en oppakken van (knelpunten in) processen en deze vanuit verschillende perspectieven bekijken; Kennis van Osiris is een pré. Kennis van Lean is een pré. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Education & Student Affairs Education & Student Affairs (ESA) ondersteunt het College van Bestuur en het onderwijs van de gehele instelling met (strategisch) onderwijsbeleid, met het voeren van de onderwijs- en studentenadministratie, coördinatie van het onderwijsbeleid, functioneel beheer onderwijsapplicaties en realisatie monitoring- en management rapportages, het begeleiden en ondersteunen van (buitenlandse) studenten en promovendi, het verzorgen van (didactische) trainingen, het geven van onderwijskundig advies en ondersteuning, en het aanbieden van sport & cultuur activiteiten. ESA bestaat uit de afdelingen Policy & Implementation, Education Service Centre, Academic Services, Information Management en X en telt ongeveer 500 medewerkers. ESA staat binnen de TU Delft bekend om de hoge kwaliteit van haar dienstverlening en kent een proactieve en oplossingsgerichte cultuur. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 28-32 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 08 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3537 - €4673 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Elize van 't Riet ( e.m.vantriet@tudelft.nl of 015-27 82116) Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 8 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Elize van 't Riet. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Education & Student Affairs Salaris range: €3537 - €4673 Uren per week: 28-32 FTE: 0,7-0,8 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 8 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3984 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Data-Steward-Sequencing-&-Phenotyping-2628-CD/1375376557/": {
      "title": "Data Steward",
      "description": "Data Steward - Sequencing & Phenotyping Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Data Steward - Sequencing & Phenotyping TU Delft & CropXR are looking for a Data Steward with a strong affinity for plant research, sequencing and phenotyping data. You will work closely with researchers to make sure that valuable research data is well organised, understandable, findable and reusable. Job description Your responsibilities You will be a bridge between research, data and the CropXR data infrastructure. Your work includes: Supporting researchers with data management throughout the research lifecycle, from experiment design and data collection to publication and long-term reuse. Working with sequencing and phenotyping data, including sample and plant-material information, experimental metadata, sensor and imaging data, and files such as FASTQ, BAM and VCF. Helping researchers describe experiments and datasets using consistent metadata and relevant standards, including MIAPPE, ISA and the CropXR Metadata Management Procedure. Making research data more FAIR by establishing practical conventions for file organisation, naming, identifiers, metadata, versioning and documentation. Reviewing datasets with researchers, identifying missing information, and advising on suitable formats, repositories, access conditions and data publication, including submissions to repositories such as ENA or NCBI. Preparing and connecting datasets for the CropXR Resilience Hub and contributing to CropXR-wide data-management guidelines and best practices. Your approach You combine scientific curiosity with a pragmatic, service-oriented mindset. You enjoy talking to researchers about their experiments, asking the questions that uncover missing context, and translating FAIR data principles into practical actions. You are comfortable working across disciplines and can communicate with experimental scientists, bioinformaticians, data scientists and infrastructure developers. Success means that good data management becomes a natural part of the CropXR research workflow: datasets are well described, can move smoothly into analysis and repositories, and remain understandable and reusable by other researchers. Job requirements You have a completed university degree at MSc level, or an equivalent level of academic training, in a relevant field such as plant sciences, biology, bioinformatics, biotechnology, genetics, computational biology, data science or a related discipline. You have a good understanding of how biological research data is generated and used. You do not need to develop sequencing pipelines or phenotyping platforms yourself, but you should understand sequencing and phenotyping data well enough to communicate effectively with both researchers and technical teams. You are comfortable with metadata, FAIR data principles and research data repositories. Experience with relevant standards and data-management approaches is an advantage, but a willingness and ability to learn is more important. Some familiarity with structured data or scripting — for example Python, R, command-line tools, JSON, CSV or APIs — is useful for understanding and validating datasets. This is not primarily a software-development role. You communicate clearly in English and are comfortable working in a collaborative, interdisciplinary research environment. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Delft University of Technology is built on strong foundations. As creators of the world-famous Dutch waterworks and pioneers in biotech, TU Delft is a top international university combining science, engineering and design. It delivers world class results in education, research and innovation to address challenges in the areas of energy, climate, mobility, health and digital society. For generations, our engineers have proven to be entrepreneurial problem-solvers, both in business and in a social context. At TU Delft we embrace diversity as one of our core values and we actively engage to be a university where you feel at home and can flourish. We value different perspectives and qualities. We believe this makes our work more innovative, the TU Delft community more vibrant and the world more just. Together, we imagine, invent and create solutions using technology to have a positive impact on a global scale. That is why we invite you to apply. Your application will receive fair consideration. Challenge. Change. Impact! Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. CropXR CropXR was launched in 2023 to help make agricultural production less vulnerable to climate change and less dependent on artificial fertilisers and chemical pesticides. It is a collaboration between the universities of Amsterdam, Delft, Wageningen and Utrecht, together with partners from the plant-breeding sector. CropXR brings together plant sciences, computational and data sciences, social sciences and industry to develop more resilient crops and contribute to sustainable agriculture. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 2 years. Temporary. A job of 38-40 hours per week. A salary based on Scale 10 of the CAO for Dutch Universities with a salary between €3706 - €5760 gross per month based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Prof. Marcel Reinders, via m.j.t.reinders@tudelft.nl . This position is with the Delft Bioinformatics Lab, part of the Computer Science department of Delft University of Technology, under the supervision of Prof. Marcel Reinders and Thomas Abeel ( t.abeel@tudelft.nl ). In addition, the position is embedded in DataXR, part of the national CropXR programme, for which Auke Damstra ( technologydirector@cropxr.org ) is CTO. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: A brief Motivation letter explaining your interest in the position, how your background and skills align with the role, and why you would like to work within TU Delft and CropXR. An up-to-date CV detailing your education, work experience and relevant technical or research experience. If applicable, examples of relevant projects or experience related to research data management, bioinformatics, sequencing, phenotyping or scientific data infrastructures. Academic transcripts, if requested or if you are a recent graduate. You can address your application to Prof. Marcel Reinders. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 3995 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-in-ML-Based-Interpretation-of-Geophysical-Legacy-Data-for-Mineral-Exploration-2628-CD/1375334857/": {
      "title": "PhD Position in ML-Based Interpretation of Geophysical Legacy Data for Mineral Exploration",
      "description": "PhD Position in ML-Based Interpretation of Geophysical Legacy Data for Mineral Exploration Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position in ML-Based Interpretation of Geophysical Legacy Data for Mineral Exploration Develop and test new methods for deep exploration of sediment-hosted copper systems by integrating legacy seismic and well-log data with basin modelling, geochemistry and machine learning. Job description We are looking for a PhD candidate who is keen to explore how legacy seismic and well-log data acquired for petroleum exploration can be transformed into a new resource for deep mineral exploration. The candidate will combine quantitative geophysical interpretation, basin modelling and machine learning to investigate a challenging target: the thin Kupferschiefer horizon buried beneath the Netherlands and the North Sea. The Dutch subsurface offers an exceptional dataset of more than 6,000 wells, including approximately 1,700 in which the Kupferschiefer has been identified, together with extensive high-quality 2D and 3D seismic reflection data and available cores. Yet these data were acquired and interpreted for hydrocarbon exploration. Recognizing and mapping a horizon a few metres thick at kilometers depth, and identifying features associated with its mineral potential, requires methods that can extract information across datasets with very different resolution, coverage and physical meaning. The goal of this PhD project is to develop an integrated methodology for characterizing the Kupferschiefer and its geological context. You will analyse well logs to identify the target horizon and extrapolate it to wells where it has not yet been recognized. You will use seismic data for cross-well correlation and improved spatial characterization, and basin analysis to investigate the roles of stratigraphy, faulting and basin evolution. Geological, petrophysical, geochemical and mineralogical information will be integrated to identify characteristics and fingerprints associated with copper mineralization. Machine learning will be an important part of this methodological development. You will establish robust and interpretable baseline models for well-log analysis and investigate approaches designed for sequential data, including convolutional and transformer-based models. You will also contribute to multimodal methods that combine seismic, well-log, geological and geochemical information while incorporating geological knowledge and physical constraints. A postdoctoral researcher will work alongside you for one year, focusing primarily on advanced multimodal and physics-informed machine-learning developments. The research is part of the EU-funded INTELLIGENT project. Results from the Dutch basin will be combined with complementary studies by other groups working on the Kupferschiefer and related systems to develop a regional-scale mineral-system model and transferable exploration workflows. Your multidisciplinary research work will be carried out within the Applied Geophysics and Petrophysics Section and the Resource Engineering Section of GSE at TU Delft. Through close collaboration with TNO, the National Materials Observatory and partners from universities, geological surveys, research institutes and industry across Europe, you will test new methodological ideas within an international network and against a real, societally relevant exploration challenge. Job requirements Being creative and independent, you have the ability to conduct independent research and collaborate across geoscience, engineering and data-science disciplines. You also have: An MSc degree in geophysics, geology, earth sciences, geological or petroleum engineering, or a closely related discipline. Interest in applied geophysics and resource exploration and machine learning methods. Experience in scientific programming (preferably Python or Matlab). Good writing and communication skills. Experience in one or more of the fields below is considered an advantage: Basin analysis, basin modelling or sedimentary-basin evolution. Quantitative interpretation of seismic reflection data and well logs. Petrophysics, low temperature geochemistry and mineralogy. Machine Learning (deep learning and/or statistical learning methods). TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences The Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences (CEG) is committed to outstanding international research and education in the field of civil engineering, applied earth sciences, traffic and transport, water technology, and delta technology. Our research feeds into our educational programmes and covers societal challenges such as climate change, energy transition, resource availability, urbanisation and clean water. Our research projects are conducted in close cooperation with a wide range of research institutions. CEG is convinced of the importance of open science and supports its scientists in integrating open science in their research practice. The Faculty of CEG comprises 28 research groups in the following seven departments: Materials Mechanics Management & Design, Engineering Structures, Geoscience and Engineering, Geoscience and Remote Sensing, Transport & Planning, Hydraulic Engineering and Water Management. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this vacancy, please contact Valentina Socco, Geophysics ( L.V.Socco@tudelft.nl ), Mike Buxton, Resource Engineering ( M.W.N.Buxton@tudelft.nl ), or Jing Sun, Machine Learning ( ing.Sun@tudelft.nl ). Please apply via the website of TU Delft, unsolicited emails will not be considered or answered. #EU funded: This is an EU funded project, named INTELLIGENT: Innovative exploration technologies for deep-targeting critical mineral deposits, HE - Horizon Europe (HORIZON) Call: HORIZON-CL4-2026-01, Project: 101345448, Coordinator Uppsala University. Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 17 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: Motivation letter. Curriculum Vitae, including a list of relevant courses. If applicable, the topic of your MSc thesis. You can address your application to Valentina Socco. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 32-38 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 17 Nov 2026 ID job: 3990 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-IP-&-Technology-Transfer-Manager-2628-CD/1375373157/": {
      "title": "IP & Technology Transfer Manager Functiedetails",
      "description": "IP & Technology Transfer Manager Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » IP & Technology Transfer Manager Help onze wetenschappers baanbrekende uitvindingen te beschermen én naar de markt te brengen! In deze rol sta je midden in de nieuwste technologische ontwikkelingen en maak je innovatie mogelijk. Functieomschrijving Van nieuwe duurzame technologieën tot innovatieve toepassingen in de gezondheidszorg: onze wetenschappers werken dagelijks aan ontdekkingen die de wereld kunnen veranderen. Maar hoe zorg je ervoor dat deze uitvindingen goed beschermd worden teneinde hun weg te vinden naar de samenleving? Als IP & Technology Transfer Manager bij TU Delft speel jij daarin een sleutelrol. Je neemt verantwoordelijkheid in het proces van uitvinding tot octrooi, licentie en/of commerciële samenwerking en je monitort de voortgang en uitkomsten. Zo help je wetenschappelijke kennis om te zetten in maatschappelijke en economische impact. Je bent hierbij het eerste aanspreekpunt voor onderzoekers van onze faculteiten. Je beoordeelt nieuwe uitvindingen op octrooieerbaarheid, waarde en commerciële mogelijkheden. Je adviseert over intellectueel eigendom (IP), ontwikkelt strategieën voor bescherming en vermarkting en begeleidt octrooiprocedures. Daarnaast onderzoek je kansen voor technologieoverdracht, stel je businesscases op en onderhandel je over licenties en andere IP-overeenkomsten, in overleg met je team en Delft Enterprises. In deze functie verbind je wetenschap en bedrijfsleven. Je werkt samen met uitvinders, decanen, startups, mkb-bedrijven en internationale industriële partners. Daarbij weet je uiteenlopende belangen samen te brengen en complexe IP-vraagstukken helder uit te leggen. Soms begeleid je een traject van begin tot eind, terwijl je in andere situaties vooral strategisch adviseert. Steeds zoek je naar de beste manier om innovatieve technologie verder te brengen. Je komt te werken bij het Innovation & Impact Centre (I&IC) van TU Delft, waar het verbinden van wetenschappelijke kennis met de praktijk centraal staat. Hier werk je met je collega's aan het vergroten van de maatschappelijke en economische impact van ons onderzoek. Dat doen we o.a. door: Het beheren en beschermen van TU Delft intellectueel eigendom (IP) en ondersteunen van de wetenschapper in de route van IP naar licenties, spin-offs en benutting van IP in de markt Het stimuleren van ondernemerschap bij wetenschapper en student in samenwerking met andere TU Delft organisatieonderdelen zoals Delft Enterprises Het begeleiden van het opschalen van innovaties in de maatschappij Binnen het I&IC is het IP team jouw thuisbasis. Je werkt in een open, betrokken en grotendeels zelfsturend team van 8 collega's. Samen zorgen jullie voor het beschermen, beheren en vermarkten van intellectueel eigendom, waaronder octrooien, software en merk- en modelrechten. Je richt je vooral op de uitvindingen van onze acht faculteiten, maar werkt ook nauw samen met je directe collega's en andere experts binnen het I&IC en Delft Enterprises. Zo maak je deel uit van een inspirerende omgeving waarin wetenschap, innovatie en ondernemerschap samenkomen. Je krijgt volop ruimte om je expertise uit te bouwen. En je hoeft niet alles al te kunnen: je collega's begeleiden je bij je verdere ontwikkeling in dit vakgebied. Functie-eisen Je hebt een universitair diploma, bij voorkeur in computer science, electrical engineering of een andere technische / natuurwetenschappelijke richting. Je hebt ervaring met intellectueel eigendom, business development en/of technologische innovatie. Je hebt affiniteit met innovatieve technologie en wetenschappelijk onderzoek en wilt bijdragen aan de maatschappelijke toepassing van nieuwe uitvindingen. Je hebt kennis van commerciële (contract)onderhandelingen, bij voorkeur internationaal en gericht op licentieovereenkomsten voor octrooien of software. Je communiceert helder en overtuigend, legt gemakkelijk contacten en schakelt soepel tussen wetenschappers, ondernemers en andere betrokkenen. Je neemt initiatief, werkt zelfstandig en zoekt pro-actief samenwerking met collega's. Je deelt graag kennis en vergroot bij wetenschappers het bewustzijn over intellectueel eigendom. Je werkt gestructureerd, stelt prioriteiten en schakelt gemakkelijk tussen verschillende projecten. Je spreekt en schrijft goed Nederlands en Engels. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Directie Innovation & Impact Centre Je treedt in dienst bij het Innovation & Impact Centre (I&IC) dat verantwoordelijk is voor valorisatie - naast onderwijs en onderzoek de derde kerntaak van de universiteit. Wij zetten ons in om de kennis en technologie die we bij de TU Delft ontwikkelen ten goede te laten komen aan de maatschappij. Het werk bij I&IC is divers en varieert van advisering op het gebied van onderzoeksfinanciering tot het opzetten van grote publiek-private samenwerkingsverbanden. Ook houden we ons bezig met de ontwikkeling van de TU Delft Campus als innovatie-ecosysteem. We stimuleren ondernemerschap, (inter)nationale samenwerking en strategische planvorming op het gebied van innovatie. Afhankelijk van je profiel kom je werken op het gebied van onderzoeksfinanciering (zowel NL als EU), intellectueel eigendom, public affairs, corporate innovations, campusontwikkeling, projecten of innovation affairs. Het I&IC is gevestigd midden op de TU Delft Campus, het bruisende innovatie-ecosysteem dat naast de universiteit bijna 300 bedrijven, kennisinstellingen, fieldlabs, (pre-)incubators, restaurants en cafés huisvest. Een inspirerende plek waar je je dagelijks omringt met studenten, onderzoekers, ondernemers en andere innovatieve geesten; allemaal gedreven door dezelfde missie: impact for a better society. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 11 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €4925 - €6682 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie en sollicitatieprocedure? Neem dan contact op met Adriaan van Noord, Hoofd IP, via 015 - 278 69 02 of a.j.e.vannoord@tudelft.nl Let op: tijdens de looptijd van de vacature kunnen er al gesprekken worden gepland. Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 22 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Adriaan van Noord. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Innovation & Impact Centre Salaris range: €4925 - €6682 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 22 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3998 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Managementassistent-afdeling-Engineering-Systems-and-Services-2628-CD/1375224057/": {
      "title": "Managementassistent afdeling Engineering Systems and Services Functiedetails",
      "description": "Managementassistent afdeling Engineering Systems and Services Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Managementassistent afdeling Engineering Systems and Services Wij zoeken twee initiatiefrijke managementassistenten die energie krijgen van het soepel laten verlopen van processen binnen een internationale, wetenschappelijke afdeling. Functieomschrijving De afdeling Engineering Systems and Services (ESS) doet onderzoek naar complexe systemen op het gebied van energie, mobiliteit en digitalisering. Denk bijvoorbeeld aan het ontwerpen van toekomstbestendige energiesystemen voor de energietransitie, het ontwikkelen van slimme laadnetwerken voor elektrisch vervoer en het verantwoord inzetten van AI en digitale platforms in onze samenleving. De afdeling is opgedeeld in drie secties, die elk worden ondersteund door twee vaste managementassistenten. Twee collega’s zetten een mooie vervolgstap naar een andere functie binnen de TU Delft. Daardoor zoeken wij twee nieuwe collega's die met hun kennis, initiatief en organisatietalent ons team komen versterken. Je maakt deel uit van een professioneel en betrokken team van managementassistenten. Collega's weten elkaar gemakkelijk te vinden, delen kennis en springen waar nodig voor elkaar in. Je werkt in nauwe samenwerking met een collega voor een van de secties. Daarnaast ondersteun je waar nodig ook de andere secties, bijvoorbeeld tijdens drukke periodes of bij afwezigheid van een collega. Dankzij jouw inzet verlopen de dagelijkse werkprocessen soepel, zodat wetenschappers zich kunnen richten op onderwijs en onderzoek. Je vervult een afwisselende functie met veel contacten en uiteenlopende werkzaamheden. Je ondersteunt de sectie bij administratieve en organisatorische processen op het gebied van HR, financiën en secretariële dienstverlening. Daarnaast ben je een belangrijk aanspreekpunt voor medewerkers en draag je bij aan de organisatie van bijeenkomsten en evenementen. Je werkzaamheden bestaan onder andere uit: het dagelijks ondersteunen van de sectieleider, hoogleraren en universitair (hoofd)docenten; het verzorgen van administratieve processen rondom aanstellingen en personele mutaties; het onboarden van nieuwe (internationale) medewerkers en gasten; het plannen en organiseren van afspraken, vergaderingen, workshops, symposia en andere bijeenkomsten; het regelen van catering, reizen en andere praktische zaken; het beantwoorden van vragen van medewerkers en bezoekers en het fungeren als aanspreekpunt binnen de sectie. Je werkt graag samen en zoekt actief de afstemming met collega's. Tegelijkertijd pak je zelfstandig werkzaamheden op, stel je prioriteiten en maak je weloverwogen keuzes. In afstemming met de leidinggevende kun je na de inwerkperiode 1 dag per week thuis werken. Functie-eisen Herken jij jezelf in het onderstaande profiel? Dan nodigen we je van harte uit om te solliciteren. Je hebt een afgeronde administratieve of secretariële opleiding en een MBO+ werk- en denkniveau. Je hebt meerdere jaren ervaring in een vergelijkbare functie. Ervaring binnen de TU Delft of een andere universiteit is een pré. Je weet prioriteiten te herkennen, schakelt gemakkelijk tussen verschillende werkzaamheden en behoudt overzicht. Je hebt ervaring met Microsoft Office en voelt je snel thuis in administratieve systemen en databases. Je hebt oog voor mensen, culturele verschillen en organisatorische verhoudingen. Je bent servicegericht, collegiaal en communicatief vaardig. Je werkt proactief, nauwkeurig en verantwoordelijk en bent flexibel inzetbaar. Je beheerst de Nederlandse en Engelse taal goed, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Techniek, Bestuur & Management De Faculteit TBM levert een belangrijke bijdrage aan het oplossen van complexe, technisch-maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Dit betreft actuele vraagstukken zoals de energietransitie, mobiliteit, digitalisering, waterbeheer en (cyber)security. Dit doet TBM met haar uitstekende onderwijs en onderzoek op het raakvlak van techniek, maatschappij en bestuur. TBM combineert inzichten uit de technische wetenschappen, de sociale en de geesteswetenschappen. TBM is kennisgericht, internationaal georiënteerd en beschikt over een uitgebreid netwerk van kennisinstellingen, bedrijven, maatschappelijke organisaties en overheden. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Techniek, Bestuur en Management te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 07 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3202 - €4159 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Ilse Oonk, afdelingssecretaris ESS, i.oonk@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 2 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Ilse Oonk, afdelingssecretaris ESS. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Technology, Policy & Management Salaris range: €3202 - €4159 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0.8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 2 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3986 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-MetNH3Energy-2628-CD/1375188057/": {
      "title": "Postdoc MetNH3Energy",
      "description": "Postdoc MetNH3Energy Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc MetNH3Energy Work at the intersection of hydrogen, ammonia, and sustainability. Join the MetNH3Energy project and help identify low-carbon solutions that can power Europe's energy trans Job description The European Union (EU), through initiatives such as REPowerEU, REFuelEU, and FuelEU Maritime, is driving the transition toward lower greenhouse gas emissions. Green hydrogen is expected to play a key role, with part of the demand being met through imports. Ammonia is emerging as a promising hydrogen carrier due to its suitability for storage, transport, and applications such as ammonia cracking, shipping, and power generation. As part of the European MetNH3Energy project, you will assess the techno-economic and environmental performance of three ammonia value chains to support the identification of sustainable pathways for carbon footprint reduction. The role involves conducting process modeling, ex-ante techno-economic (TEA) and life cycle (LCA) assessments. Because several technologies under evaluation are not yet commercial, you will apply scenario-based “what-if” analyses to evaluate their future environmental and economic impacts. This work will contribute to developing sustainable ammonia and hydrogen solutions that support the EU's energy transition objectives. Job requirements We are looking for a researcher who: Has an academic backgrund at PhD level in e.g. chemical engineering or process system engineering. Wants to make an active contribution to the energy transition. Has knowledge and proven experience in process modelling (e.g ASPEN) and life cycle assessment. Enjoys working in an interdisciplinary group and is a team player. Very good communication and writing skills in the English language are required. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporary. A job of 32-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Recruitment-tnw@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 9 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter If the applicants are selected for an interview, they will be asked to provide contact details of two referees with their consent. You can address your application to Andrea Ramirez Ramirez. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 32-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 9 Nov 2026 ID job: 3970 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-in-Foil-Drone-2628-CD/1375189257/": {
      "title": "PhD Position in Foil Drone",
      "description": "PhD Position in Foil Drone Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position in Foil Drone Pioneering the future of maritime surveillance? Join as a PHD to research and advance autonomous, wind-powered drones, featuring tethered hydrofoils for indefinite ocean monitoring. Job description Are you ready to shape the future of autonomous maritime security? We are looking for a highly motivated and talented PhD Candidate to spearhead advanced research on the FoilDrone system—an innovative, future-proof maritime surveillance concept. Project Context & Mission Maritime domain awareness is a critical global priority. Traditional surveillance options face major trade-offs: airborne drones offer high speed but suffer from critically low endurance (6 to 22 hours), while unmanned surface vessels (like the Saildrone) boast long endurance but travel at very low speeds (3 to 5 knots) and cannot see over the horizon. The FoilDrone system bridges this market gap by combining an aerial Vertical Take-Off and Landing (VTOL) rotating-wing sailplane with a submerged, tethered hydrofoil. completely eliminating propulsion power consumption during operations. Key Responsibilities & Research Focus As a PhD candidate, you will take ownership of the next phase of FoilDrone research. You will take the design from conceptual idea towards physical implementation through independent research, simulation and experimentation. Your core duties will include: Advanced Multi-Body Dynamics & Control: Deepen and expand simulation models linking the aerial vehicle to the submerged hydrofoil via a flexible tether. Refine independent controllers to ensure stability during critical transitions (transit, deployment, sailing, and recovery). Aerodynamic & Hydrodynamic Optimization: Investigate the complex interactions of fixed wing drone, cabels, and hydrofoils. Optimize aerodynamic and hydrodynamic efficiencies across varying sea states and wind disturbances. Experimental Validation: Translate theoretical models into physical hardware. Collaborate with technical staff and student teams to design wind-tunnel experiments, tow-tank tests, and open-water flight trials to validate structural integrity, deployment mechanisms, and control strategies. Academic Contribution: Publish high-impact scientific papers in leading international journals, present findings at global aerospace and marine conferences, and assist in supervising Master's and Bachelor's student thesis projects. What We Offer A fully funded, multi-year PhD position within a world-leading aerospace research environment. Access to state-of-the-art simulation tools, testing facilities, and prototyping equipment. Opportunities to collaborate closely with pioneers in UAV technology, maritime sensors, and renewable energy systems. A vibrant, international, and inspiring workplace dedicated to creating innovative drone solutions that work in the real world. If you are eager to push the boundaries of aerial-marine robotics and make a tangible impact on global maritime safety, we invite you to submit your application Job requirements Educational Background: Hold a Master of Science degree in Aerospace Engineering, Robotics, Control Systems, or a closely related discipline. Technical Expertise: Strong background in flight dynamics, multi-body system modeling, guidance, navigation, and control (GNC). Simulation Skills: Demonstrated proficiency in numerical simulation environments (such as MATLAB/Simulink, Python) for aerial or underwater systems. Research Drive: Passion for academic research, experimental verification, and autonomous systems, with a proven ability to publish findings in peer-reviewed journals. Collaboration & Communication: Excellent English written and verbal communication skills, with a collaborative mindset to work alongside interdisciplinary academic and industrial partners. Practical Experience: Demonstrated hands-on experience in building, assembling, or maintaining (fixed-wing) unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) and/or marine hydrofoil systems, including composite manufacturing and mechanical integration. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Bart Remes, via B.D.W.Remes@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 2 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter Drone license (if applicable) You can address your application to Bart Remes. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Applying for an exemption for specific research and educational areas is an obligatory part of the selection procedure for this vacancy. This exemption must be obtained from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science (OCW) before an employment contract is agreed upon. Click here for more information. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 2 Nov 2026 ID job: 3978 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-RICH-ID-III-Reducing-Impact-of-CO2-Hydrates-on-Injectivity-Decline-2628-CD/1375215257/": {
      "title": "Postdoc RICH-ID-III: Reducing Impact of CO2 Hydrates on Injectivity Decline",
      "description": "Postdoc RICH-ID-III: Reducing Impact of CO2 Hydrates on Injectivity Decline Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc RICH-ID-III: Reducing Impact of CO2 Hydrates on Injectivity Decline Job description The main goal of the research is to quantify the impact of hydrate formation on injectivity of CO2 injection well and to develop chemical-based solutions to either inhibit the formation of hydrates (preventive methods) or to remediate the injectivity once formation of the hydrate led to injectivity decline (mitigation methods). The focus is at testing the identified potential mitigation and prevention solutions including injection of chemicals to dissociate already-formed CO2 hydrates. The experimental program will be conducted in close collaboration between TU Delft and JIP scientists to align the experiments and research objectives of JIP participants. Job requirements A PhD degree in e.g. geoscience, chemical, petroleum or mechanical engineering with a following skills: Strong lab work experience. Basic modeling skills. Data processing ability. Good command of English language. Team player. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences The Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences (CEG) is committed to outstanding international research and education in the field of civil engineering, applied earth sciences, traffic and transport, water technology, and delta technology. Our research feeds into our educational programmes and covers societal challenges such as climate change, energy transition, resource availability, urbanisation and clean water. Our research projects are conducted in close cooperation with a wide range of research institutions. CEG is convinced of the importance of open science and supports its scientists in integrating open science in their research practice. The Faculty of CEG comprises 28 research groups in the following seven departments: Materials Mechanics Management & Design, Engineering Structures, Geoscience and Engineering, Geoscience and Remote Sensing, Transport & Planning, Hydraulic Engineering and Water Management. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Civil Engineering & Geosciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 18 Months. Temporary. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, a discount for health insurance and sport memberships, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. An International Children’s Centre offers childcare and an international primary school. Dual Career Services offers support to accompanying partners. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Denis Voskov: d.v.voskov@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 11 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Denis Voskov. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Civil Engineering and Geosciences Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 11 Nov 2026 ID job: 3969 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Recruitment-medewerker-2628-CD/1375249257/": {
      "title": "Recruitment medewerker Functiedetails",
      "description": "Recruitment medewerker Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Recruitment medewerker Als sturende en adviserende spin in het web help je mee aan een soepel wervingsproces en een prettige candidate journey bij een internationale topuniversiteit. Functieomschrijving Je bent vaak het eerste aanspreekpunt bij de recruitmentafdeling en daarmee een belangrijke ambassadeur. Zo plaats je de vacatureteksten in ons Applicant Tracking System (ATS) die door onze HR-adviseurs of vacaturehouders worden aangeleverd. Deze teksten screen je op kwaliteit, je overlegt eventueel over aanvullingen of aanpassingen wat betreft de inhoud en zet deze teksten vervolgens online. Dat is een belangrijk en secuur proces, want dit zijn onze visitekaartjes. Daarnaast begeleid je vacaturehouders en afdelingsassistenten door het recruitmentproces zodat duidelijk is welke acties van hen verwacht worden en ben je tevens een belangrijke vraagbaak voor hen. Je voelt goed aan wie extra ondersteuning nodig heeft om een recruitmentproces succesvol te laten verlopen. Om het wervingsproces aan de achterkant optimaal te laten verlopen, werk je nauwgezet en prioriteer je doorlopend. Je herkent urgentie van vragen van collega’s en bepaalt wat je vandaag oppakt en wat tot morgen kan wachten. Je hebt een zelfstandige rol in een uniform proces zodat tegelijkertijd alle recruitment medewerkers elkaars werk kunnen opvangen als dat nodig is. Je houdt het overzicht over meerdere lopende processen en benadert collega’s proactief. Zie je bijvoorbeeld dat een vacaturehouder de sollicitaties nog niet beoordeeld heeft terwijl morgen de laatste mogelijkheid is, zie je dat het aantal sollicitanten achterblijft of denk je dat een aangeleverde vacaturetekst beter kan? Dan reageer je daar proactief op. Op de campus, tussen alle studenten, wetenschappers en stafmedewerkers zie je direct waarvoor je jouw werk doet. Samen met de andere recruitment medewerkers en Talent Acquisition Specialists vorm je een hecht team dat meehelpt aan de kwaliteit van het onderwijs en onderzoek van de oudste en grootste technische universiteit van Nederland. Jij en je collega’s ondersteunen elkaar en letten op elkaars welzijn. Onderling is er veel contact, tijdens zakelijke overleggen én gezellige (online) momenten. Veel processen staan vast, maar denk je dat het slimmer kan? Laat je vooral horen! Er is altijd ruimte om verder te professionaliseren en we staan open voor creatieve ideeën. Binnen de TU Delft zijn er voldoende doorgroeimogelijkheden, dus ook starters nodigen wij van harte uit te solliciteren. Functie-eisen Je hebt hbo-niveau. Je hebt interesse in recruitment(processen). Je spreekt en schrijft uitstekend Nederlands en Engels. Je hebt sterke digitale vaardigheden en kunt snel (leren) werken met onze systemen. Heb je al ervaring met werken in een ATS? Dan is dat uiteraard mooi meegenomen. Je werkt nauwkeurig, zodat wervingsprocessen van A tot Z goed verlopen. Je neemt initiatief en kunt anticiperen op risico’s. Als je vermoedt dat een proces vertraging oploopt, dan wacht je niet af maar onderneem je actie. Je kunt collega’s op enthousiaste wijze overtuigen van het optimale gebruik van ons ATS. Daarbij voel je goed aan hoe je een collega het beste benadert en aanspreekt. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Human Resources Om haar strategische doelstellingen te realiseren zet de TU Delft in op het aantrekken en ontwikkelen van ambitieuze en getalenteerde medewerkers. Het personeelsbeleid is gericht op recruitment en de ontwikkeling van talent, leiderschap en de organisatie, en draagt bij aan de versterking van onderwijs, onderzoek en valorisatie. Een veilige, uitdagende en betekenisvolle werkomgeving staat voorop. Hieraan draagt de HR-organisatie bij met de medewerkers van HR Advies die werken bij de faculteiten en de Universiteitsdienst (de ondersteunende diensten) op locatie, en daarnaast met de centrale HR-diensten van de afdelingen HR Talent & Development, Health Safety Environment (HSE), Compensation & Benefits en HR Services. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk. Een functieomvang van 36-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 07 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3202 - €4159 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze functie kun je contact opnemen met Edith Holierhoek via E.J.M.Holierhoek@tudelft.nl Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 9 november via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Edith Holierhoek. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Human Resources Salaris range: €3202 - €4159 Uren per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 9 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3987 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Technicus-voor-Hogedruk-en-Warmtetechniek-2628-CD/1374344857/": {
      "title": "Technicus voor Hogedruk- en Warmtetechniek Functiedetails",
      "description": "Technicus voor Hogedruk- en Warmtetechniek Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Technicus voor Hogedruk- en Warmtetechniek Bouw en verbeter experimentele installaties voor onderzoek naar hoge druk, warmte en innovatieve energiesystemen. Met jouw technische expertise draag je bij aan oplossingen voor de energie van morgen. Functieomschrijving Hoe gedragen warmte en vloeistoffen zich onder extreme omstandigheden? En hoe kunnen we energie efficiënter omzetten en benutten? Binnen de afdeling Process & Energy van de faculteit Mechanical Engineering van de TU Delft onderzoeken wetenschappers deze vraagstukken. Dit onderzoek draagt bij aan de ontwikkeling van geavanceerde energiesystemen en technologieën die relevant zijn voor de energietransitie, waaronder systemen voor toekomstige kerncentrales. Om dit onderzoek mogelijk te maken, zijn betrouwbare en veilige experimentele installaties onmisbaar. En daar speel jij als technicus een belangrijke rol in. Als Technicus vertaal je deze wetenschappelijke onderzoeksvragen naar praktische technische oplossingen. Samen met onderzoekers en collega-technici ontwerp, bouw en verbeter je experimentele opstellingen voor onderzoek naar warmteoverdracht, hogedrukprocessen en moderne krachtcycli. Denk bijvoorbeeld aan een helische stoomgenerator waarmee onderzoekers kookinstabiliteiten bestuderen, of een installatie voor onderzoek naar superkritische CO₂-cycli. Als technicus zorg je ervoor dat onderzoekers hun ideeën kunnen toetsen aan experimenten. Jouw verantwoordelijkheden Je ontwerpt, bouwt en verbetert experimentele onderzoeksinstallaties, soms met afmetingen van circa 3 × 1,5 × 2 meter, bijvoorbeeld met AutoCAD. Je beoordeelt de thermische en mechanische belastbaarheid, betrouwbaarheid en veiligheid van installaties en experimenten. Je ontwikkelt en programmeert besturings- en regelsystemen met bijvoorbeeld LabVIEW, Python of vergelijkbare software. Je zorgt voor een veilige werkwijze en verzorgt de bijbehorende veiligheidsdocumentatie en risicobeoordelingen. Je werkt samen met onderzoekers, collega-technici en externe partners om wetenschappelijke vraagstukken te vertalen naar praktische technische oplossingen. Je ondersteunt studenten bij technische studieprojecten en onderzoeksopdrachten, zowel individueel als in groepsverband. Zo help je wetenschappers hun onderzoek uit te voeren en draag je tegelijkertijd bij aan de ontwikkeling van toekomstige ingenieurs. Functie-eisen Je werkt veiligheidsbewust en hebt ervaring met veiligheidsdocumentatie en het beoordelen van technische risico’s, of bent bereid je hierin verder te ontwikkelen. Je werkt graag samen met onderzoekers, technici, externe partners en studenten en hebt affiniteit met het begeleiden van technische projecten. Verder voldoe je aan de volgende eisen: Je hebt een afgeronde mbo+ of hbo-opleiding in werktuigbouwkunde, procestechnologie, HVAC, technische natuurkunde of een vergelijkbare technische richting. Je hebt kennis van en ervaring met warmte- en hogedruksystemen, bij voorkeur met drukken tot circa 100 bar. Je hebt bij voorkeur relevante certificeringen, bijvoorbeeld op het gebied van de Pressure Equipment Directive (PED) of STEK/F-gassen, of bent bereid hiervoor een opleiding te volgen. Je kunt technische installaties ontwerpen en realiseren, bijvoorbeeld met AutoCAD, en hebt inzicht in de thermische en mechanische belastbaarheid van systemen, of bent bereid om je hierin te ontwikkelen. Je hebt ervaring met of interesse in het ontwikkelen van besturings- en regelsystemen met LabVIEW, Python of vergelijkbare software. Je beheerst het Nederlands en Engels goed, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Mechanical Engineering Van chip tot schip. Van machine tot mens. Van idee naar oplossing. Vanuit de wil om de omgeving te begrijpen en te achterhalen welke mechanismen daaraan ten grondslag liggen, richten onderzoek en onderwijs zich op fundamenteel begrip, ontwerp, productie, toepassing en verbetering van producten, materialen, processen en (mechanische) systemen. De faculteit ME is een dynamische en innovatieve faculteit met een internationale scope en high-tech lab-faciliteiten. Omdat we zo groot en veelzijdig zijn, kunnen we unieke dwarsverbanden leggen en vakgebieden combineren. Dit vindt zijn weerslag in uitstekend en modern onderwijs dat studenten opleidt tot maatschappelijk betrokken en verantwoordelijke ingenieurs en onderzoekers. De kennis en inzichten die we opdoen, vertalen we in oplossingen voor maatschappelijke vraagstukken, bijdragen aan een duurzame samenleving en aan de ontwikkeling van welvaart en welzijn. Dat is wat ons verbindt in grensverleggend onderzoek, inspirerend onderwijs en (inter)nationale samenwerking. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Mechanical Engineering te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 36-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 9 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3873 - €5264 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Voor deze vacature is een ontheffing kennisembargo nodig, zie ook: https://www.government.nl/themes/education/secondary-vocational-education-mbo-and-tertiary-higher-education/exemption-certain-engineering-or-nuclear-related-courses-of-study Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie en sollicitatieprocedure? Neem dan contact op met dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters ( j.w.r.peeters@tudelft.nl ). Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 15 November 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan dr. ir. Jurriaan Peeters. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Bij deze vacature is het aanvragen van een ontheffing kennisembargo een verplicht onderdeel van de selectieprocedure. Voordat er een arbeidsovereenkomst wordt overeengekomen moet deze ontheffing worden verkregen bij het ministerie van Onderwijs, Cultuur en Wetenschap (OCW). Lees hier alvast meer over op de website van OCW. Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salaris range: €3873 - €5264 Uren per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 15 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 3938 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Onderwijsco%C3%B6rdinator-faculteit-ME-2628-CD/1375954357/": {
      "title": "Onderwijscoördinator faculteit ME Functiedetails",
      "description": "Onderwijscoördinator faculteit ME Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Onderwijscoördinator faculteit ME Ben jij een organisatietalent met oog voor verbetering? Als onderwijscoördinator bij Mechanical Engineering maak jij het verschil en zorg je dat complexe onderwijsprocessen soepel verlopen. Functieomschrijving Elf opleidingen, tientallen vakgebieden en ruim 6.000 studenten: dit maakt de faculteit Mechanical Engineering (ME) tot de grootste faculteit van de TU Delft. Internationaal staan we bekend om ons toonaangevende onderzoek en ons hoogwaardige onderwijs Samen met vijf collega-onderwijscoördinatoren vorm je een hecht team binnen de afdeling Onderwijs- en Studentenzaken. Als onderwijscoördinator ligt je focus op de praktische inrichting van de toegekende onderwijsprogramma’s. Je bent verantwoordelijk voor de organisatie van de processen waaronder het BSA-proces en Bachelor Eind Project, je zorgt voor een duidelijke en correcte Studiegids, evenals voor de ontvangst van eerstejaarsstudenten en voor de informatievoorziening m.b.t.  bijvoorbeeld programma- en roosterwijzigingen. Daarnaast draag je bij aan de organisatie van de StudieKeuzeCheck bij de BSc Maritieme Techniek en de selectiedag van de BSc Klinische Technologie. Ook draag je bij aan het opzetten, invoeren en onderhouden van systemen voor het inrichten en implementeren van het onderwijs. Je analyseert knelpunten en denkt mee over mogelijke verbeteringen in de inrichting en uitvoering van het onderwijs. Al met al fungeer je als een spil van de opleidingen en neem je daardoor zoveel mogelijk werk uit handen van de opleidingsdirecteuren. Bij al deze werkzaamheden maken oog voor detail, structuur en nauwkeurigheid het verschil. Het werkveld van onderwijscoördinatie binnen onze faculteit is breed, dynamisch en volop in ontwikkeling. Dit vraagt flexibiliteit, omdat er periodes zijn met een hogere piekbelasting en periodes waarin het rustiger is. Er is veel afwisseling, ruimte voor eigen initiatief en kansen om jezelf verder te ontwikkelen. Zo draag je iedere dag zichtbaar bij aan onderwijs dat voor studenten én docenten uitstekend georganiseerd is en optimaal verloopt. Wil jij jouw organisatietalent inzetten in een inspirerende academische omgeving en direct bijdragen aan de kwaliteit van het onderwijs aan de TU Delft? Dan maken we graag kennis met je. Functie-eisen Hebt HBO+-niveau en bij voorkeur affiniteit met techniek Hebt ervaring met het organiseren van onderwijs en weet hoe een grote (academische) onderwijsorganisatie werkt óf je hebt sterke affiniteit met onderwijs en ervaring op het gebied van procesmanagement in een complexe omgeving Hebt bij voorkeur ervaring met digitale leeromgevingen en andere educatieve technologieën zoals Sqill, Osiris en Brightspace Spreekt en schrijft (aantoonbaar) goed Nederlands en Engels Bent een aanpakker en werkt oplossingsgericht Bent toegankelijk en voor collega’s en docenten duidelijk zichtbaar als aanspreekpunt Houdt de planning en risico’s scherp in de gaten, werkt nauwkeurig en je durft ook ‘nee’ te zeggen TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Mechanical Engineering Van chip tot schip. Van machine tot mens. Van idee naar oplossing. Vanuit de wil om de omgeving te begrijpen en te achterhalen welke mechanismen daaraan ten grondslag liggen, richten onderzoek en onderwijs zich op fundamenteel begrip, ontwerp, productie, toepassing en verbetering van producten, materialen, processen en (mechanische) systemen. De faculteit ME is een dynamische en innovatieve faculteit met een internationale scope en high-tech lab-faciliteiten. Omdat we zo groot en veelzijdig zijn, kunnen we unieke dwarsverbanden leggen en vakgebieden combineren. Dit vindt zijn weerslag in uitstekend en modern onderwijs dat studenten opleidt tot maatschappelijk betrokken en verantwoordelijke ingenieurs en onderzoekers. De kennis en inzichten die we opdoen, vertalen we in oplossingen voor maatschappelijke vraagstukken, bijdragen aan een duurzame samenleving en aan de ontwikkeling van welvaart en welzijn. Dat is wat ons verbindt in grensverleggend onderzoek, inspirerend onderwijs en (inter)nationale samenwerking. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Mechanical Engineering te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 10 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3706 - €5760 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie? Neem dan contact op met het secretariaat O&S via secretariaat-OS-ME@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 22 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Sabrina van de Velde. Je hoort in week 48 of je wordt uitgenodigd voor de eerste ronde. Gesprekken in een eerste ronde worden gevoerd op dinsdag 1 december. Gesprekken in een tweede ronde worden gevoerd op dinsdagmiddag 8 december en/of woensdagochtend 9 december. Let op: Om je persoonsgegevens te beschermen, nemen we alleen sollicitaties in behandeling die via de ‘solliciteer-knop’ bij ons binnenkomen. Deze kan je vinden onder de gepubliceerde vacatures op onze website. Sollicitaties en aanvullende informatie die per e-mail of op een andere manier worden verstuurd, kunnen we helaas niet in behandeling nemen of beantwoorden. Dit geldt ook voor open sollicitaties. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Mechanical Engineering Salaris range: €3706 - €5760 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 22 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4012 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Laboratory-Technician-IEPG-Group-2628-CD/1375948557/": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician IEPG Group",
      "description": "Laboratory Technician IEPG Group Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Laboratory Technician IEPG Group Join the IEPG group and help build the next generation power system research infrastructure by integrating real-world grid hardware with advanced real-time simulation and digital substation technology. Job description UTOPYS (Understanding Large, Complex Power Systems) is a ten-year programme to build a new theory of large, complex power systems, enabled by the a state-of-the-art real-time power system simulator. As Laboratory Technician, you will help build, operate, and maintain this large-scale real-time simulation environment and its laboratory in. The technician will contribute to the deployment and operation of a large-scale real-time simulation environment for future power systems, supporting researchers in developing, validating, and operating simulation models and associated laboratory infrastructure. Key Responsibilities: UTOPYS Research Infrastructure Support the installation, operation, maintenance, and expansion of the UTOPYS simulation platform and associated laboratory infrastructure. Power System Models and Simulation Support researchers in configuring, validating, and operating real-time power system simulations and experimental environments. Substation and Grid Technologies Contribute practical expertise on power system operation, substation equipment (relays, IEDs, merging units), protection schemes, and grid automation to support realistic modelling and experimental validation. Simulation Platform Integration Build and configure hardware-in-the-loop setups, connecting simulators to physical equipment through I/O interfaces, cables, communication networks, measurement systems, and other related software and hardware components. Technical Support for Research Teams Assist researchers, PhD candidates, students, and industrial partners in preparing and operating experimental setups and simulation studies. Laboratory Operations and Safety Ensure safe operation of laboratory facilities and compliance with laboratory procedures. You will become a member of the ESP Lab team, headed by Lab Manager Sandra Dordevic. The ESP Lab team is responsible for the operation, maintenance, and development of the department’s research infrastructure and experimental facilities supporting research and education activities. Your work will primarily focus on supporting the Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) section, headed by Professor Peter Palensky, with a particular emphasis on the UTOPYS programme. This position offers an excellent opportunity to work in a multidisciplinary environment together with researchers, students, utilities, manufacturers, and industrial partners, contributing to the development of future sustainable and resilient power systems. About the Department The Department of Electrical Sustainable Energy addresses the technical, scientific, and societal challenges of the energy transition through research in: DC Systems, Energy Conversion and Storage (DCE&S) Photovoltaic Materials and Devices (PVMD) Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) High Voltage Technologies (HVT) The department provides expertise across the entire electrical energy system chain, from generation and conversion to transmission, distribution, and end-use applications. The department operates the Electrical Sustainable Power (ESP) Lab, one of Europe's largest academic power systems laboratories. The ESP Lab hosts advanced facilities for high-voltage testing, DC grids research, power electronics, protection and control, digital substations, and real-time power system simulation, supporting research and education in future energy systems. The Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) section conducts research on the operation, control, digitalisation, and resilience of future power systems, with a strong focus on real-time simulation, digital twins, cyber-physical energy systems, protection and control, and grid automation. UTOPYS is one of its initiatives, providing a unique large-scale platform for power system simulation and experimentation. Job requirements MBO/HBO degree in Electrical Engineering, Energy Technology, Power Systems, or a related field. Practical experience with electrical power systems, substations, or transmission and distribution networks. Understanding of power system protection, control, and automation principles. Experience with power system simulation platforms, SCADA systems, RTDS, OPAL-RT, or similar technologies is an advantage. Familiarity with communication protocols and digital substation concepts (e.g. IEC 61850) is desirable. Hands-on, analytical, and solution-oriented, with strong troubleshooting skills. Comfortable working in a multidisciplinary research environment with researchers, students, and industrial partners. Good communication skills in English, both written and spoken. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 5 years. Temporary 2.2A. A job of 38-40 hours per week. A salary based on Scale 10 of the CAO for Dutch Universities with a salary between €3706 - €5760 gross per month based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Prof. Peter Palensky, via P.Palensky@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 16 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Prof. Peter Palensky. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 16 Nov 2026 ID job: 3988 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Studieadviseur-2628-CD/1375957657/": {
      "title": "Studieadviseur Functiedetails",
      "description": "Studieadviseur Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Studieadviseur Kom jij het team van studieadviseurs (tijdelijk) versterken bij de bruisende faculteit Bouwkunde? Functieomschrijving In een dynamische werkomgeving, waarin professionaliteit, betrokkenheid en initiatief hoog in het vaandel staan, ben je als studieadviseur verantwoordelijk voor het bevorderen van een goede studievoortgang van bachelor-, master- en schakelstudenten gedurende hun gehele studieloopbaan. Het betreft een tijdelijke functie vanwege interne doorgroei binnen het team, voor de periode van 1 december 2026 tot en met mei 2027 (5 à 6 maanden). Afhankelijk van de ontwikkelingen binnen de universiteit bestaat er een mogelijkheid dat het dienstverband langer kan duren. Als studieadviseur ben je adviseur, begeleider en coach. Je bent een toegankelijk en vertrouwd aanspreekpunt voor studenten en ondersteunt hen bij vragen over hun studieprogramma, studievoortgang en welzijn. Je voert individuele begeleidingsgesprekken, onderhoudt contact met studenten die risico lopen op studievertraging en houdt spreekuren waarin studenten terechtkunnen met vragen over alle aspecten van hun studie. Vanuit een coachende benadering help je studenten regie te nemen over hun studieproces, weloverwogen keuzes te maken en hun talenten verder te ontwikkelen. Daarbij heb je oog voor zowel hun academische ontwikkeling als hun persoonlijke omstandigheden. Wanneer studenten te maken krijgen met uitdagingen zoals ziekte, persoonlijke omstandigheden of een functiebeperking, bied je passende ondersteuning en denk je mee over mogelijkheden binnen de opleiding. Waar nodig verwijs je door naar gespecialiseerde ondersteuning, zoals een studentenarts, huisarts, studentenpsycholoog, studentendecaan, loopbaanadviseur of de examencommissie. Daarnaast werk je samen met docenten, opleidingsmanagement, de examencommissie en andere ondersteunende professionals binnen en buiten de universiteit. Vanuit deze samenwerking draag je bij aan een inclusieve, veilige en ondersteunende leeromgeving, waarin studenten zich gezien en gehoord voelen en worden gestimuleerd het beste uit zichzelf te halen. Het team Studieadvies maakt deel uit van de afdeling Onderwijs- en Studentenzaken. Deze afdeling faciliteert het onderwijs van de bacheloropleiding Bouwkunde, de masteropleidingen Bouwkunde en Geomatics en The Berlage post-master in Architecture and Urban Design. Met circa 25 medewerkers verzorgt de afdeling onderwijsadvies, onderwijscoördinatie, het International Office, studieadvisering en de ondersteuning van de examencommissie. De afdeling werkt nauw samen met collega's binnen de faculteit en met medewerkers van de directie Education & Student Affairs. Functie-eisen Academisch werk- en denkniveau, met ervaring in coaching en begeleiding van studenten in het hoger onderwijs; Uitstekende gespreks- en coachingsvaardigheden; Ervaring met begeleiding bij persoonlijke, studiegerelateerde en motivatievraagstukken; Sterk empathisch en analytisch vermogen; Proactief en creatief in het vinden van passende oplossingen; In staat om zelfstandig én in teamverband effectief te werken; Stressbestendig en daadkrachtig in drukke of onverwachte situaties; Uitstekende beheersing van het Nederlands en Engels, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Faculteit Bouwkunde De faculteit Bouwkunde heeft wereldwijd een leidende rol in onderwijs en onderzoek. De drijvende kracht achter het succes van de faculteit is het robuuste onderzoeksprofiel in combinatie met de energie en creativiteit van de studenten en de academische gemeenschap. Het is een bruisende plek waar ruim vierduizend mensen vol passie en energie studeren, werken, ontwerpen, onderzoek doen en kennis vergaren en verspreiden. Onze faculteit heeft een sterke focus op ‘ontwerpgericht onderzoek' dat al enkele jaren wordt erkend en bekroond, met als resultaat een toppositie op de wereldranglijsten. Medewerkers en studenten werken aan de verbetering van de gebouwde omgeving met behulp van een breed scala aan disciplines, waaronder architectonisch ontwerp, stedenbouw, bouwtechnologie, sociale wetenschappen, procesmanagement en geo-informatiewetenschappen. De faculteit werkt nauw samen met andere faculteiten, universiteiten, private partijen en de publieke sector en heeft een uitgebreid netwerk, zowel in Nederland als internationaal. Klik hier om naar de website van faculteit Bouwkunde te gaan. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is tijdelijk voor 5 of 6 maanden. Een functieomvang van 0.6 - 0.7 fte, 24-28 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 10 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3546 - €5538 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Wil je meer informatie over de functie? Neem dan contact op met Rowan Hulskamp of Sylvia van Opdorp-Stijlen via studieadviseurs-bk@tudelft.nl . Via dit emailadres kun je desgewenst ook een telefonisch kennismakingsgesprek inplannen. Voor meer informatie over de sollicitatieprocedure, kun je contact op met Sofie Hennekens, HR adviseur, via e-mail: recruitment-BK@tudelft.nl . Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 8 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: Curriculum vitae. Motivatiebrief. De eerste gesprekken vinden plaats op dinsdag 10 november. Eventuele tweede gesprekken worden gepland op 12 november in de middag. We vragen je om hier alvast rekening mee te houden in je agenda. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: Faculty of Architecture and the Built Environment Salaris range: €3546 - €5538 Uren per week: 24-28 FTE: 0.6-0.7 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 8 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4013 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-Energy-Data-Sharing-for-City-Level-Policy-Making-Using-Digital-Twins-2628-CD/1375920457/": {
      "title": "PhD Position Energy Data Sharing for City-Level Policy Making Using Digital Twins",
      "description": "PhD Position Energy Data Sharing for City-Level Policy Making Using Digital Twins Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position Energy Data Sharing for City-Level Policy Making Using Digital Twins Job description The Delft University of Technology is hiring a doctoral candidate on the subject of \"Energy data sharing for city-level policy making using digital twins\". The PhD position is a part of the FEDERATE NWO project. Municipal policy makers are making city decarbonization and sustainability policies using digital twins that rely on fragmented, partial and incomplete data. The data mostly comes from public sources, such as CBS (Central Bureau for Statistics) and through time consuming and costly data collection initiatives initiated by municipalities. However, this is insufficient to provide a high-resolution picture that the policy makers need. In 2026, a new Energy Law enacted in the Netherlands that provisions easier energy data sharing among different parties including municipalities and their citizens and local companies. Although it unlocks new possibilities of data sharing among these actors, this law is yet to become operationalized in the data sharing processes of municipalities. This PhD research project will investigate data sharing architectures for energy data sharing between citizens, local companies and municipalities, compatible with digital twins that municipalities use. The work involves designing of ontologies and knowledge graphs and their integration with digital twins of municipalities and other tools that could be used for data collection from citizens and companies. This is a four-year doctoral appointment. You will be supervised by Dr. Milos Cvetkovic. You will be a member of the section Intelligent Electrical Power Grids in the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics, and Computer Science. The project will offer opportunities to collaborate with industrial partners but also with academics from other disciplines. Within the team, we strive to develop methods that are mathematically rigorous and have near-term application potential. We are strong supporters of open science (publishing, source code, data). You will also be expected to assist in teaching activities (student supervision, labs) related to your subject area. About the department The research in the Department of Electrical Sustainable Energy is inspired by the technical, scientific, and societal challenges originating from the transition toward a more sustainable society and focuses on three areas: DC Systems, Energy Conversion and Storage (DCE&S) Photovoltaic Materials and Devices (PVMD) Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) High Voltage Technologies (HVT) The department provides expertise across the entire energy system chain and hosts extensive research facilities, including high-voltage testing laboratories, DC grids testing environments, and large-scale RTDS infrastructure for real-time simulation of future electrical power systems, AC/DC protection, and wide-area monitoring and protection. The Intelligent Electrical Power Grids (IEPG) group, headed by Prof. Peter Palensky, focuses on the future evolution of electrical power systems. The group develops advanced power technologies and intelligent control approaches to enable reliable, efficient, stable, affordable, and sustainable energy systems with increasing levels of distributed and renewable generation. Job requirements We are looking for a candidate that already has an MSc degree in Computer Science, Electricical Engineering, Mathematics, or a similar field. They have demonstrated working proficiency in programming. They have excellent analytical skills and solid basis in one or more of the following: knowledge graphs, knowledge representation, data engineering, model-driven software engineering, data space architectures, etc. Idealy, they have already demonstrated high inclination towards modeling of socio-technical systems and processes, and they have worked in large projects with many partners. The ideal candidate is open minded, curious and creative. The PhD will develop new science, write scientific papers and publish them in journals and conferences, work on deliverables of the FEDERATE project, attend project meetings and work alongside project partners, complete the graduate school requirements of TU Delft and write the PhD dissertation by the end of the project. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Delft University of Technology is built on strong foundations. As creators of the world-famous Dutch waterworks and pioneers in biotech, TU Delft is a top international university combining science, engineering and design. It delivers world class results in education, research and innovation to address challenges in the areas of energy, climate, mobility, health and digital society. For generations, our engineers have proven to be entrepreneurial problem-solvers, both in business and in a social context. At TU Delft we embrace diversity as one of our core values and we actively engage to be a university where you feel at home and can flourish. We value different perspectives and qualities. We believe this makes our work more innovative, the TU Delft community more vibrant and the world more just. Together, we imagine, invent and create solutions using technology to have a positive impact on a global scale. That is why we invite you to apply. Your application will receive fair consideration. Challenge. Change. Impact! Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. Milos Cvetkovic, via m.cvetkovic@tudelft.nl . For information about the selection procedure, please contact Carla Jager, Management Assistant, email: c.p.jager@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 20 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter that details your motivation and fit to the job requirements. Incomplete applications will not be considered A list of grades of your qualifying degrees (BSc, MSc) You can address your application to Dr. Milos Cvetkovic. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 20 Nov 2026 ID job: 3992 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Contractadministrateur-2628-CD/1376043357/": {
      "title": "Contractadministrateur Functiedetails",
      "description": "Contractadministrateur Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Contractadministrateur Wil jij bijdragen aan baanbrekend onderzoek en onderwijs door grip te houden op contracten en inkoopprocessen? Als Administratief Medewerker inhuur- en contractbeheer zorg jij voor overzicht. Functieomschrijving Bij TU Delft werk je aan de uitdagingen van morgen: van quantumtechnologie tot duurzame luchtvaart en van slimme gebouwen tot de energietransitie. In deze rol ondersteun je dat werk achter de schermen door contracten en inkoop- en inhuurprocessen administratief stevig te organiseren. Je werkt voor alle acht faculteiten en tien universiteitsdiensten en maakt deel uit van een team van acht contractmanagers en twee contractadministrateurs. Jij werkt binnen het accountteam faculteiten en inhuur. Vanaf je start word je goed ingewerkt in de organisatie, onze werkwijze en de CATS-CM-methodiek. Daarna ga je zelfstandig aan de slag met inhuur- en contractbeheer en werk je nauw samen met de inhuur- en (inkoop)contractmanagers Procurement. Ook heb je regelmatig contact met contracteigenaren en realisatie- en verificatiemanagers binnen de faculteiten. Je bent verantwoordelijk voor het administratief inhuur- en contractmanagementbeheer en ondersteunt het inkoopproces binnen Procurement. Je zorgt dat het contractmanagementsysteem juist, volledig en actueel is ingericht op basis van aangeleverde informatie. Je controleert invoer op eenduidigheid en volledigheid, voert contracten en projecten in en ondersteunt collega’s bij het correct vastleggen van gegevens. Daarnaast verzorg je maandelijkse rapportages over de status van projecten en contracten en stel je rapportages op over uitgaven en spend in relatie tot contracten, onder andere met Power BI en het ERP-systeem. Je bent het eerste aanspreekpunt voor het contractmanagementsysteem en werkt samen met DAFS aan het operationeel verbeteren en actueel houden ervan. Ook ondersteun je het inhuur-, inkoop- en contractmanagementproces administratief, bijvoorbeeld door het beheren van de centrale mailboxen van Procurement, het signaleren van knelpunten richting de afdelingshoofden en het beheren en actualiseren van standaardformulieren. Vanuit rapportages signaleer je waar het proces (niet) gevolgd wordt en werk je samen met de inhuur- of contractmanagers aan het beter naleven van de processen. Je levert een actieve bijdrage aan afdelingsbrede werkzaamheden en neemt deel aan overleg binnen Procurement en contractmanagement. TU Delft vindt een gezonde werk-privébalans belangrijk. Daarom bieden we flexibele werktijden en, bij een fulltime dienstverband en als het werk het toelaat, de mogelijkheid om 40% per week vanuit huis te werken. Functie-eisen Je hebt minimaal mbo werk- en denkniveau. Je hebt minimaal twee jaar relevante werkervaring in een administratieve functie, bij voorkeur met contractadministratie binnen een complexe organisatie. Je werkt gestructureerd en resultaatgericht, met oog voor naleving én optimalisatie van afspraken. Je communiceert helder met diverse stakeholders in het Nederlands en Engels. Je bent digitaal vaardig en werkt makkelijk met systemen en rapportagetools. Je bent leergierig en bereid je verder te ontwikkelen binnen het vakgebied inhuur- en contractmanagement. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Finance De ambitie van de TU Delft vraagt om investeringen in onderzoek, techniek, en onderwijs, en dat zegt direct alles over het belang van Finance. Wij adviseren het College van Bestuur, de faculteiten en diensten over financiële vraagstukken op het gebied van business control, procurement, treasury management, fiscaliteiten en verzekeringen. Daarnaast zijn wij verantwoordelijk voor de planning- en controlcyclus en de gehele financiële administratie. Dit alles is onmisbaar voor de TU Delft om hun ambities waar te maken. Je bent van harte uitgenodigd om hiervan deel uit te maken. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk. Een functieomvang van 32 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 08 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3537 - €4673 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature kun je contact opnemen met Gerben Ouwens-Nooijen ( g.ouwens-nooijen@tudelft.nl ) en indien afwezig via Odile Uijlenbroek ( O.E.C.Uijlenbroek@tudelft.nl ). Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 15 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Odile Uijlenbroek. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. TU Delft voert in het kader van kennisveiligheid een risicobeoordeling uit bij het werven van personeel. Dit doen wij onder meer om ongewenste overdracht van gevoelige kennis en technologie te voorkomen. De beoordeling gebeurt op basis van informatie die door kandidaat zelf is aangeleverd, zoals de motivatiebrief en het cv. De beoordeling vindt plaats bij de laatst overgebleven kandidaten in het selectieproces. Wanneer de uitkomst van de risicobeoordeling negatief is, dan wordt de kandidaat daarover geïnformeerd. De verwerking van persoonsgegevens in het kader van deze risicobeoordeling vindt plaats op basis van de wettelijke grondslag van de AVG ‘uitvoering van de publieke taak van algemeen belang’. Meer informatie over deze beoordeling vind je op onze website over kennisveiligheid . Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Finance Salaris range: €3537 - €4673 Uren per week: 32 FTE: 0,8 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 15 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4005 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-IDEE-project-on-&apos;The-Transition-from-Secondary-Education-to-Higher-Education&apos;-2628-CD/1376078257/": {
      "title": "Postdoc IDEE project on 'The Transition from Secondary Education to Higher Education'",
      "description": "Postdoc IDEE project on 'The Transition from Secondary Education to Higher Education' Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc IDEE project on 'The Transition from Secondary Education to Higher Education' Come and innovate TU Delft education with your postdoctoral research Job description At the TU Delft, we are proud to welcome thousands of students every year within our engineering education. While the students’ transition from high school to our university is an exciting milestone, it also presents significant academic, social, and personal challenges. Our team is interested in how our university supports students during this critical period best, and what successful transitioning actually embodies? In this postdoctoral project, you will investigate student success from an integrated perspective, considering study progress, well-being, and competency development as interconnected actors. Through design-based research, you will develop, implement, and evaluate innovative approaches that help students thrive during their transition to higher education. The TU Delft Teaching Academy has recognized student transition as a key theme within the Initiative on Innovation in Delft Engineering Education (IDEE). IDEE is a cross-faculty program for innovations and research in engineering education at TU Delft. This project seeks to identify factors that contribute to a successful transition and explore evidence-based practices that support it. As a postdoctoral researcher, you will focus on one or more of the following: Conceptualize what a ‘successful transition’ to higher education entails. Identify key factors influencing student success. Analyze and evaluate evidence-based practices that support student transition. Design and evaluate new practices that support student transition. You will work as part of the IDEE team on transition, which consists of 20 members from all faculties, as well as educational services at the TU Delft. The supervision team will consist of three staff members. You will be working in a dynamic team with scientific and educational staff, another postdoc and a PhD candidate for this project, supported by the TU Delft Teaching Academy. The Teaching Academy is the network for and by lecturers of TU Delft with the mission to collaboratively enhance engineering education and drive education innovations across faculty boundaries. While the chosen candidate will work in the IDEE team on transition, they will be appointed to the section Science and Engineering Education (SEEd), which is part of the department Imaging Physics at the Faculty of Applied Sciences, in the same section as one of the supervisors Dr. Anna Hotze. This will create the opportunity to discuss your research with SEEd colleagues and exchange ideas on science and engineering education. The Science & Engineering Education (SEEd) section is an academic group that conducts education, research and outreach in the field of STEM education. The section SEEd investigates science and engineering education across primary, secondary and tertiary levels with a focus on pedagogical approaches of monodisciplinary science subjects and more interdisciplinary forms of teaching and learning. Job requirements We are looking for an organized and motivated candidate with: A PhD degree, in one of the social sciences such as Educational Studies or Cognitive Psychology, with a strong interest in engineering and engineering education. Experience with educational design based research is a plus. Skills to organize the research work in consultation with a multidisciplinary team; ability to work through ambiguities, inconsistencies, and uncertainties that come when interacting with multiple stakeholders with different interests and values. Acquaintance with the secondary and higher educational system, with interest in the Dutch system, is a plus. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporarily with a posibility for extension. A job of 36-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Dr. Anna Hotze, Dr. Yukihiro Murakami or Dr. Hylkje Geertsema, via a.hotze@tudelft.nl , y.murakami@tudelft.nl or h.j.geertsema@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 29 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter of at most 600 words. If the applicants are selected for an interview, they will be asked to provide contact details of two referees with their consent. You can address your application to Dr. Anna Hotze, Dr. Yukihiro Murakami and Dr. Hylkje Geertsema. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 29 Nov 2026 ID job: 4002 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Quantum-Error-Correction-and-Compilation-2628-CD/1376175257/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Quantum Error Correction and Compilation",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Quantum Error Correction and Compilation Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoctoral Researcher in Quantum Error Correction and Compilation Join us and shape the quantum devices of tomorrow! Job description Join the Feld Group at QuTech, where we are seeking a motivated Postdoctoral Researcher to advance research at the intersection of quantum technologies, GPU acceleration, and high-performance computing. Our team is working on enabling the next generation of tightly integrated quantum-classical computing systems, connecting advances in hardware with scalable software solutions for fault-tolerant quantum computing. Our current research spans several exciting directions, and you will have the opportunity to contribute to all of them. Low-Latency Quantum-Classical Integration: You will work with industrial partners such as Qblox to develop and benchmark low-latency GPU integration with quantum-control hardware. Quantum Error Correction and Decoding: You will design and optimize GPU-accelerated decoding algorithms for quantum error correction, supporting the development of scalable fault-tolerant quantum computers. GPU-Enabled Quantum Software: You will contribute to hardware-aware quantum software and high-performance computing solutions for next-generation quantum-classical systems. Quantum Compilation and Hardware-Aware Optimization: You will develop and evaluate compilation methods for emerging quantum architectures, with a focus on mapping, routing, and hardware-aware optimization for scalable and fault-tolerant quantum systems. Reliable and Fault-Tolerant Quantum Computing: You will investigate methods for improving the reliability and scalability of quantum computations, spanning fault-tolerant execution, hardware-software co-design, and advanced techniques for quantum error correction, including ASIC-based decoding. Although this position has a strong focus on systems and software, it will be closely intertwined with collaborations across QuTech, TU Delft, and industrial partners. This collaborative approach ensures that your work has a direct impact on the development of next-generation quantum computing technologies. Finally, you will join a welcoming, inclusive, and supportive team where diverse perspectives are valued. Requirements You hold a PhD in computer science, physics, electrical engineering, applied mathematics, or a related field at the start of the position. You have experience with GPU programming and high-performance computing, gained through research or industry projects. This may include areas such as CUDA, parallel computing, performance optimization, or systems software engineering. Experience with quantum computing is considered a plus, but extensive expertise in quantum error correction is not required. You are motivated to tackle challenging research problems, enjoy working in multidisciplinary teams. You combine strong communication and collaboration skills with a proactive and curious mindset. You are eager to contribute to the development of practical technologies for large-scale quantum computing and to collaborate with both academic and industrial partners. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. QuTech At QuTech, we work on radically new technologies with world-changing potential. Our mission: to develop scalable prototypes of a quantum computer and a quantum internet by integrating world-class research and groundbreaking innovation. Through excellence, relevance, and leadership, we cultivate a vibrant quantum technology ecosystem. Together, we are creating the quantum future, because we believe that quantum technologies can be a game changer in many societal and economic sectors, including health, agriculture and safety. Have a look at our video and get a glimpse of QuTech. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 24 months. Temporarily with a posibility for extension. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this position, please contact Sebastian Feld at QuTech at S.feld@tudelft.nl . For questions about the procedure, please contact our talent acquisition specialist Audrey Monje at A.Monje@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 30 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter You can address your application to Sebastian Feld. Please note: To protect your personal data, we only accept applications submitted via the ‘Apply’ button advertised under the vacancies on our website. Applications and additional information sent by email or through other channels, including unsolicited applications, will not be considered or responded to. This also applies to open applications. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: QuTech Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 30 Nov 2026 ID job: 4021 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Observations-of-Aircraft-Contrails-to-Evaluate-and-Improve-Model-Predictions-2628-CD/1376148657/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Observations of Aircraft Contrails to Evaluate and Improve Model Predictions",
      "description": "Postdoc Observations of Aircraft Contrails to Evaluate and Improve Model Predictions Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Observations of Aircraft Contrails to Evaluate and Improve Model Predictions Combine observations of contrails from different instruments to create the datasets that we can use to improve our models and reduce aviation's climate impact. Job description Contrails are a major contributor to aviation's climate impact: their impact can be mitigated by means of contrail avoidance - deviating aircraft around the regions of the atmosphere where contrails can persist for multiple hours. One of the current limitations to contrail avoidance is uncertainty in the models that we use to predict where contrails are going to persist and how much impact they will have. As a postdoctoral researcher, you will contribute to evaluating and improving contrail prediction models by creating high-quality datasets of contrail observations. Specifically, you will combine observations from different instruments - such as ground-based imagery, LIDAR measurements, and satellite imagery - to construct datasets that modelers can use to evaluate and improve their predictions. You will be based in the Operations and Environment section of TU Delft's faculty of Aerospace Engineering, and work closely with Dr. Vincent Meijer, PhD candidates and MSc students. Job requirements A PhD in atmospheric science, remote sensing, aerospace engineering, physics, or a closely related field. Strong programming and data-analysis skills, preferably in Python. Experience with atmospheric observations, remote sensing, and/or numerical modelling. Ability to work with large datasets from multiple sources. Understanding of uncertainty analysis and model evlauation. Ability to conduct independent research and publish scientific results. Good collobration and communication skills in English. Experience with contrails, cloud physics, or machine learning is an advantage. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Aerospace Engineering The Faculty of Aerospace Engineering at Delft University of Technology is a leading international community where innovation in aerospace meets global challenges. Our support and scientific staff, including PhD candidates, postdocs, and students, largely work together on three main themes: the energy transition, sustainable aerospace, and safety and security, with the aim of tackling climate change and contributing to the independence and security of Europe. When you join us, you become part of a diverse, collaborative, and forward-thinking environment where your ideas and perspectives are valued. Our work extends beyond the lab—into field labs, innovation hubs, and partnerships with other faculties, research institutes, governments, and industry, both locally and globally. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace, assisted by an active Diversity & Inclusion team . This includes tangible support such as funding for extra personnel for family and caregiving responsibilities, mentoring programmes, and initiatives that promote cultural exchange and integration. You don’t just join our faculty — you join a community where you can thrive, grow, and help shape the future of aerospace. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Aerospace Engineering. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1 year. Temporary external finance. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information For more information about this position, please contact Dr. Vincent Meijer at V.R.Meijer@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 1 December 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV. Motivational letter. Relevant research exprerience. You can address your application to Vincent Meijer. Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Aerospace Engineering Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 1 Dec 2026 ID job: 3981 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Ultrafast-Spectroscopy-on-2D-Materials-for-Quantum-Photonics-2628-CD/1376205957/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Ultrafast Spectroscopy on 2D Materials for Quantum Photonics",
      "description": "Postdoc Ultrafast Spectroscopy on 2D Materials for Quantum Photonics Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Ultrafast Spectroscopy on 2D Materials for Quantum Photonics Pump-probe optical and terahertz spectroscopy on dynamics of excitons and charge carriers in 2D materials for single-photon emitters. Job description The ultimate aim of the project is to develop defect-based single-photon emitters in 2D transition metal dichalcogenides (TMDCs) for quantum photonic applications. The project is a collaboration with two PhD students at the University of Amsterdam (UvA) where samples and photonic devices will be prepared. You will perform fundamental studies on the formation, motion and decay dynamics of photogenerated charge carriers and excitons. For single-photon emitters these species need to travel to intentionally created defects sites in the materials, such as atomic vacancies and local strain. You use ultrafast pump-probe laser spectroscopy with optical (TA, PL) and terahertz conductivity detection to monitor the charge and exciton dynamics and the formation of excitons at the defects where they should decay by single-photon emission. Depending on your experience and interests involvement in computational modelling (DFT/GW/BSE) of charge carriers and excitons is an option. This fundamental project will be in collaboration with two industrial partners, Toyota Motor Europe and Quix, the latter being a leading photonic quantum computing startup providing photonic integrated circuits (PICs). Job requirements You have a relevant university degree in physics, materials science or chemistry and experience with ultrafast pump-probe laser spectroscopy. PhD degree, experience with ultrafast laser spectroscopy. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Working at TU Delft means contributing to solutions that really make a difference. For over 180 years, we have been training engineers who make an impact worldwide in companies, government bodies, or as entrepreneurs. Our alumni turn knowledge into concrete solutions for the challenges of today and tomorrow. These challenges are changing rapidly. That is why we focus on themes such as energy, climate, digitalisation, artificial intelligence (AI), and smart mobility every day. Our education and research are directly aligned with what society needs now and in the future. At TU Delft, our people make the difference. With their knowledge and curiosity, our staff provide a high-quality education and conduct pioneering research that extends beyond the campus. You will have the opportunity to take the initiative, work with others, and grow as a professional. Working at TU Delft means join an international community of professionals and students. Together, we create knowledge, innovations, and solutions that help move the world forward. Faculty Applied Sciences With more than 1,100 employees, including 150 pioneering principal investigators, as well as a population of about 3,600 passionate students, the Faculty of Applied Sciences is an inspiring scientific ecosystem. Focusing on key enabling technologies, such as quantum- and nanotechnology, photonics, biotechnology, synthetic biology and materials for energy storage and conversion, our faculty aims to provide solutions to important problems of the 21st century. To that end, we educate innovative students in broad Bachelor's and specialist Master's programmes with a strong research component. Our scientists conduct ground-breaking fundamental and applied research in the fields of Life and Health Science & Technology, Nanoscience, Chemical Engineering, Radiation Science & Technology, and Engineering Physics. We are also training the next generation of high school teachers. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Applied Sciences. Conditions of employment Duration of contract is 1,5 years. Temporary external finance. A job of 38-40 hours per week. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities. An excellent pension scheme via the ABP. The possibility to compile an individual employment package every year. Discount with health insurers on supplemental packages. Flexible working week. Every year, 232 leave hours (at 38 hours). You can also sell or buy additional leave hours via the individual choice budget. Plenty of opportunities for education, training and courses. Partially paid parental leave Attention for working healthy and energetically with the vitality program. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands.  . Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Prof. Dr. Laurens D.A. Siebbeles, via l.d.a.siebbeles@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 15 November 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter If the applicants are selected for an interview, they will be asked to provide contact details of two referees with their consent. You can address your application to Prof. Dr. Laurens D.A. Siebbeles. Please note: To protect your personal data, we only accept applications submitted via the ‘Apply’ button advertised under the vacancies on our website. Applications and additional information sent by email or through other channels, including unsolicited applications, will not be considered or responded to. This also applies to open applications. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: €3706 - €5760 Hours per week: 38-40 FTE: 1,0 Submission is possible until: 15 Nov 2026 ID job: 4006 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-PhD-Position-in-AI-for-Software-Reuse-and-Agentic-Development-2628-CD/1376215257/": {
      "title": "PhD Position in AI for Software Reuse and Agentic Development",
      "description": "PhD Position in AI for Software Reuse and Agentic Development Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » PhD Position in AI for Software Reuse and Agentic Development How can AI agents build on existing software instead of reinventing it? Join this collaboration between TU Delft and ING to research more reliable agentic software development. Job description Software intensive organizations rely on increasingly large and complex software ecosystems consisting of services, libraries, APIs, frameworks, documentation, and other shared engineering knowledge. Recent advances in generative AI and software engineering agents are changing how software is developed and how developers interact with these ecosystems. TU Delft is collaborating with ING to investigate how we can make enterprise software development more sustainable and reliable in this changing landscape. We will develop new techniques and tools that help developers and AI agents make better use of existing software and developer knowledge. Our research will combine AI with software repository mining, program and architecture analysis, empirical software engineering, and studies with practitioners. The research will focus on real-world software engineering challenges at ING, while contributing scientific insights and open research results that can benefit the broader software engineering community. Within this collaboration, we explore two main research directions: Direction 1: Software Reuse in Enterprise Software Ecosystems Large organizations invest substantially in reusable software assets. However, as a consequence similar functionality can be implemented independently across teams, increasing fragmentation and long-term maintenance costs. AI-assisted software development makes this challenge even more important: software engineering agents can rapidly generate new code, but may reproduce functionality that already exists elsewhere in an organization. This direction investigates how software assets are discovered, consumed, adapted, and evolved across large software ecosystems. We will study where opportunities for reuse exist, how software can successfully be adapted across teams, how reusable assets evolve over time, and how developers and AI agents can be guided towards suitable existing software. Ultimately, we aim to develop intelligent techniques that help organizations maximize reuse while reducing unnecessary duplication and maintenance effort. Direction 2: Reliable Agentic Software Development AI software engineering agents can increasingly perform tasks such as implementing features, fixing bugs, testing, and refactoring software. Their success, however, depends not only on the underlying AI models, but also on the engineering context available to them. In enterprise environments, relevant knowledge is distributed across source code, documentation, architecture descriptions, requirements, APIs, development history, and organizational practices. This direction investigates the engineering foundations required for reliable agentic software development. We will study what context agents need for different software engineering tasks, what makes specifications sufficiently complete and precise, how stale or incomplete context and software complexity affect agent performance, and how organizations can determine when tasks can be reliably delegated to AI agents. The goal is to develop techniques and safeguards that enable organizations to integrate increasingly autonomous software engineering agents while maintaining software quality and human oversight. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive research environment and encourage applications from all qualified candidates, regardless of their background or experience. We believe that diversity contributes to a more innovative and creative research community. If you do not meet some of the optional requirements listed, we encourage you to still apply and explain how your unique experience and skills can contribute to our research. Job requirements Required Master's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field Proficiency in the English language Additional requirements: Research focus, characterized by curiosity, data fluency, and critical thinking Engineering mindset, including ability to create experimental prototypes and demonstrators Team player, good listener, and ready to help To thrive as a PhD candidate, it’s crucial to have a strong research mindset driven by curiosity and passion for your topic. Reflecting on your motivation for pursuing a PhD trajectory is essential, as this path involves unique challenges and uncertainties inherent to scientific exploration. Success requires dedication, adaptability, the ability to analyze complex problems, manage your time effectively, innovate and stay resilient under pressure. Combined with the ability and willingness to work independently and collaborate well, these qualities are indispensable for a fulfilling PhD journey. These experiences will build you as an independent researcher, expand your professional network, and pave the way for diverse career pave the way for diverse career paths, inside or outside academia. TU Delft (Delft University of Technology) Delft University of Technology is built on strong foundations. As creators of the world-famous Dutch waterworks and pioneers in biotech, TU Delft is a top international university combining science, engineering and design. It delivers world class results in education, research and innovation to address challenges in the areas of energy, climate, mobility, health and digital society. For generations, our engineers have proven to be entrepreneurial problem-solvers, both in business and in a social context. At TU Delft we embrace diversity as one of our core values and we actively engage to be a university where you feel at home and can flourish. We value different perspectives and qualities. We believe this makes our work more innovative, the TU Delft community more vibrant and the world more just. Together, we imagine, invent and create solutions using technology to have a positive impact on a global scale. That is why we invite you to apply. Your application will receive fair consideration. Challenge. Change. Impact! Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science The Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science (EEMCS) brings together three scientific disciplines. Combined, they reinforce each other and are the driving force behind the technology we all use in our daily lives. Technology such as the electricity grid, which our faculty is helping to make completely sustainable and future-proof. At the same time, we are developing the chips and sensors of the future, whilst also setting the foundations for the software technologies to run on this new generation of equipment – which of course includes AI. Meanwhile we are pushing the limits of applied mathematics, for example mapping out disease processes using single cell data, and using mathematics to simulate gigantic ash plumes after a volcanic eruption. In other words: there is plenty of room at the faculty for ground-breaking research. We educate innovative engineers and have excellent labs and facilities that underline our strong international position. In total, more than 1000 employees and 4,000 students work and study in this innovative environment. Click here to go to the website of the Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics and Computer Science. Conditions of employment Doctoral candidates will be offered a 4-year period of employment in principle, but in the form of 2 employment contracts. An initial 1,5 year contract with an official go/no go progress assessment within 15 months. Followed by an additional contract for the remaining 2,5 years assuming everything goes well and performance requirements are met. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities, increasing from €3204 - €4051 gross per month, from the first year to the fourth year based on a fulltime contract (38 hours), plus 8% holiday allowance and an end-of-year bonus of 8.3%. As a PhD candidate you will be enrolled in the TU Delft Graduate School. The TU Delft Graduate School provides an inspiring research environment with an excellent team of supervisors, academic staff and a mentor. The Doctoral Education Programme is aimed at developing your transferable, discipline-related and research skills. The TU Delft offers a customisable compensation package, discounts on health insurance, and a monthly work costs contribution. Flexible work schedules can be arranged. Will you need to relocate to the Netherlands for this job? TU Delft is committed to make your move as smooth as possible! The HR unit, Coming to Delft Service , offers information on their website to help you prepare your relocation. In addition, Coming to Delft Service organises events to help you settle in the Netherlands, and expand your (social) network in Delft. A Dual Career Programme is available, to support your accompanying partner with their job search in the Netherlands. Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Andy Zaidman, via A.E.Zaidman@tudelft.nl . Application procedure Are you interested in this vacancy? Please apply no later than 1 December 2026 via the application button and upload the following documents: CV Motivational letter. In your motivation letter, please include your preference for one of the two research directions you are most interested in. If you have previously written academic works (theses, papers, …), please include them or link to them in your application package. You can address your application to Andy Zaidman. The PhD position will be fully at TU Delft, with strong collaboration with ING. Please include a brief statement in your application indicating whether and, if so, how you used AI tools to prepare your application documents. Doing a PhD at TU Delft requires English proficiency at a certain level to ensure that the candidate is able to communicate and interact well, participate in English-taught Doctoral Education courses, and write scientific articles and a final thesis. For more details please check the Graduate Schools Admission Requirements . Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about this assessment on our website about knowledge security. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Electrical Engineering, Mathematics & Computer Science Salary range: €3204 - €4051 Hours per week: 36-40 FTE: 1 Submission is possible until: 1 Dec 2026 ID job: 3997 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Facilitair-medewerker-2628-CD/1376237457/": {
      "title": "Facilitair medewerker Functiedetails",
      "description": "Facilitair medewerker Functiedetails | TU Delft Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Alle vacatures Werken bij TU Delft Taal English Nederlands Profiel weergeven Zoek op trefwoord Meer opties weergeven Laden... Faculteit/Dienst Alle Type vacature Alle Opleidingsniveau Alle Fulltime/parttime Alle Werkterrein Alle Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Job alert aanmaken × Selecteer hoe vaak (in dagen) je een job alert wil ontvangen: Solliciteer nu » Facilitair medewerker Hoe bijzonder is het dat we bij de TU Delft baanbrekend onderzoek doen en nieuwe technologieën ontwikkelen? Dat kan alleen als alles op facilitair gebied tot in de puntjes is geregeld. En daar speel je een onmisbare rol in. Functieomschrijving Als Facilitair Medewerker zorg je dat medewerkers en studenten op onze campus optimaal kunnen werken, studeren en samenwerken. Je bent zichtbaar aanwezig in het gebouw en zorgt dat alles soepel verloopt, van goed werkende apparatuur in collegezalen tot nette, toegankelijke en veilige ruimtes. Geen dag is hetzelfde. Je ondersteunt docenten bij colleges door audiovisuele middelen gebruiksklaar te maken en storingen snel op te lossen. Je helpt studenten door te zorgen voor prettige studieplekken en een goed functionerende leeromgeving. Daarnaast pak je zelfstandig facilitaire aanvragen op, bijvoorbeeld op het gebied van logistiek, verhuizingen, huisvesting, schoonmaak, evenementen of toegangsbeheer. Je bent de verbindende schakel tussen gebruikers, collega’s en leveranciers. Je signaleert onregelmatigheden in en rond het gebouw en komt met verbetervoorstellen. Naast je werkzaamheden op de werkvloer verricht je ook lichte administratieve taken achter de computer, bijvoorbeeld in systemen voor meldingen en registratie. Je werkt in een team en samen met je collega’s zorg je voor een goede dienstverlening in de onderwijsgebouwen zoals Pulse, Echo of Library. Functie-eisen In deze rol ben je een georganiseerde en servicegerichte professional die ziet wat nodig is. Je combineert gastvrijheid met heldere communicatie, werkt proactief en oplossingsgericht. Je pakt zelfstandig taken op, maar zoekt ook actief de samenwerking met collega’s. Met oog voor detail signaleer je knelpunten en kom je met verbeterideeën. Je bent bereid deel te nemen aan de BHV-organisatie. Daarnaast voldoe je aan het volgende: Je hebt minimaal mbo werk- en denkniveau. Je hebt bij voorkeur ervaring in het facilitaire werkveld. Je spreekt en schrijft goed Nederlands en hebt kennis van het Engels. Je hebt bij voorkeur ervaring met software zoals SharePoint en TOPdesk. TU Delft Werken bij TU Delft betekent bijdragen aan oplossingen die er echt toe doen. Al meer dan 180 jaar leiden we ingenieurs op die wereldwijd impact maken bij bedrijven, overheden of als ondernemer. Onze alumni zetten kennis om in concrete oplossingen voor de uitdagingen van vandaag en morgen. Die uitdagingen veranderen snel. Daarom werken we elke dag aan thema’s zoals energie, klimaat, digitalisering, AI en slimme mobiliteit. Ons onderwijs en onderzoek sluiten direct aan op wat de samenleving nodig heeft, nu en straks. Bij TU Delft maken mensen het verschil. Met hun kennis en nieuwsgierigheid zorgen zij voor sterk onderwijs, vernieuwend onderzoek en innovaties die verder komen dan de campus. Je krijgt de ruimte om initiatief te nemen, samen te werken en jezelf te ontwikkelen. Wie bij TU Delft werkt, sluit zich aan bij een internationale community van professionals en studenten. Samen bouwen we aan kennis, innovatie en oplossingen die de wereld vooruithelpen. Universiteitsdienst – Directie Campus Real Estate & Facility Management Om de ambities van de TU Delft te realiseren is een omgeving nodig die uitdaagt en inspireert. Campus Real Estate & Facility Management werkt met meer dan 250 collega’s dagelijks aan onze ontwikkeling, het beheren van de gebouwen en terreinen en het faciliteren van de meer dan 30.000 gebruikers van de TU Delft. Duurzaamheid staat daarbij hoog in het vaandel. Onze ambitie: een CO2-neutrale en circulaire campus in 2030. Wij creëren een omgeving waarin studenten, wetenschappers, medewerkers en samenwerkingspartners maximaal kunnen bijdragen aan een betere samenleving. Als medewerker van Campus Real Estate & Facility Management werk je dus in een bijzondere omgeving, waar je samen met collega’s, met heldere processen en in een open sfeer, bijdraagt aan de topprestaties van de TU Delft. Arbeidsvoorwaarden Het dienstverband is 1 jaar. Tijdelijk met uitzicht op vast. Een functieomvang van 32-40 uur per week. Een salaris dat is gebaseerd op Schaal 06 uit de CAO Nederlandse Universiteiten met salaris tussen €3173 - €3785 bruto per maand op basis van een volledige werkweek (38 uur), plus 8% vakantiegeld en een eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3%. Een uitstekende pensioenregeling via het ABP. De mogelijkheid om jaarlijks een individueel arbeidsvoorwaardenpakket samen te stellen. Korting bij zorgverzekeraars op aanvullende pakketten. Flexibele werkweek. Jaarlijks 232 verlofuren (bij 38 uur). Via het individueel keuzebudget kun je bovendien verlofuren verkopen of bijkopen. Volop mogelijkheden om opleidingen, trainingen en cursussen te volgen. Gedeeltelijk doorbetaald ouderschapsverlof. Aandacht voor gezond en energiek werken met het vitaliteitsprogramma. Additionele informatie Voor meer informatie over deze vacature, neem contact op met Tim Vermeulen, coördinator operations onderwijsgebouwen, e-mail: T.A.Vermeulen@tudelft.nl , tel: 0639250922 Sollicitatieprocedure Heb je interesse in deze vacature? Solliciteer dan uiterlijk 9 november 2026 via de sollicitatiebutton en upload de volgende documenten: CV Motivatiebrief Je kunt je sollicitatie richten aan Tim Vermeulen. Let op: Solliciteren gaat eenvoudig online. Sollicitaties die per email en/of post worden verstuurd nemen we niet in behandeling. Een pre-employment screening kan onderdeel zijn van de selectieprocedure. Een kennisveiligheidscheck maakt onderdeel uit van de sollicitatieprocedure. Deze check zal worden uitgevoerd op de laatst overgebleven kandidaten. Voor meer informatie over deze check verwijzen wij u naar hoofdstuk 8 van de ‘ National Knowledge Security Guidelines ’. Deze check voeren wij uit op basis van de grondslag gerechtvaardigd belang. Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Faculteit/Dienst: University Corporate Office – Campus Real Estate & Facility Management Salaris range: €3173 - €3785 Uren per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1,0 Solliciteren kan tot en met: 9 Nov 2026 ID vacature: 4014 Solliciteer nu » Zoek soortgelijke banen: Vacatures, All jobs Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad. Opent in een nieuw tabblad."
    },
    "https://careers.tudelft.nl/job/Delft-Postdoc-Fellowships-European-Synthetic-Cell-Initiative-%28SynCell-nExUs-programme%29-2628-CD/1376285757/": {
      "title": "Postdoc Fellowships European Synthetic Cell Initiative (SynCell-nExUs programme)",
      "description": "Postdoc Fellowships European Synthetic Cell Initiative (SynCell-nExUs programme) Job Details | TU Delft Skip to main content Language English Nederlands View Profile Language English Nederlands View Profile Back to all jobs Working at TU Delft Language English Nederlands View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Faculty/Department All Vacancy Type All Level of education All Fulltime/parttime All Field of work All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Postdoc Fellowships European Synthetic Cell Initiative (SynCell-nExUs programme) Join SynCell-nExUs and collaborate with leading researchers across Europe to tackle the big challenges in Synthetic Cells research. Job description SynCell-nExUs, (“SynCellEU programme for recruiting next generation European leaders in Synthetic Cell research”) is a new pan-European postdoctoral excellence programme led by the Max Planck Society for the Advancement of Science e.V. and managed in collaboration with the European Synthetic Cell Initiative (SynCellEU). The programme will run for five years, during which a total of 40 postdoctoral fellowships will be offered. The appointed fellows will join an interdisciplinary community of researchers dedicated to building synthetic cells from the bottom up. By recreating essential cellular functions, this community aims to better understand how living cells work and to translate this knowledge into cutting-edge, nature-inspired technologies. In this 1st call, SynCell-nExUs offers 20 fully funded, 3-year postdoctoral fellowships. Applicants are invited to develop their own research project in one of the following SynCell-nExUs research lines on synthetic cells: Metabolism and energy; Division and replication; Information processing and evolution; Enabling technologies. Selected fellows will be appointed at one of the proposed hosting labs, where they will work at the own research project, while being embedded in the lab and receiving supervision by the hosting PI. At the same time, they will participate in the activities of the network. They also will have the opportunity for exchange through a personalized programme of visits and secondments. Detailed information can be found in the Application Package that can be downloaded on the SynCell-nExUs website (see link under \"Application Procedure\"). Job requirements A PhD degree, in a field relevant to the SynCell-nExUs programme, at the time of the call deadline. Researchers who have successfully defended their doctoral thesis, but who have not yet formally been awarded the doctoral degree will also be considered as postdoctoral researchers and will be considered eligible to apply. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. Ability to work independently as well as in multidisciplinary research teams. Excellent knowledge of the English language. Good organisational and time-management skills. Please consult the Application Package for further details and templates. Further, candidates must comply with the COFUND-specific eligibility rules: Mobility rule: applicants must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in the country of the recruiting organisation or implementing partner for more than 12 months in the 36 months immediately before the deadline of the co-funded programme's call. Applicants must not already be permanently employed by the organisation hosting them. About the Programme This five-year programme offers 40 fully funded three-year postdoctoral positions across a network of 50+ labs in 22 leading research institutions across Europe . Co-funded by the European Union through Horizon Europe and MSCA COFUND , it is designed to develop the next generation of leaders in bottom-up synthetic biology and related fields. Fellows benefit from an outstanding training programme that combines cutting-edge research with professional development, including scientific communication, research diversity, transferable skills, and a dedicated personal development retreat. International and intersectoral collaboration is a core feature of the programme, supported by associated partners from the SynBioEU network and industry. Learn more: https://www.syntheticcell.eu/syncellnexus . The SynCell-nExUs programme is coordinated by the Max Planck Society and brings together a network of participating institutions across Europe. Postdoctoral researchers recruited through the programme will be hosted by one of the participating institutions, where they will carry out their research under the supervision of researchers and group leaders at the respective host institution. TU Delft is one of the participating institutions in the SynCell-nExUs programme and co-coordinates the recruitment process. Depending on the selected research project and supervisor, successful candidates may therefore be appointed at TU Delft or at another participating institution elsewhere in Europe. Candidates apply to the SynCell-nExUs programme and its research opportunities rather than exclusively to a specific host institution. The final host institution and supervisor will be determined based on the selected research project and the outcome of the recruitment process. Conditions of employment (depending on national regulations of host country) Duration of contract is 3 years. Temporary. A job of 32-40 hours per week. Appointment is at one of the participating hosting labs, with full social security coverage in the hosting country. A competitive salary in line with MSCA COFUND requirements. The remuneration will include the applicable social security contributions, taxes, and other mandatory deductions in accordance with the national legislation of the host institution. Where applicable, additional allowances may be provided, including a long-term leave allowance and a special needs allowance. For further details on the employment conditions and remuneration, please consult the SynCell-nExUS programme webpage: https://syntheticcell.eu/syncellnexus/ Additional information If you would like more information about this vacancy or the selection procedure, please contact Finn Mccartney, via syncellnexus@tudelft.nl . This is an EU co-funded project, named SynCell-nExUs , with project number 101261790, within program HORIZON EUROPE/ Marie Sklodowska Curie Actions COFUND. Application procedure Applicants should consult the applicants guide and downloadable forms on the SynCell-nExUs website here: How to apply . For this call (call one of two) 20 36-months postdoc positions are available. Applications must be submitted by 31 December 2026 through the application portals that are linked on the SynCell-nExUs webpage . Applications sent by email or post will not be processed. Applications should comply with the instructions set out in the ‘guide for applicants’ document. Each applicant can submit only one application, in one of the four available research areas.  In the application form, you will indicate your chosen area and sub-field and indicate up to three potential supervisors (hosting labs listed on the website). Please note: You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. As part of knowledge security, TU Delft conducts a risk assessment during the recruitment of personnel who will be appointed at TU Delft and employed under a TU Delft contract. We do this, among other things, to prevent the unwanted transfer of sensitive knowledge and technology. The assessment is based on information provided by the candidates themselves, such as their motivation letter and CV, and takes place at the final stages of the selection process. When the outcome of the assessment is negative, the candidate will be informed. The processing of personal data in the context of the risk assessment is carried out on the legal basis of the GDPR: performing a public task in the public interest. You can find more information about TU Delft’s assessment on our webpage on knowledge security . Candidates who are appointed at another participating institution within the SynCell-nExUs programme will be subject to the applicable procedures of that institution. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Faculty/Department: Faculty of Applied Sciences Salary range: Zie vacaturetekst Hours per week: 32-40 FTE: 0,8-1 Submission is possible until: 31 Dec 2026 ID job: 3762 Apply now » Find similar jobs: Vacatures, All jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab."
    }
  },
